[; cx-stdlib/diagram — the §10.1.2 reference diagram renderer, in CX.

   RULED 2026-08-20 (#758, DR-1…DR-11 all (a); owner "7b" — see
   ledger/rulings_2026_08_20_diagram_renderer.md). Wave 1 (DR-9a): the
   MERMAID target and the reverse-parse source extractors for ALL THREE
   formats live here as pure CX; the V mermaid path is deleted. DOT/SVG/
   PNG rendering and the `subprocess(dot)` seam are wave 2; the
   playground emitter is wave 3.

   INPUT IMAGE (DR-7a + mini-ruling DRW1-1): the engine injects the
   program's program-XML structural image (spec/ast.md §4 projection)
   materialized as a CXDM data tree, plus the verbatim source bytes and
   the detail rung, through the [?eval]-context pattern. No public
   parse surface exists here; a fork of this module still runs under
   engine invocation.

   BIT-FOR-BIT (DR-8a): every text this module produces is pinned
   byte-for-byte against the captured V-renderer golden corpus
   (vcx/tests/testdata/diagram_mermaid_golden/ — 20 program-viz
   fixtures + the synthetic pin set, ×3 detail rungs). Node-id minting
   order, node shapes, label grammar, truncation caps, and the escape
   set are all normative in spec/03-approved/std-lib/diagram.md.

   RULED 2026-08-20 (#890, DSC-1 — owner "1a";
   ledger/rulings_2026_08_20_diagram_svg_capability.md) SUPERSEDES two
   wave-2 preserve-as-is dispositions that the bit-for-bit bar had
   frozen: (a) the SVG metadata carrier now lands INSIDE the root
   element instead of in the XML prolog, so the emitted SVG is a
   well-formed document — the splice.svg golden moved deliberately;
   (c) `render-svg` / `render-png` REQUIRE the `subprocess` capability
   and refuse loudly (CXER0271) without it, instead of degrading to
   the dot-less envelope — which remains the answer for graphviz being
   unavailable, a different condition. PNG's tEXt splice was checked
   for the analogous defect and is CLEAN (DSC-1b), unchanged.

   DISPATCH DISCIPLINE (DR-6a): per-node dispatch is a flat [?if]
   chain (~2µs/arm) — a wide per-node [?match] is REFUSED at review
   (~20-45µs/arm measured). The render-rules table below is sealed
   DATA (DR-4a): the completeness gate diffs it against the spec table,
   the golden corpus, and the grammar registry.

   NOTE: this file IS the bundled source (vcx/code/stdlib_bundle.v
   embeds it); there is no second copy.

   NO SIBLING [?lib] IMPORTS. Every other frozen `cx-stdlib` module
   forwards straight to its native primitives (`[$str-…]`,
   `[$bytes-…]`) rather than importing a sibling module, and the
   loader's per-module isolation gate (vcx/tests/stdlib_umbrella_test)
   loads each bundled module against an EMPTY table — a sibling import
   fails there with CXER0213. The string/bytes work below therefore
   calls the same primitives cx-stdlib/strings and cx-stdlib/bytes
   wrap, which is also one dispatch hop cheaper in the per-node path
   (DR-6a). ]

[; ══ §1 the sealed render-rules table (DR-4a) ═══════════════════════════
   One artifact: spec table rows (incl. the DRW1-3 pipe row), the
   registry aliases (DRW1-5), the scaffolding set (DRW1-6), and the
   nested-only emitters (DRW1-4). The top-level admission set IS
   rows ∪ aliases ∪ scaffolding — finding 6's drift dies structurally. ]
[?def rules scope=public pure [returns element] ()
  [render-rules
    [row directive=for             rule="Loop activation in caller's lane; [par] renders parallel branches"]
    [row directive=map             rule="Iteration container; [par] renders parallel branches"]
    [row directive=reduce          rule="Iteration container with fold sink; [par] renders parallel branches"]
    [row directive=if              rule="Alternative branches, predicate at branch point"]
    [row directive=match           rule="Alternative branches, predicate at branch point"]
    [row directive=retry           rule="Wrapped activation with retry-annotation badge"]
    [row directive=timeout         rule="Wrapped activation with policy-annotation badge"]
    [row directive=circuit-breaker rule="Wrapped activation with policy-annotation badge"]
    [row directive=fallback        rule="Wrapped activation with policy-annotation badge; recovery branch off the err edge"]
    [row directive=rate-limit      rule="Wrapped activation with policy-annotation badge"]
    [row directive=bulkhead        rule="Wrapped activation with policy-annotation badge"]
    [row directive=http-service    rule="Endpoint with [resource] children as message handlers"]
    [row directive=worker          rule="Independent swimlane"]
    [row directive=channel         rule="Channel lane between workers"]
    [row directive=send            rule="Arrows between swimlanes"]
    [row directive=receive         rule="Arrows between swimlanes"]
    [row directive=try-send        rule="Arrows between swimlanes"]
    [row directive=try-receive     rule="Arrows between swimlanes"]
    [row directive=select          rule="Multi-arrow choice point"]
    [row directive=async           rule="Detached activation in a new swimlane"]
    [row directive=await           rule="Synchronization barrier"]
    [row directive=await-all       rule="Synchronization barrier"]
    [row directive=await-any       rule="Synchronization barrier"]
    [row directive=await-race      rule="Synchronization barrier"]
    [row directive=cancel          rule="Cancellation arrow + barrier"]
    [row directive=pipe            rule="Pipeline stages: input → stage₁ → … → result (DRW1-3)"]
    [alias directive=for-array of=for]
    [alias directive=for-map   of=for]
    [scaffold directive=let]
    [scaffold directive=def]
    [scaffold directive=const]
    [scaffold directive=lib]
    [nested directive=http-client]
    [nested directive=fn]]]

[; admitted — the top-level admission check (§10.1.2 CXER0281 gate,
   top-level-only per shipped behavior; consult finding C4). ]
[?def admitted scope=public pure [returns bool] ($local::string)
  [$exists [$first [?for [in $r [$rules]/*]
    [where [and [not [= [$name $r] "nested"]] [= [$string $r@directive] $local]]]
    [yield 1]]]]]

[; ══ §2 small helpers ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ ]

[; esc — the mermaid label escape set (normative: diagram.md §escapes):
   backslash → \\ first, then quote → \", then newline → \n. ]
[?def esc pure [returns string] ($s::string)
  [$str-replace [$str-replace [$str-replace $s "\\" "\\\\"] "\"" "\\\""] "\n" "\\n"]]

[; jn — join two line chunks, dropping empties (a chunk is newline-joined
   lines with no trailing newline; "" = no lines). ]
[?def jn pure [returns string] ($a::string $b::string)
  [?if [= $a ""] [then $b]
    [else [?if [= $b ""] [then $a] [else [$concat $a "\n" $b]]]]]]

[?def jn3 pure [returns string] ($a::string $b::string $c::string)
  [$jn [$jn $a $b] $c]]

[?def jn4 pure [returns string] ($a::string $b::string $c::string $d::string)
  [$jn [$jn $a $b] [$jn $c $d]]]

[; label-cap — the detail-rung truncation caps (48/72/120). ]
[?def label-cap pure [returns int] ($detail::string)
  [?if [= $detail "full"] [then 120]
    [else [?if [= $detail "compact"] [then 72] [else 48]]]]]

[; is-cx / local-of — program-image namespace tests. ]
[?def is-cx pure [returns bool] ($el::any)
  [$str-starts-with [$name $el] "cx:"]]

[?def local-of pure [returns string] ($el::any)
  [?let [= $n [$name $el]]
    [?if [$str-starts-with $n "cx:"]
      [then [$str-slice $n 3 [$str-length $n]]]
      [else $n]]]]

[; value-tag — the ast.md §4 VALUE tags: a `cx:`-local that denotes a
   value form, not a directive. NOT per-node-hot: the flow and label
   dispatchers handle the frequent tags in their own flat arms before
   consulting this; it decides only the rare remainder. ]
[?def value-tag pure [returns bool] ($l::string)
  [$exists [$first [?for
    [in $x ("var", "str", "int", "op", "seq", "call", "pattern", "arr",
            "map", "block", "bool", "atom", "dur", "float", "expr",
            "decimal", "bigint", "period", "date", "datetime", "data",
            "wildcard", "slice", "slice-access", "element")]
    [where [= $x $l]]
    [yield 1]]]]]

[; kids — materialized child elements of an element. ]
[?def kids pure [returns any] ($el::any)
  [?for [in $k $el/*] [yield $k]]]

[; lab — the labeled slot L of a directive element: the child named
   `cx:L` wrapping exactly ONE element (the emit convention for labeled
   slots), or () when absent. Consult finding C8: the XML image cannot
   distinguish a labeled slot from a same-named positional directive;
   the single-child wrap + per-emitter SOUGHT-label rule reproduces
   every golden (divergence class recorded in the ledger). ]
[?def lab pure [returns any] ($el::any $l::string)
  [?let [= $tag [$concat "cx:" $l]]
    [$first [?for [in $k $el/*]
      [where [and [= [$name $k] $tag] [= [$count $k/*] 1]]]
      [yield [hit [?splice [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]]]]]]]

[; lab-val — unwrap a [hit …] wrapper to the slot value. A [hit V] is
   never empty even when V is an empty element, so [$exists] on the
   WRAPPER is the reliable found-test (a bare empty element reads as
   ABSENT under the CX absence model — found the hard way; consult
   finding C9 in the ledger). ]
[?def lab-val pure [returns any] ($h::any)
  [$first [?for [in $v $h/*] [yield $v]]]]

[; lab-present — presence of labeled slot L (any wrapped value). ]
[?def lab-present pure [returns bool] ($el::any $l::string)
  [?let [= $tag [$concat "cx:" $l]]
    [$exists [$first [?for [in $k $el/*] [where [= [$name $k] $tag]] [yield 1]]]]]]

[; str-lab — labeled slot L's value when it is a string literal, else "".
   NESTED [?if]s, not [and]: operands evaluate eagerly, so a name-read
   of an absent slot would propagate an err value (consult finding C9). ]
[?def str-lab pure [returns string] ($el::any $l::string)
  [?let [= $w [$lab $el $l]]
    [?if [$exists $w]
      [then [?if [= [$name [$lab-val $w]] "cx:str"]
        [then [$string [$lab-val $w]]]
        [else ""]]]
      [else ""]]]]

[; ══ §3 expression labels (expr_label / expr_label_raw twins) ═══════ ]

[; attr-chips — `@k=v` chips per detail rung: min → none; compact →
   first 2 + ` (+K)`; full → all. Attrs ride as <cx:attr name=…> kids. ]
[?def attr-chips pure [returns string] ($el::any $detail::string)
  [?if [= $detail "min"]
    [then ""]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $attrs [?for [in $k $el/*] [where [= [$name $k] "cx:attr"]] [yield $k]]]
        [= $total [$count $attrs]]
        [?if [= $total 0]
          [then ""]
          [else
            [?let
              [= $capn [?if [= $detail "full"] [then $total] [else 2]]]
              [= $shown [$chips-upto $attrs 1 $capn $detail ""]]
              [= $rest [- $total $capn]]
              [?if [> $rest 0]
                [then [$concat $shown " (+" [?str '{$rest}'] ")"]]
                [else $shown]]]]]]]]]

[?def chips-upto pure [returns string] ($attrs::any $i::int $capn::int $detail::string $acc::string)
  [?if [or [> $i $capn] [> $i [$count $attrs]]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $a [$nth $attrs $i]]
        [= $vl [?if [> [$count $a/*] 0]
          [then [$label-raw [$first [?for [in $x $a/*] [yield $x]]] $detail]]
          [else ""]]]
        [$chips-upto $attrs [+ $i 1] $capn $detail
          [$concat $acc " @" [$string $a@name] "=" $vl]]]]]]

[; op-symbol — <cx:op name=…> → its CX operator symbol. ]
[?def op-symbol pure [returns string] ($n::string)
  [?if [= $n "add"] [then "+"]
  [else [?if [= $n "sub"] [then "-"]
  [else [?if [= $n "mul"] [then "*"]
  [else [?if [= $n "div"] [then "/"]
  [else [?if [= $n "eq"] [then "="]
  [else [?if [= $n "ne"] [then "!="]
  [else [?if [= $n "lt"] [then "<"]
  [else [?if [= $n "le"] [then "<="]
  [else [?if [= $n "gt"] [then ">"]
  [else [?if [= $n "ge"] [then ">="]
  [else $n]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[; items-of — unwrap the <item> children of a cx:seq / cx:arr. ]
[?def items-of pure [returns any] ($el::any)
  [?for [in $k $el/*]
    [yield [?if [= [$name $k] "item"]
      [then [$first [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]]
      [else $k]]]]]

[?def items-labels pure [returns string] ($items::any $i::int $detail::string $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $items]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $l [$label-raw [$nth $items $i] $detail]]
        [$items-labels $items [+ $i 1] $detail
          [?if [= $acc ""] [then $l] [else [$concat $acc ", " $l]]]]]]]]

[; var-steps — binding path steps → the compact spelling suffix. ]
[?def var-steps pure [returns string] ($steps::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $steps]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $st [$nth $steps $i]]
        [= $kind [$string $st@kind]]
        [= $kt [?if [$exists $st@kind-test] [then [$string $st@kind-test]] [else ""]]]
        [= $nt [?if [= $kt ""] [then [$string $st@name]] [else [$kt-spelling $kt]]]]
        [= $part
          [?if [= $kind "child"] [then [$concat "/" $nt]]
          [else [?if [= $kind "attr"] [then [$concat "@" $nt]]
          [else [?if [= $kind "member"] [then [$concat "." $nt]]
          [else [?if [= $kind "wildcard_children"] [then "/*"]
          [else [?if [= $kind "descendant"] [then [$concat "//" $nt]]
          [else [?if [= $kind "descendant_wildcard"] [then "//*"]
          [else [?if [= $kind "parent"] [then "/.."]
          [else ""]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]
        [= $preds [$preds-marks [$count $st/*] ""]]
        [$var-steps $steps [+ $i 1] [$concat $acc $part $preds]]]]]]

[?def preds-marks pure [returns string] ($n::int $acc::string)
  [?if [< $n 1] [then $acc] [else [$preds-marks [- $n 1] [$concat $acc "[…]"]]]]]

[; kt-spelling — the [131b] kind-test spelling used by binding labels. ]
[?def kt-spelling pure [returns string] ($kt::string)
  [$concat $kt "()"]]

[; call-args — <cx:call> argument labels (cx:arg unwrapped; cx:step
   postfix children excluded — V's label ignores result steps). ]
[?def call-args pure [returns string] ($el::any $detail::string)
  [?let [= $args [?for [in $k $el/*]
      [where [not [= [$name $k] "cx:step"]]]
      [yield [?if [= [$name $k] "cx:arg"]
        [then [$first [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]]
        [else $k]]]]]
    [$items-labels $args 1 $detail ""]]]

[; label-raw — expr_label_raw: one-line label for any program-image
   node, per node kind. Flat chain (DR-6a). ]
[?def label-raw pure [returns string] ($el::any $detail::string)
  [?if [not [$is-cx $el]]
    [then [$element-label [$name $el] $el $detail]]
    [else
      [?let [= $l [$local-of $el]]
        [?if [= $l "var"]
          [then
            [?if [$exists $el@name]
              [then [$concat "$" [$string $el@name] [$var-steps [$kids $el] 1 ""]]]
              [else [$concat "$" [$string $el]]]]]
        [else [?if [= $l "str"] [then [$concat "'" [$string $el] "'"]]
        [else [?if [= $l "int"] [then [$string $el]]
        [else [?if [= $l "float"] [then [$string $el]]
        [else [?if [= $l "bool"] [then [$string $el]]
        [else [?if [= $l "atom"] [then [$concat ":" [$string $el]]]
        [else [?if [= $l "dur"] [then [$string $el]]
        [else [?if [= $l "op"] [then [$element-label [$op-symbol [$string $el@name]] $el $detail]]
        [else [?if [= $l "seq"] [then [$concat "(" [$items-labels [$items-of $el] 1 $detail ""] ")"]]
        [else [?if [= $l "arr"] [then [$concat "[" [$items-labels [$items-of $el] 1 $detail ""] "]"]]
        [else [?if [= $l "block"] [then "…"]
        [else [?if [= $l "call"]
          [then
            [?let [= $argl [$call-args $el $detail]]
              [?if [= $argl ""]
                [then [$concat [$string $el@fn] "()"]]
                [else [$concat [$string $el@fn] "(" $argl ")"]]]]]
        [else [?if [= $l "for-comp"] [then "[?for]"]
        [else [?if [= $l "pattern"]
          [then [$concat "[" [?if [$exists $el@value] [then [$string $el@value]] [else ""]] "]"]]
        [else [?if [= $l "expr"]
          [; the §4 escape hatch (PathExpr / dynamic names): labeled with
             its verbatim carried source (consult finding C5). ]
          [then [$string $el]]
        [else [?if [= $l "wildcard"]
          [then [?if [$exists $el@deep] [then "**"] [else "*"]]]
        [else [?if [= $l "slice"] [then "[slice]"]
        [else [?if [= $l "slice-access"]
          [then
            [?let [= $b [$first [?for [in $k $el/*] [where [= [$name $k] "cx:var"]] [yield $k]]]]
              [$concat [?if [$exists $b] [then [$label-raw $b $detail]] [else ""]] "[…]"]]]
        [else [?if [= $l "map"] [then [$cd-map-label $el]]
        [else [?if [$cd-in-list $l ("decimal", "bigint", "date", "datetime", "period")]
          [then [$string $el]]
        [else [?if [$value-tag $l]
          [then "<lit>"]
          [; a directive collapses to its source shape ]
          [else [$concat "[?" $l "]"]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[; element-label — bareword element (or op-symbol head): name + chips
   per detail + ` …` when it has a body. Body = non-attr children
   (positional items or labeled slots). ]
[?def element-label pure [returns string] ($nm::string $el::any $detail::string)
  [?let
    [= $chips [$attr-chips $el $detail]]
    [= $body [?for [in $k $el/*] [where [not [= [$name $k] "cx:attr"]]] [yield $k]]]
    [?if [> [$count $body] 0]
      [; a single MAP-literal body inlines its `{k: v, …}` summary — the
         graph used to collapse `[person {name: 'Alice', …}]` to
         `[person …]` (playground report 2026-08-22); everything else
         keeps the `…` hint. The `label` cap still truncates. ]
      [then [?if [?if [= [$count $body] 1]
              [then [?if [$is-cx [$first $body]]
                [then [= [$local-of [$first $body]] "map"]]
                [else false]]]
              [else false]]
        [then [$concat "[" $nm $chips " " [$cd-map-label [$first $body]] "]"]]
        [else [$concat "[" $nm $chips " …]"]]]]
      [else [$concat "[" $nm $chips "]"]]]]]

[; label — expr_label: label-raw truncated at the detail cap. ]
[?def label pure [returns string] ($el::any $detail::string)
  [?let
    [= $raw [$label-raw $el $detail]]
    [= $max [$label-cap $detail]]
    [?if [> [$str-length $raw] $max]
      [then [$concat [$str-slice $raw 0 $max] "…"]]
      [else $raw]]]]

[; ══ §4 node/edge line builders (functional MermaidState twin) ═══════
   R = {id, n, ch, out}: minted node id; id counter; channel registry
   (a [chans [c name=… id=…]…] accumulator); the emitted chunk. ]

[?def nid pure [returns string] ($n::int)
  [?str 'n{$n}']]

[?def node-line pure [returns string] ($id::string $open::string $label::string $close::string)
  [$concat "    " $id $open [$esc $label] $close]]

[?def mk-rect pure [returns string] ($id::string $label::string)
  [$node-line $id "[\"" $label "\"]"]]

[?def mk-round pure [returns string] ($id::string $label::string)
  [$node-line $id "([\"" $label "\"])"]]

[?def mk-diamond pure [returns string] ($id::string $label::string)
  [$node-line $id "{\"" $label "\"}"]]

[?def mk-hex pure [returns string] ($id::string $label::string)
  [$node-line $id "{{\"" $label "\"}}"]]

[?def mk-subr pure [returns string] ($id::string $label::string)
  [$node-line $id "[[\"" $label "\"]]"]]

[; mk-chan-line — the lean channel shape; label pre-escaped by callers
   exactly where the V builder escaped (mmd_channel / channel_node_for). ]
[?def mk-chan-line pure [returns string] ($id::string $label-escaped::string)
  [$concat "    " $id "[/\"" $label-escaped "\"/]"]]

[?def edge-line pure [returns string] ($from::string $to::string)
  [$concat "    " $from " --> " $to]]

[?def ledge-line pure [returns string] ($from::string $to::string $label::string)
  [$concat "    " $from " -- \"" [$esc $label] "\" --> " $to]]

[; chan-find / chan-add — the channel-name → node-id registry. ]
[?def chan-find pure [returns any] ($ch::element $nm::string)
  [$first [?for [in $c $ch/*] [where [= [$string $c@name] $nm]] [yield [$string $c@id]]]]]

[?def chan-add pure [returns element] ($ch::element $nm::string $id::string)
  [chans [?splice [?for [in $x $ch/*] [yield $x]]] [c name=$nm id=$id]]]

[?def r-of pure [returns map] ($id::string $n::int $ch::element $out::string)
  {id: $id, n: $n, ch: $ch, out: $out}]

[; ══ §5 the flowchart emitters ═══════════════════════════════════════ ]

[; flow — render one program-image node; returns R. Dispatch is a flat
   [?if] chain on the cx: local (DR-6a — NEVER a wide [?match] here). ]
[?def cd-flow-map-literal pure [returns bool] ($e::any)
  [?let [= $ks [?for [in $k $e/*] [yield $k]]]
    [?if [= [$count $ks] 0]
      [then true]
      [else [not [$exists [$first [?for [in $k $ks] [where [not [= [$name $k] "entry"]]] [yield 1]]]]]]]]]

[?def flow pure [returns map] ($e::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string)
  [?if [not [$is-cx $e]]
    [then [$leaf $e $n $ch $detail]]
    [else
      [?let [= $l [$local-of $e]]
        [?if [= $l "for-comp"] [then [$forcomp-flow $e $n $ch $detail]]
        [else [?if [= $l "if"] [then [$if-flow $e $n $ch $detail]]
        [else [?if [= $l "let"] [then [$let-flow $e $n $ch $detail]]
        [else [?if [= $l "pipe"] [then [$pipe-flow $e $n $ch $detail]]
        [else [?if [= $l "match"] [then [$match-flow $e $n $ch $detail]]
        [else [?if [= $l "fn"] [then [$fn-flow $e $n $ch $detail]]
        [else [?if [= $l "map"]
          [; the map LITERAL and the [?map] directive share the local —
             a literal's children are all `entry` wraps, a stage's never
             are. The literal is a VALUE node, not a pipeline (playground
             report 2026-08-22: `{name: 'Alice'}` drew start→map→collect). ]
          [then [?if [$cd-flow-map-literal $e]
            [then [$leaf $e $n $ch $detail]]
            [else [$iter-flow $e $n $ch $detail "map" false]]]]
        [else [?if [= $l "reduce"] [then [$iter-flow $e $n $ch $detail "reduce" true]]
        [else [?if [= $l "for"] [then [$for-directive-flow $e $n $ch $detail]]
        [else [?if [or [= $l "retry"] [or [= $l "timeout"] [or [= $l "circuit-breaker"] [or [= $l "rate-limit"] [= $l "bulkhead"]]]]]
          [then [$resilience-flow $e $n $ch $detail]]
        [else [?if [= $l "fallback"] [then [$fallback-flow $e $n $ch $detail]]
        [else [?if [= $l "channel"] [then [$channel-flow $e $n $ch $detail]]
        [else [?if [or [= $l "send"] [= $l "try-send"]] [then [$send-flow $e $n $ch $detail]]
        [else [?if [or [= $l "receive"] [= $l "try-receive"]] [then [$receive-flow $e $n $ch $detail]]
        [else [?if [= $l "select"] [then [$select-flow $e $n $ch $detail]]
        [else [?if [= $l "async"] [then [$async-flow $e $n $ch $detail]]
        [else [?if [or [= $l "await"] [or [= $l "await-all"] [or [= $l "await-any"] [= $l "await-race"]]]]
          [then [$await-flow $e $n $ch $detail]]
        [else [?if [= $l "cancel"] [then [$cancel-flow $e $n $ch $detail]]
        [else [?if [= $l "http-service"] [then [$service-flow $e $n $ch $detail]]
        [else [?if [= $l "worker"] [then [$worker-flow $e $n $ch $detail]]
        [else [?if [= $l "http-client"] [then [$http-client-flow $e $n $ch $detail]]
        [else [?if [= $l "block"] [then [$block-flow $e $n $ch $detail]]
        [else [?if [$value-tag $l]
          [then [$leaf $e $n $ch $detail]]
          [else [$generic-flow $l $n $ch]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[; ── block (RULED: D913-1 #913) — a multi-form program: each form
   flows in order, chained by edges, returning the LAST form's R (the
   same convention pipe-flow ships, envelope wiring included). Before
   this the value-tag arm collapsed the WHOLE document to one `…` leaf
   — the flowchart twin of the DOT walk's empty canvas. The image
   wraps each form in a single-child `item` element (dgi_items_wrapper);
   the chain unwraps those. ]
[?def block-forms pure [returns any] ($d::any)
  [?for [in $k $d/*]
    [yield [?if [and [= [$name $k] "item"] [= [$count $k/*] 1]]
      [then [$first [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]]
      [else $k]]]]]

[?def block-flow pure [returns map] ($d::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string)
  [?let [= $forms [$block-forms $d]]
    [?if [= [$count $forms] 0]
      [then [$leaf $d $n $ch $detail]]
      [else
        [?let [= $r0 [$flow [$nth $forms 1] $n $ch $detail]]
          [$block-chain $forms 2 $r0 $detail]]]]]]

[?def block-chain pure [returns map] ($forms::any $i::int $r::map $detail::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $forms]]
    [then $r]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $rs [$flow [$nth $forms $i] $r.n $r.ch $detail]]
        [= $out [$jn3 $r.out $rs.out [$edge-line $r.id $rs.id]]]
        [$block-chain $forms [+ $i 1] [$r-of $rs.id $rs.n $rs.ch $out] $detail]]]]]

[?def leaf pure [returns map] ($e::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string)
  [?let [= $id [$nid $n]]
    [$r-of $id [+ $n 1] $ch [$mk-rect $id [$label $e $detail]]]]]

[?def generic-flow pure [returns map] ($l::string $n::int $ch::element)
  [?let [= $id [$nid $n]]
    [$r-of $id [+ $n 1] $ch [$mk-rect $id [$concat "[?" $l "]"]]]]]

[; pos-kids — positional children: every child that is not one of the
   emitter's SOUGHT labels (single-child cx:L wraps; see `lab`). ]
[?def sought pure [returns bool] ($k::any $labels::any)
  [?if [not [$is-cx $k]]
    [then false]
    [else
      [?let [= $l [$local-of $k]]
        [and [$exists [$first [?for [in $x $labels] [where [= $x $l]] [yield 1]]]]
             [= [$count $k/*] 1]]]]]]

[?def pos-kids pure [returns any] ($el::any $labels::any)
  [?for [in $k $el/*] [where [not [$sought $k $labels]]] [yield $k]]]

[; ── pipe ── ]
[?def pipe-flow pure [returns map] ($d::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string)
  [?let
    [= $posk [$pos-kids $d ("through")]]
    [= $stages [?for [in $k $d/*] [where [$sought $k ("through")]] [yield [$first [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]]]]
    [= $r0 [?if [> [$count $posk] 0]
      [then [$flow [$first $posk] $n $ch $detail]]
      [else [?let [= $id [$nid $n]] [$r-of $id [+ $n 1] $ch [$mk-rect $id "input"]]]]]]
    [$pipe-stages $stages 1 $r0 $detail]]]

[?def pipe-stages pure [returns map] ($stages::any $i::int $r::map $detail::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $stages]]
    [then $r]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $st [$nth $stages $i]]
        [= $rs [$pipe-stage $st $r.n $r.ch $detail]]
        [= $out [$jn3 $r.out $rs.out [$edge-line $r.id $rs.id]]]
        [$pipe-stages $stages [+ $i 1] [$r-of $rs.id $rs.n $rs.ch $out] $detail]]]]]

[?def pipe-stage pure [returns map] ($st::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string)
  [?if [and [$is-cx $st] [= [$local-of $st] "fn"]]
    [then [?let [= $id [$nid $n]]
      [$r-of $id [+ $n 1] $ch [$mk-subr $id [$fn-capsule $st $detail]]]]]
    [else [$flow $st $n $ch $detail]]]]

[; ── if ── ]
[?def if-flow pure [returns map] ($d::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string)
  [?let
    [= $posk [$pos-kids $d ("then", "else")]]
    [= $then [$lab $d "then"]]
    [= $else [$lab $d "else"]]
    [= $cond-label [?if [> [$count $posk] 0] [then [$label [$first $posk] $detail]] [else "?"]]]
    [= $dia [$nid $n]]
    [= $join [$nid [+ $n 1]]]
    [= $head [$jn [$mk-diamond $dia [$concat "if " $cond-label]] [$mk-rect $join "[?if] result"]]]
    [= $rt [?if [$exists $then]
      [then
        [?let [= $r [$flow [$lab-val $then] [+ $n 2] $ch $detail]]
          [$r-of $join $r.n $r.ch
            [$jn3 $r.out [$ledge-line $dia $r.id "true"] [$edge-line $r.id $join]]]]]
      [else [$r-of $join [+ $n 2] $ch ""]]]]
    [= $re [?if [$exists $else]
      [then
        [?let [= $r [$flow [$lab-val $else] $rt.n $rt.ch $detail]]
          [$r-of $join $r.n $r.ch
            [$jn3 $r.out [$ledge-line $dia $r.id "false"] [$edge-line $r.id $join]]]]]
      [else [$r-of $join $rt.n $rt.ch [$ledge-line $dia $join "false"]]]]]
    [$r-of $join $re.n $re.ch [$jn3 $head $rt.out $re.out]]]]

[; ── match ── ]
[?def match-flow pure [returns map] ($d::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string)
  [?let
    [= $posk [$pos-kids $d ("case", "else", "yield")]]
    [= $subj-label [?if [> [$count $posk] 0] [then [$label [$first $posk] $detail]] [else "?"]]]
    [= $arms [$match-arms [$kids $d] 1 () false [match-arm-acc] $detail]]
    [= $dia [$nid $n]]
    [= $join [$nid [+ $n 1]]]
    [= $head [$jn [$mk-diamond $dia [$concat "match " $subj-label]] [$mk-rect $join "[?match] result"]]]
    [?if [= [$count $arms/*] 0]
      [then [$r-of $join [+ $n 2] $ch [$jn $head [$edge-line $dia $join]]]]
      [else
        [?let [= $ra [$match-arm-emit [$kids $arms] 1 [$r-of $join [+ $n 2] $ch $head] $dia $join $detail]]
          $ra]]]]]

[; match-arms — the V pending-pattern state machine over the directive's
   SOUGHT labeled slots (case / else / yield), in child order. Arms
   accumulate as [arm label=… [BODY]] children. ]
[?def match-arms pure [returns element] ($ks::any $i::int $pending::any $pending-else::bool $acc::element $detail::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $k [$nth $ks $i]]
        [?if [$sought $k ("case")]
          [then [$match-arms $ks [+ $i 1] [hit [?splice [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]] false $acc $detail]]
        [else [?if [$sought $k ("else")]
          [then [$match-arms $ks [+ $i 1] () true $acc $detail]]
        [else [?if [$sought $k ("yield")]
          [then
            [?let [= $body [$first [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]]
              [?if $pending-else
                [then [$match-arms $ks [+ $i 1] () false
                  [match-arm-acc [?splice [?for [in $x $acc/*] [yield $x]]] [arm label=":else" $body]] $detail]]
                [else [?if [$exists $pending]
                  [then [$match-arms $ks [+ $i 1] () false
                    [match-arm-acc [?splice [?for [in $x $acc/*] [yield $x]]] [arm label=[$label [$lab-val $pending] $detail] $body]] $detail]]
                  [else [$match-arms $ks [+ $i 1] $pending $pending-else $acc $detail]]]]]]]
          [else [$match-arms $ks [+ $i 1] $pending $pending-else $acc $detail]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def match-arm-emit pure [returns map] ($arms::any $i::int $r::map $dia::string $join::string $detail::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $arms]]
    [then $r]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $arm [$nth $arms $i]]
        [= $body [$first [?for [in $v $arm/*] [yield $v]]]]
        [= $rb [$flow $body $r.n $r.ch $detail]]
        [= $out [$jn4 $r.out $rb.out [$ledge-line $dia $rb.id [$string $arm@label]] [$edge-line $rb.id $join]]]
        [$match-arm-emit $arms [+ $i 1] [$r-of $join $rb.n $rb.ch $out] $dia $join $detail]]]]]

[; ── let ── ]
[?def let-flow pure [returns map] ($d::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string)
  [?let
    [= $bind-name [$str-lab $d "bind"]]
    [= $value [$lab $d "value"]]
    [= $body [$lab $d "body"]]
    [= $rv [?if [$exists $value]
      [then [$flow [$lab-val $value] $n $ch $detail]]
      [else [?let [= $id [$nid $n]] [$r-of $id [+ $n 1] $ch [$mk-rect $id "?"]]]]]]
    [= $ch2 [?if [= $bind-name ""]
      [then $rv.ch]
      [else [?if [$exists $value]
        [then [?if [$is-cx [$lab-val $value]]
          [then [?if [= [$local-of [$lab-val $value]] "channel"]
            [then [$chan-add $rv.ch $bind-name $rv.id]]
            [else $rv.ch]]]
          [else $rv.ch]]]
        [else $rv.ch]]]]]
    [= $bid [$nid $rv.n]]
    [= $head [$jn3 $rv.out [$mk-subr $bid [$concat "$" $bind-name]] [$edge-line $rv.id $bid]]]
    [?if [$exists $body]
      [then
        [?let [= $rb [$flow [$lab-val $body] [+ $rv.n 1] $ch2 $detail]]
          [$r-of $rb.id $rb.n $rb.ch [$jn3 $head $rb.out [$edge-line $bid $rb.id]]]]]
      [else [$r-of $bid [+ $rv.n 1] $ch2 $head]]]]]

[; ── fn ── ]
[?def fn-flow pure [returns map] ($d::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string)
  [?let [= $id [$nid $n]]
    [$r-of $id [+ $n 1] $ch [$mk-subr $id [$fn-capsule $d $detail]]]]]

[; fn-extract twin: labeled params/body override; else first positional
   = params, second = body. ]
[?def fn-capsule pure [returns string] ($d::any $detail::string)
  [?let
    [= $lp [$lab $d "params"]]
    [= $lb [$lab $d "body"]]
    [= $pos [$pos-kids $d ("params", "body")]]
    [= $params-node [?if [$exists $lp]
      [then [hit [$lab-val $lp]]]
      [else [?if [> [$count $pos] 0] [then [hit [$first $pos]]] [else ()]]]]]
    [= $body [?if [$exists $lb] [then [hit [$lab-val $lb]]]
      [else [?if [$exists $lp]
        [then [?if [> [$count $pos] 0] [then [hit [$first $pos]]] [else ()]]]
        [else [?if [> [$count $pos] 1] [then [hit [$nth $pos 2]]] [else ()]]]]]]]
    [?if [not [$exists $body]]
      [then "[?fn]"]
      [else
        [$concat "fn("
          [?if [$exists $params-node] [then [$param-names [$lab-val $params-node]]] [else ""]]
          ") → " [$label [$lab-val $body] $detail]]]]]]

[?def param-names pure [returns string] ($node::any)
  [?if [= [$name $node] "cx:var"]
    [then [?if [$exists $node@name] [then [$string $node@name]] [else [$string $node]]]]
    [else [?if [or [= [$name $node] "cx:seq"] [= [$name $node] "cx:arr"]]
      [then
        [?let [= $names [?for [in $it [$items-of $node]]
            [where [= [$name $it] "cx:var"]]
            [yield [?if [$exists $it@name] [then [$string $it@name]] [else [$string $it]]]]]]
          [$join-names $names 1 ""]]]
      [else ""]]]]]

[?def join-names pure [returns string] ($xs::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $xs]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$join-names $xs [+ $i 1]
      [?if [= $acc ""] [then [$nth $xs $i]] [else [$concat $acc "," [$nth $xs $i]]]]]]]]

[; ── map / reduce ── ]
[?def iter-flow pure [returns map] ($d::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string $nm::string $is-reduce::bool)
  [?let
    [= $posk [$pos-kids $d ("using", "init", "par", "ordered")]]
    [= $usingw [$lab $d "using"]]
    [= $initw [$lab $d "init"]]
    [= $is-par [$lab-present $d "par"]]
    [= $is-ordered [$lab-present $d "ordered"]]
    [= $rs [?if [> [$count $posk] 0]
      [then [$flow [$first $posk] $n $ch $detail]]
      [else [?let [= $id [$nid $n]] [$r-of $id [+ $n 1] $ch [$mk-rect $id "xs"]]]]]]
    [= $hlabel0 [?if $is-par [then [$concat $nm " :par"]] [else $nm]]]
    [= $hlabel [?if [and $is-reduce [$exists $initw]]
      [then [$concat $hlabel0 " :init " [$label [$lab-val $initw] $detail]]]
      [else $hlabel0]]]
    [= $hid [$nid $rs.n]]
    [= $head [$jn3 $rs.out [$mk-hex $hid $hlabel] [$edge-line $rs.id $hid]]]
    [= $sink-label [?if $is-reduce [then "fold"] [else "collect"]]]
    [?if [$exists $usingw]
      [then
        [?let
          [= $using [$lab-val $usingw]]
          [= $rb [?if [and [$is-cx $using] [= [$local-of $using] "fn"]]
            [then [?let [= $id [$nid [+ $rs.n 1]]]
              [$r-of $id [+ $rs.n 2] $rs.ch [$mk-subr $id [$fn-capsule $using $detail]]]]]
            [else [$flow $using [+ $rs.n 1] $rs.ch $detail]]]]
          [= $mid [$jn3 $head $rb.out [$ledge-line $hid $rb.id ":using"]]]
          [?if [and $is-par $is-ordered]
            [then
              [?let
                [= $oid [$nid $rb.n]]
                [= $sid [$nid [+ $rb.n 1]]]
                [$r-of $sid [+ $rb.n 2] $rb.ch
                  [$jn4 $mid
                    [$jn [$mk-rect $oid "preserve order"] [$edge-line $rb.id $oid]]
                    [$mk-round $sid $sink-label]
                    [$edge-line $oid $sid]]]]]
            [else
              [?let [= $sid [$nid $rb.n]]
                [$r-of $sid [+ $rb.n 1] $rb.ch
                  [$jn3 $mid [$mk-round $sid $sink-label] [$edge-line $rb.id $sid]]]]]]]]
      [else
        [?let [= $sid [$nid [+ $rs.n 1]]]
          [$r-of $sid [+ $rs.n 2] $rs.ch
            [$jn3 $head [$mk-round $sid $sink-label] [$edge-line $hid $sid]]]]]]]]

[; ── for (directive shape) ── ]
[?def for-directive-flow pure [returns map] ($d::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string)
  [?let
    [= $source [$lab $d "in"]]
    [= $yield [$lab $d "yield"]]
    [= $where [$lab $d "where"]]
    [= $bind-name [$str-lab $d "bind"]]
    [= $is-par [$lab-present $d "par"]]
    [= $rs [?if [$exists $source]
      [then [$flow [$lab-val $source] $n $ch $detail]]
      [else [?let [= $id [$nid $n]] [$r-of $id [+ $n 1] $ch [$mk-rect $id "source"]]]]]]
    [= $hlabel0 [?if [= $bind-name ""] [then "for"] [else [$concat "for $" $bind-name]]]]
    [= $hlabel [?if $is-par [then [$concat $hlabel0 " :par"]] [else $hlabel0]]]
    [= $hid [$nid $rs.n]]
    [= $head [$jn3 $rs.out [$mk-hex $hid $hlabel] [$edge-line $rs.id $hid]]]
    [= $rw [?if [$exists $where]
      [then
        [?let [= $wid [$nid [+ $rs.n 1]]]
          [$r-of $wid [+ $rs.n 2] $rs.ch
            [$jn $head [$jn [$mk-diamond $wid [$concat ":where " [$label [$lab-val $where] $detail]]] [$ledge-line $hid $wid "iter"]]]]]]
      [else [$r-of $hid [+ $rs.n 1] $rs.ch $head]]]]
    [?if [$exists $yield]
      [then
        [?let
          [= $rb [$flow [$lab-val $yield] $rw.n $rw.ch $detail]]
          [= $sid [$nid $rb.n]]
          [$r-of $sid [+ $rb.n 1] $rb.ch
            [$jn4 $rw.out
              [$jn $rb.out [$ledge-line $rw.id $rb.id [?if [$exists $where] [then "true"] [else "iter"]]]]
              [$mk-round $sid "collect"]
              [$edge-line $rb.id $sid]]]]]
      [else
        [?let [= $sid [$nid $rw.n]]
          [$r-of $sid [+ $rw.n 1] $rw.ch
            [$jn3 $rw.out [$mk-round $sid "collect"] [$edge-line $rw.id $sid]]]]]]]]

[; ── for-comprehension (cx:for-comp) ── ]
[?def forcomp-flow pure [returns map] ($f::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string)
  [?let
    [= $clauses [?for [in $k $f/*] [where [= [$name $k] "cx:clause"]] [yield $k]]]
    [= $genw [$last [?for [in $c $clauses] [where [= [$string $c@kind] "generator"]] [yield [hit $c]]]]]
    [= $gen [$lab-val $genw]]
    [= $bind-name [?if [and [$exists $genw] [$exists $gen@bind]] [then [$string $gen@bind]] [else ""]]]
    [= $source [?if [$exists $genw]
      [then [$last [?for [in $s $gen/*] [where [= [$name $s] "cx:source"]] [yield [hit [?splice [?for [in $v $s/*] [yield $v]]]]]]]]
      [else ()]]]
    [= $fclause [$last [?for [in $c $clauses] [where [= [$string $c@kind] "filter"]] [yield [hit $c]]]]]
    [= $filter [?if [$exists $fclause]
      [then [$last [?for [in $w [$lab-val $fclause]/*] [where [= [$name $w] "cx:expr-clause"]]
        [yield [hit [?splice [?for [in $v $w/*] [yield $v]]]]]]]]
      [else ()]]]
    [= $is-par [$exists [$first [?for [in $c $clauses] [where [= [$string $c@kind] "par"]] [yield 1]]]]]
    [= $is-ordered [$exists [$first [?for [in $c $clauses] [where [= [$string $c@kind] "ordered"]] [yield 1]]]]]
    [= $yieldw [$last [?for [in $k $f/*] [where [= [$name $k] "cx:yield"]]
      [yield [hit [?splice [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]]]]]]
    [= $rs [?if [$exists $source]
      [then [$flow [$lab-val $source] $n $ch $detail]]
      [else [?let [= $id [$nid $n]] [$r-of $id [+ $n 1] $ch [$mk-rect $id "source"]]]]]]
    [= $hlabel0 [?if [= $bind-name ""] [then "for"] [else [$concat "for $" $bind-name]]]]
    [= $hlabel1 [?if $is-par [then [$concat $hlabel0 " :par"]] [else $hlabel0]]]
    [= $hlabel [?if $is-ordered [then [$concat $hlabel1 " :ordered"]] [else $hlabel1]]]
    [= $hid [$nid $rs.n]]
    [= $head [$jn3 $rs.out [$mk-hex $hid $hlabel]
      [$ledge-line $rs.id $hid [?if [= $bind-name ""] [then "iter"] [else [$concat "binds $" $bind-name]]]]]]
    [= $rw [?if [$exists $filter]
      [then
        [?let [= $wid [$nid [+ $rs.n 1]]]
          [$r-of $wid [+ $rs.n 2] $rs.ch
            [$jn $head [$jn [$mk-diamond $wid [$concat ":where " [$label [$lab-val $filter] $detail]]] [$edge-line $hid $wid]]]]]]
      [else [$r-of $hid [+ $rs.n 1] $rs.ch $head]]]]
    [= $rb [$flow [$lab-val $yieldw] $rw.n $rw.ch $detail]]
    [= $sid [$nid $rb.n]]
    [$r-of $sid [+ $rb.n 1] $rb.ch
      [$jn4 $rw.out
        [$jn $rb.out [$ledge-line $rw.id $rb.id [?if [$exists $filter] [then "true"] [else "iter"]]]]
        [$mk-round $sid "collect"]
        [$edge-line $rb.id $sid]]]]]

[; ── resilience wrappers ── ]
[?def resilience-flow pure [returns map] ($d::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string)
  [?let
    [= $l [$local-of $d]]
    [= $body [$lab $d "body"]]
    [= $dur [?if [= $l "timeout"]
      [then [$first [?for [in $k $d/*]
        [where [and [not [$resilience-param $k]] [not [$sought $k ("body")]]]]
        [yield [hit $k]]]]]
      [else ()]]]
    [= $params [?for [in $k $d/*] [where [$resilience-param $k]]
      [yield [$concat ":" [$local-of $k] " " [$label [$first [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]] $detail]]]]]
    [= $plabel [$policy-label [$concat "[?" $l "]"] $dur $params $detail]]
    [= $pid [$nid $n]]
    [= $head [$mk-subr $pid $plabel]]
    [?if [$exists $body]
      [then
        [?let [= $rb [$flow [$lab-val $body] [+ $n 1] $ch $detail]]
          [$r-of $rb.id $rb.n $rb.ch [$jn3 $head $rb.out [$ledge-line $pid $rb.id ":body"]]]]]
      [else [$r-of $pid [+ $n 1] $ch $head]]]]]

[; resilience-param — a labeled policy-parameter slot: single-child
   cx:L where L is neither `body`, a value tag (with the shipped `name`
   exception), a ruled/nested/scaffolding directive, nor a positional
   directive child (consult finding C8's classification rule). ]
[?def resilience-param pure [returns bool] ($k::any)
  [?if [not [$is-cx $k]]
    [then false]
    [else
      [?let [= $l [$local-of $k]]
        [?if [not [= [$count $k/*] 1]]
          [then false]
          [else [?if [= $l "body"]
            [then false]
            [else [?if [= $l "name"]
              [then true]
              [else [?if [$value-tag $l]
                [then false]
                [else [not [$admitted-or-nested $l]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def admitted-or-nested pure [returns bool] ($l::string)
  [$exists [$first [?for [in $r [$rules]/*]
    [where [= [$string $r@directive] $l]]
    [yield 1]]]]]

[?def policy-label pure [returns string] ($head::string $dur::any $params::any $detail::string)
  [?let
    [= $with-dur [?if [$exists $dur] [then [$concat $head " " [$label [$lab-val $dur] $detail]]] [else $head]]]
    [= $np [$count $params]]
    [= $shown [$params-upto $params 1 [?if [> $np 2] [then 2] [else $np]] $with-dur]]
    [?if [> $np 2] [then [$concat $shown " …"]] [else $shown]]]]

[?def params-upto pure [returns string] ($params::any $i::int $capn::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i $capn]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$params-upto $params [+ $i 1] $capn [$concat $acc " " [$nth $params $i]]]]]]

[; ── fallback ── ]
[?def fallback-flow pure [returns map] ($d::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string)
  [?let
    [= $body [$lab $d "body"]]
    [= $recover [$lab $d "recover-with"]]
    [= $gid [$nid $n]]
    [= $join [$nid [+ $n 1]]]
    [= $head [$jn [$mk-subr $gid "[?fallback]"] [$mk-rect $join "[?fallback] result"]]]
    [?if [$exists $body]
      [then
        [?let
          [= $rb [$flow [$lab-val $body] [+ $n 2] $ch $detail]]
          [= $mid [$jn4 $head $rb.out [$edge-line $gid $rb.id] [$edge-line $rb.id $join]]]
          [?if [$exists $recover]
            [then
              [?let [= $rr [$flow [$lab-val $recover] $rb.n $rb.ch $detail]]
                [$r-of $join $rr.n $rr.ch
                  [$jn4 $mid $rr.out [$ledge-line $rb.id $rr.id "err"] [$edge-line $rr.id $join]]]]]
            [else [$r-of $join $rb.n $rb.ch $mid]]]]]
      [else [$r-of $join [+ $n 2] $ch $head]]]]]

[; ── channel / send / receive ── ]
[?def channel-flow pure [returns map] ($d::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string)
  [?let
    [= $nm [$str-lab $d "name"]]
    [= $buffer [$lab $d "buffer"]]
    [= $label0 [?if [= $nm ""] [then "channel"] [else [$concat "channel \"" $nm "\""]]]]
    [= $label1 [?if [$exists $buffer]
      [then [$concat $label0 " (buffer " [$label [$lab-val $buffer] $detail] ")"]]
      [else $label0]]]
    [= $id [$nid $n]]
    [= $ch2 [?if [= $nm ""] [then $ch] [else [$chan-add $ch $nm $id]]]]
    [$r-of $id [+ $n 1] $ch2 [$mk-chan-line $id [$esc $label1]]]]]

[; chan-node-for — reuse a registered channel node for `$name` targets;
   mint a shared placeholder otherwise. Returns R (out possibly ""). ]
[?def chan-node-for pure [returns map] ($t::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string)
  [?if [?if [$is-cx $t]
         [then [?if [= [$local-of $t] "var"] [then [not [$exists $t@name]]] [else false]]]
         [else false]]
    [then
      [?let
        [= $nm [$string $t]]
        [= $hit [$chan-find $ch $nm]]
        [?if [$exists $hit]
          [then [$r-of $hit $n $ch ""]]
          [else
            [?let [= $id [$nid $n]]
              [$r-of $id [+ $n 1] [$chan-add $ch $nm $id]
                [$mk-chan-line $id [$concat "channel $" $nm]]]]]]]]
    [else
      [?let [= $id [$nid $n]]
        [$r-of $id [+ $n 1] $ch
          [$mk-chan-line $id [$concat "channel " [$esc [$label $t $detail]]]]]]]]]

[?def send-flow pure [returns map] ($d::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string)
  [?let
    [= $posk [$pos-kids $d ("to")]]
    [= $target [$lab $d "to"]]
    [= $val-label [?if [> [$count $posk] 0] [then [$label [$first $posk] $detail]] [else "?"]]]
    [= $sid [$nid $n]]
    [= $head [$mk-rect $sid [$concat "send " $val-label]]]
    [?if [$exists $target]
      [then
        [?let [= $rc [$chan-node-for [$lab-val $target] [+ $n 1] $ch $detail]]
          [$r-of $rc.id $rc.n $rc.ch
            [$jn3 $head $rc.out [$ledge-line $sid $rc.id $val-label]]]]]
      [else [$r-of $sid [+ $n 1] $ch $head]]]]]

[?def receive-flow pure [returns map] ($d::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string)
  [?let
    [= $target [$lab $d "from"]]
    [= $sid [$nid $n]]
    [= $head [$mk-rect $sid [$concat "[?" [$local-of $d] "]"]]]
    [?if [$exists $target]
      [then
        [?let [= $rc [$chan-node-for [$lab-val $target] [+ $n 1] $ch $detail]]
          [$r-of $sid $rc.n $rc.ch
            [$jn3 $head $rc.out [$ledge-line $rc.id $sid "recv"]]]]]
      [else [$r-of $sid [+ $n 1] $ch $head]]]]]

[; ── select ── ]
[?def select-flow pure [returns map] ($d::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string)
  [?let
    [= $cases [?for [in $k $d/*] [where [$sought $k ("case")]] [yield [$first [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]]]]
    [= $dia [$nid $n]]
    [= $join [$nid [+ $n 1]]]
    [= $head [$jn [$mk-diamond $dia "[?select]"] [$mk-rect $join "[?select] result"]]]
    [?if [= [$count $cases] 0]
      [then [$r-of $join [+ $n 2] $ch [$jn $head [$edge-line $dia $join]]]]
      [else [$select-cases $cases 1 [$r-of $join [+ $n 2] $ch $head] $dia $join $detail]]]]]

[?def select-cases pure [returns map] ($cases::any $i::int $r::map $dia::string $join::string $detail::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $cases]]
    [then $r]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $cv [$nth $cases $i]]
        [; case-body SLOTS (the V emitter reads cx_element slots; the
           image spells them <cx:slot label=…>) — practically unreachable
           with today's parser, kept for fidelity. ]
        [= $ct [$first [?for [in $s $cv/*]
          [where [and [= [$name $s] "cx:slot"] [= [$string $s@label] "from"]]]
          [yield [hit [?splice [?for [in $v $s/*] [yield $v]]]]]]]]
        [= $handler [$first [?for [in $s $cv/*]
          [where [and [= [$name $s] "cx:slot"]
                      [or [= [$string $s@label] "do"] [or [= [$string $s@label] "yield"] [= [$string $s@label] "body"]]]]]
          [yield [hit [?splice [?for [in $v $s/*] [yield $v]]]]]]]]
        [= $case-label [$concat "case " [?str '{$i}']]]
        [= $rt [?if [$exists $ct]
          [then
            [?let [= $rc [$chan-node-for [$lab-val $ct] $r.n $r.ch $detail]]
              [$r-of $r.id $rc.n $rc.ch
                [$jn3 $r.out $rc.out [$ledge-line $rc.id $dia $case-label]]]]]
          [else $r]]]
        [= $rh [?if [$exists $handler]
          [then
            [?let [= $rb [$flow [$lab-val $handler] $rt.n $rt.ch $detail]]
              [$r-of $join $rb.n $rb.ch
                [$jn4 $rt.out $rb.out [$ledge-line $dia $rb.id $case-label] [$edge-line $rb.id $join]]]]]
          [else [$r-of $join $rt.n $rt.ch [$jn $rt.out [$ledge-line $dia $join $case-label]]]]]]
        [$select-cases $cases [+ $i 1] $rh $dia $join $detail]]]]]

[; ── async / await / cancel ── ]
[?def async-flow pure [returns map] ($d::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string)
  [?let
    [= $lb [$lab $d "body"]]
    [= $posk [$pos-kids $d ("body")]]
    [= $body [?if [$exists $lb]
      [then [hit [$lab-val $lb]]]
      [else [?if [> [$count $posk] 0] [then [hit [$first $posk]]] [else ()]]]]]
    [= $fid [$nid $n]]
    [= $head [$mk-subr $fid "[?async] future"]]
    [?if [$exists $body]
      [then
        [?let [= $rb [$flow [$lab-val $body] [+ $n 1] $ch $detail]]
          [$r-of $fid $rb.n $rb.ch [$jn3 $head $rb.out [$ledge-line $fid $rb.id "spawn"]]]]]
      [else [$r-of $fid [+ $n 1] $ch $head]]]]]

[?def await-flow pure [returns map] ($d::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string)
  [?let
    [= $join [$nid $n]]
    [= $head [$mk-diamond $join [$concat "[?" [$local-of $d] "]"]]]
    [$await-emit-pos [$pos-kids $d ()] 1 [$r-of $join [+ $n 1] $ch $head] $join $detail]]]

[; await-emit-pos — each positional child: a cx:seq / cx:arr fans out
   into one inbound arrow per item; anything else is one arrow. ]
[?def await-emit-pos pure [returns map] ($pos::any $i::int $r::map $join::string $detail::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $pos]]
    [then $r]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $p [$nth $pos $i]]
        [= $r2 [?if [and [$is-cx $p] [or [= [$local-of $p] "seq"] [= [$local-of $p] "arr"]]]
          [then [$await-emit [$items-of $p] 1 $r $join $detail]]
          [else [$await-emit ($p) 1 $r $join $detail]]]]
        [$await-emit-pos $pos [+ $i 1] $r2 $join $detail]]]]]

[?def await-emit pure [returns map] ($items::any $i::int $r::map $join::string $detail::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $items]]
    [then $r]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $rb [$flow [$nth $items $i] $r.n $r.ch $detail]]
        [$await-emit $items [+ $i 1]
          [$r-of $join $rb.n $rb.ch [$jn3 $r.out $rb.out [$edge-line $rb.id $join]]]
          $join $detail]]]]]

[?def cancel-flow pure [returns map] ($d::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string)
  [?let
    [= $cid [$nid $n]]
    [= $head [$mk-subr $cid "[?cancel]"]]
    [$cancel-emit [$pos-kids $d ()] 1 [$r-of $cid [+ $n 1] $ch $head] $cid $detail]]]

[?def cancel-emit pure [returns map] ($items::any $i::int $r::map $cid::string $detail::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $items]]
    [then $r]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $rb [$flow [$nth $items $i] $r.n $r.ch $detail]]
        [$cancel-emit $items [+ $i 1]
          [$r-of $cid $rb.n $rb.ch [$jn3 $r.out $rb.out [$ledge-line $cid $rb.id "cancel"]]]
          $cid $detail]]]]]

[; ── services / workers / http ── ]
[?def service-flow pure [returns map] ($d::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string)
  [?let
    [= $nm [$str-lab $d "name"]]
    [= $label [?if [= $nm ""] [then "[?service]"] [else [$concat "[?service] \"" $nm "\""]]]]
    [= $id [$nid $n]]
    [$r-of $id [+ $n 1] $ch [$mk-subr $id $label]]]]

[?def worker-flow pure [returns map] ($d::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string)
  [?let
    [= $nm [$str-lab $d "name"]]
    [= $body [$lab $d "body"]]
    [= $label [?if [= $nm ""] [then "[?worker]"] [else [$concat "[?worker] \"" $nm "\""]]]]
    [= $wid [$nid $n]]
    [= $head [$mk-subr $wid $label]]
    [?if [$exists $body]
      [then
        [?let [= $rb [$flow [$lab-val $body] [+ $n 1] $ch $detail]]
          [$r-of $wid $rb.n $rb.ch [$jn3 $head $rb.out [$ledge-line $wid $rb.id ":body"]]]]]
      [else [$r-of $wid [+ $n 1] $ch $head]]]]]

[?def http-client-flow pure [returns map] ($d::any $n::int $ch::element $detail::string)
  [?let
    [= $mu [$http-method-url [$kids $d] 1 "" ""]]
    [= $label0 "[?http-client]"]
    [= $label1 [?if [= $mu.m ""] [then $label0] [else [$concat $label0 " " $mu.m]]]]
    [= $label [?if [= $mu.u ""] [then $label1] [else [$concat $label1 " " $mu.u]]]]
    [= $id [$nid $n]]
    [$r-of $id [+ $n 1] $ch [$mk-subr $id $label]]]]

[?def http-method-url pure [returns map] ($ks::any $i::int $m::string $u::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then {m: $m, u: $u}]
    [else
      [?let [= $k [$nth $ks $i]]
        [?if [$sought $k ("get", "post", "put", "delete", "patch")]
          [then
            [?let
              [= $v [$first [?for [in $x $k/*] [yield $x]]]]
              [= $u2 [?if [= [$name $v] "cx:str"] [then [$string $v]] [else $u]]]
              [$http-method-url $ks [+ $i 1] [$str-upper [$local-of $k]] $u2]]]
          [else [$http-method-url $ks [+ $i 1] $m $u]]]]]]]

[; ══ §6 dialect + sequence emitter ═══════════════════════════════════ ]

[?def top-level-temporal pure [returns bool] ($e::any)
  [?if [not [$is-cx $e]]
    [then false]
    [else
      [?let [= $l [$local-of $e]]
        [?if [or [= $l "http-service"] [or [= $l "worker"] [= $l "select"]]]
          [then true]
          [else [?if [= $l "let"]
            [then
              [?let [= $body [$lab $e "body"]]
                [?if [$exists $body] [then [$top-level-temporal [$lab-val $body]]] [else false]]]]
            [else false]]]]]]]]

[; seq-walk — the sequenceDiagram stub: one note per directive, slots
   recursed in order (labeled wraps recurse into their value). ]
[?def seq-walk pure [returns string] ($e::any $acc::string)
  [?if [not [$is-cx $e]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $l [$local-of $e]]
        [?if [= $l "for-comp"]
          [then
            [?let [= $y [$first [?for [in $k $e/*] [where [= [$name $k] "cx:yield"]] [yield [$first [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]]]]]
              [$seq-walk $y [$jn $acc "    Note over Caller: [?for]"]]]]
          [else [?if [or [$value-tag $l] [not [$is-cx $e]]]
            [then $acc]
            [else
              [$seq-kids [$kids $e] 1
                [$jn $acc [$concat "    Note over Caller: [?" $l "]"]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def seq-kids pure [returns string] ($ks::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $k [$nth $ks $i]]
        [; a labeled wrap recurses into its VALUE (V walks slot.value);
           a positional child recurses directly. ]
        [= $v [?if [?if [$is-cx $k]
                     [then [?if [not [$value-tag [$local-of $k]]] [then [= [$count $k/*] 1]] [else false]]]
                     [else false]]
          [then [$seq-label-value $k]]
          [else $k]]]
        [$seq-kids $ks [+ $i 1] [$seq-walk $v $acc]]]]]]

[; seq-label-value — a single-child cx:L wrap: when L itself has a flow
   rule the child IS the directive (positional); otherwise it is a
   labeled wrap and the walk descends into the wrapped value. ]
[?def seq-label-value pure [returns any] ($k::any)
  [?if [$admitted-or-nested [$local-of $k]]
    [then $k]
    [else [$first [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]]]]

[; ══ §7 the public render / extract surface ══════════════════════════ ]

[; render-mermaid — the §10.1.2 Mermaid reference renderer. $program is
   the engine-injected program-XML image (DRW1-1); $source the verbatim
   source bytes; $detail one of min|compact|full (DR-11 rungs; bare
   `mermaid` maps to min at the seam). ]
[; admitted-top / unrenderable — the ONE §10.1.2 top-level admission
   check, shared by all three formats (wave 2 unified them; the V
   svg/png path carried a second copy of the set). ]
[?def admitted-top pure [returns bool] ($program::any)
  [?if [not [$is-cx $program]]
    [then true]
    [else
      [?let [= $l [$local-of $program]]
        [?if [$value-tag $l]
          [then true]
          [else [?if [= $l "for-comp"] [then true] [else [$admitted $l]]]]]]]]]

[?def unrenderable pure [returns any] ($program::any)
  [err code="cx-err:CXER0281"
       message=[$concat "cx-err:CXER0281 E_UNRENDERABLE_DIRECTIVE: `[?" [$local-of $program] "]` is not in the §10.1.2 locked render-rules table"]]]

[?def render-mermaid scope=public pure [returns any] ($program::element $source::string $detail::string)
  [?if [not [$admitted-top $program]]
    [then [$unrenderable $program]]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $marker [$concat "%%cx:" [$bytes-to-base64 [$bytes-from-string-utf8 $source]] "%%"]]
        [?if [$top-level-temporal $program]
          [then [$jn [$jn $marker "sequenceDiagram"] [$seq-walk $program ""]]]
          [else
            [; RULED: D913-1 (#913) — a document with no program
               structure renders its element TREE, not the
               start→…→result envelope (see the data-tree defs by
               render-dot-detail). Any cx-node mark anywhere keeps the
               shipped envelope render byte-identically. ]
            [?if [$data-tree-doc $program]
              [then
                [?let [= $r [$data-flow-emit $program [$jn $marker "flowchart TD"] 1 "" $detail]]
                  $r.out]]
              [else
                [?let
                  [= $head [$jn $marker "flowchart TD"]]
                  [= $entry "n1"]
                  [= $exit "n2"]
                  [= $pre [$jn [$mk-round $entry "start"] [$mk-round $exit "result"]]]
                  [= $r [$flow $program 3 [chans] $detail]]
                  [= $tail [?if [= $r.id $exit]
                    [then [$edge-line $entry $r.id]]
                    [else [$jn [$edge-line $entry $r.id] [$edge-line $r.id $exit]]]]]
                  [$jn4 $head $pre $r.out $tail]]]]]]]]]]

[; extract-mermaid — recover the embedded source from a rendered
   Mermaid diagram (`%%cx:<base64>%%` leading comment). ]
[?def extract-mermaid scope=public pure [returns any] ($rendered::string)
  [?let [= $open [$str-find $rendered "%%cx:"]]
    [?if [< $open 0]
      [then [err code="cx-err:CXER0100" message="mermaid output missing %%cx:…%% marker"]]
      [else
        [?let
          [= $start [+ $open 5]]
          [= $close [$str-find-from $rendered "%%" $start]]
          [?if [< $close 0]
            [then [err code="cx-err:CXER0100" message="mermaid output missing %%cx:…%% close marker"]]
            [else [$bytes-to-string-utf8 [$bytes-from-base64 [$str-slice $rendered $start $close]]]]]]]]]]

[; extract-svg — recover the embedded source from an SVG rendering
   (`<metadata><cx:source>` block). ]
[?def extract-svg scope=public pure [returns any] ($rendered::string)
  [?let [= $a [$str-find $rendered "<cx:source"]]
    [?if [< $a 0]
      [then [err code="cx-err:CXER0100" message="svg output missing <cx:source> metadata"]]
      [else
        [?let [= $gt [$str-find-from $rendered ">" $a]]
          [?if [< $gt 0]
            [then [err code="cx-err:CXER0100" message="svg <cx:source> tag malformed"]]
            [else
              [?let
                [= $body-start [+ $gt 1]]
                [= $b [$str-find-from $rendered "</cx:source>" $body-start]]
                [?if [< $b 0]
                  [then [err code="cx-err:CXER0100" message="svg <cx:source> not closed"]]
                  [else [$bytes-to-string-utf8 [$bytes-from-base64 [$str-slice $rendered $body-start $b]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[; extract-png — recover the embedded source from a PNG rendering
   (tEXt chunk keyed `cx-source`); $rendered is the PNG bytes. ]
[?def extract-png scope=public pure [returns any] ($rendered::bytes)
  [?if [< [$bytes-length $rendered] 8]
    [then [err code="cx-err:CXER0100" message="png too small (less than 8-byte signature)"]]
    [else [$png-chunk-walk $rendered 8]]]]

[?def png-chunk-walk pure [returns any] ($b::bytes $pos::int)
  [?if [> [+ $pos 8] [$bytes-length $b]]
    [then [err code="cx-err:CXER0100" message="png output missing cx-source tEXt chunk"]]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $len [+ [* [$bytes-at $b $pos] 16777216]
                 [+ [* [$bytes-at $b [+ $pos 1]] 65536]
                 [+ [* [$bytes-at $b [+ $pos 2]] 256]
                    [$bytes-at $b [+ $pos 3]]]]]]
        [= $data-start [+ $pos 8]]
        [= $data-end [+ $data-start $len]]
        [?if [> $data-end [$bytes-length $b]]
          [then [err code="cx-err:CXER0100" message="png chunk length exceeds file bytes"]]
          [else
            [?let [= $ctype [$bytes-to-string-utf8 [$bytes-slice $b [+ $pos 4] [+ $pos 8]]]]
              [?if [= $ctype "tEXt"]
                [then
                  [?let
                    [= $data [$bytes-slice $b $data-start $data-end]]
                    [= $sep [$bytes-find $data [$bytes-from-hex "00"]]]
                    [?if [< $sep 0]
                      [then [$png-chunk-walk $b [+ $data-end 4]]]
                      [else
                        [?if [= [$bytes-to-string-utf8 [$bytes-slice $data 0 $sep]] "cx-source"]
                          [then [$bytes-to-string-utf8 [$bytes-from-base64
                            [$bytes-to-string-utf8 [$bytes-slice $data [+ $sep 1] [$bytes-length $data]]]]]]
                          [else [$png-chunk-walk $b [+ $data-end 4]]]]]]]]
                [else [$png-chunk-walk $b [+ $data-end 4]]]]]]]]]]]

[; ══ §8 DOT / SVG / PNG — the vector half (wave 2, DR-2a/DR-9a) ═════
   Everything here is text→text or bytes→bytes EXCEPT the single
   `dot` hop in render-svg / render-png, which is the module's only
   impure surface: `[$process-run ["dot" "-T…"] …]` under the
   `subprocess` capability with the executable allowlist `dot`
   (security.md §2's constraint field used as designed). The V pair
   shell_dot / import_os_execute is DELETED, not wrapped.

   The primitive is called POSITIONALLY (no [?lib] — see the module
   header): the argument order is cx-stdlib/process §3.1's
   ($argv $env $env-clear $cwd $stdin $timeout-ms $kill-on-timeout
    $capture $encoding $search-path $new-process-group $check). ]

[; ── little helpers ── ]
[?def num pure [returns string] ($n::int) [?str '{$n}']]

[?def b64 pure [returns string] ($s::string)
  [$bytes-to-base64 [$bytes-from-string-utf8 $s]]]

[?def hexdigit pure [returns string] ($n::int)
  [$str-slice "0123456789abcdef" $n [+ $n 1]]]

[?def hex2 pure [returns string] ($b::int)
  [$concat [$hexdigit [$math-bit-shift-right $b 4]] [$hexdigit [$math-bit-and $b 15]]]]

[; be32-hex — a big-endian u32 as 8 hex digits (the PNG length + CRC
   fields; paired with [$bytes-from-hex]). ]
[?def be32-hex pure [returns string] ($v::int)
  [$concat
    [$hex2 [$math-bit-and [$math-bit-shift-right $v 24] 255]]
    [$hex2 [$math-bit-and [$math-bit-shift-right $v 16] 255]]
    [$hex2 [$math-bit-and [$math-bit-shift-right $v 8] 255]]
    [$hex2 [$math-bit-and $v 255]]]]

[; be32-at — read a big-endian u32 at a byte offset. ]
[?def be32-at pure [returns int] ($b::bytes $off::int)
  [+ [* [$bytes-at $b $off] 16777216]
     [+ [* [$bytes-at $b [+ $off 1]] 65536]
        [+ [* [$bytes-at $b [+ $off 2]] 256]
           [$bytes-at $b [+ $off 3]]]]]]

[; ── PNG CRC-32 (RFC 2083: poly 0xEDB88320, init/final 0xFFFFFFFF) ──
   The bitwise form, byte by byte — no table. Verified against the
   known vectors (crc32("abc") = 0x352441C2, crc32("IEND") =
   0xAE426082). Cost is 8 CX iterations per byte; the chunk data is
   base64 of the source, so a large program pays for it — recorded in
   the module spec's performance section beside the render budget. ]
[?def crc32-bits pure [returns int] ($c::int $i::int)
  [?if [> $i 7]
    [then $c]
    [else [$crc32-bits
      [?if [= [$math-bit-and $c 1] 1]
        [then [$math-bit-xor [$math-bit-shift-right $c 1] 3988292384]]
        [else [$math-bit-shift-right $c 1]]]
      [+ $i 1]]]]]

[?def crc32-acc pure [returns int] ($b::bytes $i::int $len::int $crc::int)
  [?if [>= $i $len]
    [then $crc]
    [else [$crc32-acc $b [+ $i 1] $len
      [$crc32-bits [$math-bit-xor $crc [$bytes-at $b $i]] 0]]]]]

[?def crc32 scope=public pure [returns int] ($b::bytes)
  [$math-bit-xor [$crc32-acc $b 0 [$bytes-length $b] 4294967295] 4294967295]]

[; ── PNG chunk construction ── ]
[?def png-chunk pure [returns bytes] ($ctype::string $data::bytes)
  [?let
    [= $body [$bytes-concat ([$bytes-from-string-utf8 $ctype], $data)]]
    [$bytes-concat
      ([$bytes-from-hex [$be32-hex [$bytes-length $data]]],
       $body,
       [$bytes-from-hex [$be32-hex [$crc32 $body]]])]]]

[; png-text-data — the cx-source tEXt payload: keyword, NUL, base64. ]
[?def png-text-data pure [returns bytes] ($source::string)
  [$bytes-concat
    ([$bytes-from-string-utf8 "cx-source"],
     [$bytes-from-hex "00"],
     [$bytes-from-string-utf8 [$b64 $source]])]]

[; ── the dot-less envelopes (DR-3a: the NAMED normative contract) ── ]
[?def svg-envelope scope=public pure [returns string] ($source::string)
  [$concat
    "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n"
    "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1 1\">\n"
    "  <metadata><cx:source xmlns:cx=\"https://cx.lang/v1\">"
    [$b64 $source]
    "</cx:source></metadata>\n</svg>\n"]]

[; png-envelope — a valid 1×1 grayscale PNG carrying the source in a
   cx-source tEXt chunk. IDAT is the fixed minimal zlib stream for a
   single zero scanline (the shipped bytes, preserved). ]
[?def png-envelope scope=public pure [returns bytes] ($source::string)
  [$bytes-concat
    ([$bytes-from-hex "89504e470d0a1a0a"],
     [$png-chunk "IHDR" [$bytes-from-hex "00000001000000010800000000"]],
     [$png-chunk "tEXt" [$png-text-data $source]],
     [$png-chunk "IDAT" [$bytes-from-hex "789c6260000000020001"]],
     [$png-chunk "IEND" [$bytes-from-hex ""]])]]

[; ── the two splices ──
   inject-svg-metadata inserts the carrier as the ROOT ELEMENT'S FIRST
   CHILD — immediately after the `<svg …>` start tag (RULED: DSC-1a,
   ledger/rulings_2026_08_20_diagram_svg_capability.md).

   It used to splice after the FIRST `>` in the document. On real
   graphviz output that `>` closes the `<?xml …?>` declaration, so the
   block landed in the PROLOG: before the doctype and outside the root
   element. XML 1.0 §2.1 admits exactly one top-level element and no
   element before the doctype, so the parser took `<metadata>` as the
   document element and reported the whole drawing as extra content —
   the emitted SVG was never well-formed. Mini-ruling DRW2-2 preserved
   that bit-for-bit because a correctness fix inside the #758 port
   would have been unreviewable; DSC-1 supersedes it and fixes it.

   SVG 1.1 §5.10 admits `metadata` as a child of `svg`, conventionally
   first — the one position that is valid, keeps the carrier inside the
   document it describes, and needs no extractor change (extract-svg
   scans for `<cx:source` anywhere).

   A `<svg` that never appears is a pass-through, as before. ]
[; min-pos — the smaller of two `$str-find` results, where -1 means
   "not present" and therefore loses to any real index. ]
[?def min-pos pure [returns int] ($a::int $b::int)
  [?if [< $a 0]
    [then $b]
    [else [?if [< $b 0] [then $a] [else [?if [< $a $b] [then $a] [else $b]]]]]]]

[; svg-start-tag-end — the index of the `>` that closes the start tag
   scanning from $i, skipping any `>` that sits inside a single- or
   double-quoted attribute value (XML 1.0 `AttValue`). -1 when the tag
   never closes. The root start tag is short, so the walk is one hop
   per quoted attribute, not per character. ]
[?def svg-start-tag-end pure [returns int] ($s::string $i::int)
  [?let
    [= $gt [$str-find-from $s ">" $i]]
    [= $q [$min-pos [$str-find-from $s "\"" $i] [$str-find-from $s "'" $i]]]
    [?if [< $gt 0]
      [then -1]
      [else
        [?if [?if [< $q 0] [then true] [else [> $q $gt]]]
          [then $gt]
          [else
            [?let [= $close [$str-find-from $s [$str-slice $s $q [+ $q 1]] [+ $q 1]]]
              [?if [< $close 0]
                [then -1]
                [else [$svg-start-tag-end $s [+ $close 1]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def inject-svg-metadata scope=public pure [returns string] ($svg::string $source::string)
  [?let [= $root [$str-find $svg "<svg"]]
    [?if [< $root 0]
      [then $svg]
      [else
        [?let [= $end [$svg-start-tag-end $svg [+ $root 4]]]
          [?if [< $end 0]
            [then $svg]
            [else
              [?let
                [= $meta [$concat
                  "\n  <metadata><cx:source xmlns:cx=\"https://cx.lang/v1\">"
                  [$b64 $source]
                  "</cx:source></metadata>"]]
                [?if [= [$str-slice $svg [- $end 1] $end] "/"]
                  [; a self-closing root has no child position — open it
                     into a container so the carrier has somewhere to live. ]
                  [then [$concat
                    [$str-slice $svg 0 [- $end 1]]
                    ">"
                    $meta
                    "\n</svg>"
                    [$str-slice $svg [+ $end 1] [$str-length $svg]]]]
                  [else [$concat
                    [$str-slice $svg 0 [+ $end 1]]
                    $meta
                    [$str-slice $svg [+ $end 1] [$str-length $svg]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[; inject-png-chunk splices the tEXt chunk immediately after IHDR
   (which RFC 2083 fixes as the first chunk after the signature). A
   blob too small to be a PNG, or a bad IHDR length, passes through
   unmodified — the shipped defensive behavior. ]
[?def inject-png-chunk scope=public pure [returns bytes] ($png::bytes $source::string)
  [?if [< [$bytes-length $png] 33]
    [then $png]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $insert-at [+ [+ 16 [$be32-at $png 8]] 4]]
        [?if [> $insert-at [$bytes-length $png]]
          [then $png]
          [else
            [$bytes-concat
              ([$bytes-slice $png 0 $insert-at],
               [$png-chunk "tEXt" [$png-text-data $source]],
               [$bytes-slice $png $insert-at [$bytes-length $png]])]]]]]]]

[; ── DOT emission ──
   The shipped walk's two quirks are PRESERVED bit-for-bit (DR-8):
   the node id is the emitter buffer's CURRENT LINE COUNT (not a
   counter), and the root is emitted with parent 0, so every diagram
   carries an edge from a node `n0` that is never declared. ]
[?def dot-escape pure [returns string] ($s::string)
  [$str-replace $s "\"" "\\\""]]

[; dot-kind classifies one image child exactly as the V walk's match
   arms did: a for-comp node, a directive node, a labeled-slot wrapper
   to descend through, or a value to skip entirely.

   The discriminator is the injected image's `cx-node` MARK, not the
   tag: the §4 tag conflates a directive with a same-named value image
   (`<cx:str>` is both a string literal and a `[?str]` directive;
   `<cx:map>` is both a map literal and `[?map]`), and the grammar
   registry cannot break that tie — asking it made a string literal
   render as a `[?str]` node, which the pre-cutover DOT goldens caught
   (consult finding C13). ]
[?def dot-kind pure [returns string] ($k::any)
  [?if [not [$is-cx $k]]
    [; RULED: D913-1 (#913) — the lift's single-child `item` wrapper is
       a container to DESCEND (reachable only under cx:block, since the
       other item-wrapping tags — cx:seq/cx:arr — stay skipped values);
       every other non-cx element stays skipped, as shipped. ]
    [then [?if [and [= [$name $k] "item"] [= [$count $k/*] 1]]
      [then "wrapper"]
      [else "skip"]]]
    [else
      [?if [$exists $k@cx-node]
        [then [$string $k@cx-node]]
        [else [?if [= [$local-of $k] "block"]
          [; RULED: D913-1 (#913) — a multi-form program descends into
             its forms instead of vanishing: cx:block was in the skip
             set, so `cx diagram --format=svg` of ANY multi-form
             document was an empty canvas with exit 0. ]
          [then "wrapper"]
          [else [?if [$value-tag [$local-of $k]] [then "skip"] [else "wrapper"]]]]]]]]]

[; dot-yield-of — the for-comp's yield VALUE as a one-item sequence
   (the V walk recurses into `node.yield` and nothing else; the clause
   children are never visited). ]
[?def dot-yield-of pure [returns any] ($f::any)
  [?let [= $y [$first [?for [in $k $f/*] [where [= [$name $k] "cx:yield"]] [yield $k]]]]
    [?if [$exists $y]
      [then [?for [in $v $y/*] [yield $v]]]
      [else ()]]]]

[?def dot-emit pure [returns map] ($k::any $out::string $nl::int $parent::int)
  [?let [= $kind [$dot-kind $k]]
    [?if [= $kind "skip"]
      [then {out: $out, n: $nl}]
      [else [?if [= $kind "wrapper"]
        [then [$dot-emit-kids [$kids $k] 1 $out $nl $parent]]
        [else
          [?let
            [= $idx $nl]
            [= $label [?if [= $kind "for-comp"]
              [then "for-comp"]
              [else [$concat "[?" [$local-of $k] "]"]]]]
            [= $out1 [$jn $out [$concat "  n" [$num $idx] " [label=\"" [$dot-escape $label] "\"];"]]]
            [= $out2 [?if [>= $parent 0]
              [then [$jn $out1 [$concat "  n" [$num $parent] " -> n" [$num $idx] ";"]]]
              [else $out1]]]
            [= $nl2 [?if [>= $parent 0] [then [+ $nl 2]] [else [+ $nl 1]]]]
            [?if [= $kind "for-comp"]
              [then [$dot-emit-kids [$dot-yield-of $k] 1 $out2 $nl2 $idx]]
              [else [$dot-emit-kids [$kids $k] 1 $out2 $nl2 $idx]]]]]]]]]]

[?def dot-emit-kids pure [returns map] ($ks::any $i::int $out::string $nl::int $parent::int)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then {out: $out, n: $nl}]
    [else
      [?let [= $r [$dot-emit [$nth $ks $i] $out $nl $parent]]
        [$dot-emit-kids $ks [+ $i 1] $r.out $r.n $parent]]]]]

[?def render-dot scope=public pure [returns string] ($program::element)
  [$render-dot-detail $program "min"]]

[; ── RULED: D913-1 (#913) — the data-tree render ─────────────────────
   A document with NO program structure to draw — no cx-node-marked
   node anywhere in its image — but at least one real element renders
   its ELEMENT TREE: elements as nodes on the same min|compact|full
   label ladder ([$label]), containment as edges, in mermaid, dot, svg
   and png alike. The ERD lane proved the D910-1 lift already carries
   this content; before this ruling the DOT walk emitted ZERO nodes for
   such documents (an 8pt EMPTY canvas with exit 0 — the #910
   silent-degradation class, one lane over) and the flowchart collapsed
   the whole document to the start→…→result envelope. Directive
   renders are untouched BY CONSTRUCTION: any cx-node mark anywhere
   routes to the shipped walks byte-identically (the DR-8 pins and the
   full golden corpus constrain this to zero movement).

   data-tree-el — a node the tree renders: the ERD entity admission,
   minus the lift's own `item`/`entry` wrappers (dgi_items_wrapper /
   the map lift), which are containers the walk descends through, not
   content. (A user element genuinely NAMED `item`/`entry` folds into
   its parent — the image cannot distinguish it from the wrapper; the
   ERD lane makes the same trade.) ]
[?def data-tree-el pure [returns bool] ($k::any)
  [?if [$cd-erd-entity $k]
    [then [not [or [= [$name $k] "item"] [= [$name $k] "entry"]]]]
    [else false]]]

[; ── the TI-1 table image (#914, RULED;
   ledger/rulings_2026_08_21_table_image.md) ──
   The lift gives a table-carrying element ONE `cx:table rows=N` child
   holding one empty `cx:col name= type=` per declared column. Rows are
   SHAPE, not content: the count is in the image, the values never are.

   cd-table-cols-of — the columns of a `cx:table` node itself.
   cd-table-cols   — the columns of an ELEMENT's table child (the ERD's
                     entity fields).
   cd-has-table / cd-table-rows — presence, and the row count as its
                     image text (`""` when the element carries no table). ]
[?def cd-table-cols-of pure [returns any] ($t::any)
  [?for [in $c $t/*] [where [= [$name $c] "cx:col"]] [yield $c]]]

[?def cd-table-cols pure [returns any] ($n::any)
  [?for [in $k $n/*] [in $c $k/*]
    [where [and [= [$name $k] "cx:table"] [= [$name $c] "cx:col"]]]
    [yield $c]]]

[?def cd-has-table pure [returns bool] ($n::any)
  [$exists [$first [?for [in $k $n/*] [where [= [$name $k] "cx:table"]] [yield 1]]]]]

[?def cd-table-rows pure [returns string] ($n::any)
  [?let [= $hits [?for [in $k $n/*] [where [= [$name $k] "cx:table"]]
      [yield [$string $k@rows]]]]
    [?if [= [$count $hits] 0] [then ""] [else [$first $hits]]]]]

[; cd-table-label — RULED: TI-1, render rule 2 — the tree/DOT walks
   render a `cx:table` child as ONE node carrying the table's SHAPE. The
   columns do NOT each become a node: a 20-column table would drown the
   drawing, and per-column detail is the ERD lane's job. ]
[?def cd-table-label pure [returns string] ($t::any)
  [$concat "table(" [$string [$count [$cd-table-cols-of $t]]] " cols × "
           [$string $t@rows] " rows)"]]

[?def data-tree-doc pure [returns bool] ($img::any)
  [?if [not [= [$cd-node-kind $img] ""]]
    [then false]
    [else
      [; RULED: D913-1a (#913 addendum) — an element ROOT engages the
         tree even when directives sit INSIDE it (they render as
         [?name] LEAVES, never descended): the element-wrapped tours'
         honest picture is their section tree. A directive at top
         level — the root, or any form of a multi-form block — keeps
         the program render. ]
      [?if [$data-tree-el $img]
        [then true]
        [else
          [?if [and [$is-cx $img] [= [$local-of $img] "block"]]
            [then
              [?let [= $forms [$block-forms $img]]
                [?if [$exists [$first [?for [in $f $forms]
                    [where [not [= [$cd-node-kind $f] ""]]] [yield 1]]]]
                  [then false]
                  [else [$exists [$first [?for [in $f $forms]
                      [where [$data-tree-el $f]] [yield 1]]]]]]]]
            [else
              [; other wrapper roots (cx:seq/arr/map): the original
                 D913-1 whole-tree rule — no mark anywhere and an
                 element somewhere. ]
              [?if [$exists [$first [?for [in $k $img//*]
                  [where [not [= [$cd-node-kind $k] ""]]] [yield 1]]]]
                [then false]
                [else [$exists [$first [?for [in $k $img//*]
                    [where [$data-tree-el $k]] [yield 1]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[; the mermaid tree walk — R = {out, n}; attrs live in the label chips
   (cx:attr skipped whole), scalar/collection content is the label's
   ` …` body marker, and non-element wrappers are descended through so
   nested elements keep the nearest ELEMENT ancestor as their parent. ]
[?def data-flow-emit pure [returns map] ($k::any $out::string $n::int $parent::string $detail::string)
  [?if [= [$name $k] "cx:attr"]
    [then {out: $out, n: $n}]
    [else
      [?if [= [$name $k] "cx:table"]
        [; RULED: TI-1 — the table SHAPE node, one per table. ]
        [then
          [?let
            [= $id [$nid $n]]
            [= $out1 [$jn $out [$mk-rect $id [$cd-table-label $k]]]]
            [= $out2 [?if [= $parent ""]
              [then $out1]
              [else [$jn $out1 [$edge-line $parent $id]]]]]
            {out: $out2, n: [+ $n 1]}]]
        [else
      [?if [not [= [$cd-node-kind $k] ""]]
        [; RULED: D913-1a — an embedded directive is a LEAF labeled
           [?name], never descended: demo-code interiors do not
           masquerade as data. ]
        [then
          [?let
            [= $id [$nid $n]]
            [= $lbl [?if [= [$cd-node-kind $k] "for-comp"]
              [then "[?for]"]
              [else [$concat "[?" [$local-of $k] "]"]]]]
            [= $out1 [$jn $out [$mk-rect $id $lbl]]]
            [= $out2 [?if [= $parent ""]
              [then $out1]
              [else [$jn $out1 [$edge-line $parent $id]]]]]
            {out: $out2, n: [+ $n 1]}]]
        [else
      [?if [$data-tree-el $k]
        [then
          [?let
            [= $id [$nid $n]]
            [= $out1 [$jn $out [$mk-rect $id [$label $k $detail]]]]
            [= $out2 [?if [= $parent ""]
              [then $out1]
              [else [$jn $out1 [$edge-line $parent $id]]]]]
            [$data-flow-kids [$kids $k] 1 $out2 [+ $n 1] $id $detail]]]
        [else [$data-flow-kids [$kids $k] 1 $out $n $parent $detail]]]]]]]]]]

[?def data-flow-kids pure [returns map] ($ks::any $i::int $out::string $n::int $parent::string $detail::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then {out: $out, n: $n}]
    [else
      [?let [= $r [$data-flow-emit [$nth $ks $i] $out $n $parent $detail]]
        [$data-flow-kids $ks [+ $i 1] $r.out $r.n $parent $detail]]]]]

[; the DOT tree walk — same admission, same labels ($detail ladder),
   DOT-escaped; fresh n1.. ids and NO phantom n0 edge (the quirk is the
   PROGRAM walk's preserved history, not this new surface's). ]
[?def dot-data-emit pure [returns map] ($k::any $out::string $n::int $parent::int $detail::string)
  [?if [= [$name $k] "cx:attr"]
    [then {out: $out, n: $n}]
    [else
      [?if [= [$name $k] "cx:table"]
        [; RULED: TI-1 — the table SHAPE node, DOT side. ]
        [then
          [?let
            [= $out1 [$jn $out [$concat "  n" [$num $n] " [label=\""
                                        [$dot-escape [$cd-table-label $k]] "\"];"]]]
            [= $out2 [?if [>= $parent 0]
              [then [$jn $out1 [$concat "  n" [$num $parent] " -> n" [$num $n] ";"]]]
              [else $out1]]]
            {out: $out2, n: [+ $n 1]}]]
        [else
      [?if [not [= [$cd-node-kind $k] ""]]
        [; RULED: D913-1a — the embedded-directive LEAF, DOT side. ]
        [then
          [?let
            [= $lbl [?if [= [$cd-node-kind $k] "for-comp"]
              [then "[?for]"]
              [else [$concat "[?" [$local-of $k] "]"]]]]
            [= $out1 [$jn $out [$concat "  n" [$num $n] " [label=\"" [$dot-escape $lbl] "\"];"]]]
            [= $out2 [?if [>= $parent 0]
              [then [$jn $out1 [$concat "  n" [$num $parent] " -> n" [$num $n] ";"]]]
              [else $out1]]]
            {out: $out2, n: [+ $n 1]}]]
        [else
      [?if [$data-tree-el $k]
        [then
          [?let
            [= $out1 [$jn $out [$concat "  n" [$num $n] " [label=\"" [$dot-escape [$label $k $detail]] "\"];"]]]
            [= $out2 [?if [>= $parent 0]
              [then [$jn $out1 [$concat "  n" [$num $parent] " -> n" [$num $n] ";"]]]
              [else $out1]]]
            [$dot-data-kids [$kids $k] 1 $out2 [+ $n 1] $n $detail]]]
        [else [$dot-data-kids [$kids $k] 1 $out $n $parent $detail]]]]]]]]]]

[?def dot-data-kids pure [returns map] ($ks::any $i::int $out::string $n::int $parent::int $detail::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then {out: $out, n: $n}]
    [else
      [?let [= $r [$dot-data-emit [$nth $ks $i] $out $n $parent $detail]]
        [$dot-data-kids $ks [+ $i 1] $r.out $r.n $parent $detail]]]]]

[; render-dot-detail — the ONE DOT entry: the D913-1 data tree when the
   image has no program structure, the shipped (quirk-preserving)
   program walk otherwise. `render-dot` (public, detail-less) delegates
   at min; of-source's dot/svg/png arms pass their $detail through. ]
[?def render-dot-detail pure [returns string] ($program::any $detail::string)
  [?let
    [= $head [$jn3 "digraph CX {" "  rankdir=TB;" "  node [shape=box,fontname=\"Helvetica\"];"]]
    [?if [$data-tree-doc $program]
      [then
        [?let [= $r [$dot-data-emit $program $head 1 -1 $detail]]
          [$jn $r.out "}"]]]
      [else
        [?let [= $r [$dot-emit $program $head 3 0]]
          [$jn $r.out "}"]]]]]]

[; ── the graphviz hop (the module's ONLY impure surface) ──
   TWO conditions, TWO answers (RULED: DSC-1c, superseding DRW2-1 and
   §6's former "every reason takes one road"):

   * `subprocess` WITHHELD  → REFUSE, loudly and typed (CXER0271). The
     caller asked for a rendered diagram and has not paid for the
     effect; silently handing back a 1×1 envelope would answer a
     question nobody asked.
   * `dot` ABSENT / non-zero exit / spawn failure / timeout → the
     dot-less ENVELOPE. Still the named normative contract of §6: the
     caller DID grant the effect, the machine simply has no graphviz.

   The two are told apart by the err code the effect point returns.
   The capability guard is fail-closed BEFORE any effect and yields
   `cx-err:CXER0271`; every other failure yields a CXER40xx code or a
   `proc-result` with a non-zero exit.

   [?fallback]/[recover-with] replaces the former [?else] coalesce so
   the err is INSPECTED instead of discarded. C14's requirement still
   holds — the denial never propagates railway-style out of the [?let]
   binding (#853); it arrives as a value this function decides on. ]
[?def dot-ok pure [returns bool] ($r::any)
  [?if [= [$name $r] "proc-result"]
    [then [= $r@exit-code 0]]
    [else false]]]

[; cap-denied — did the hop fail because `subprocess` was withheld? ]
[?def cap-denied pure [returns bool] ($r::any)
  [?if [= [$name $r] "dot-failure"]
    [then [= [$concat "" $r@code] "cx-err:CXER0271"]]
    [else false]]]

[; the DSC-1c refusal: names the capability AND the exact flag. ]
[?def dot-denied-err pure [returns any] ($fmt::string)
  [err code="cx-err:CXER0271"
    message=[$concat "E_CAP_DENIED: subprocess capability required to run graphviz `dot` for the "
                     $fmt " diagram format; none granted (grant via --allow-subprocess)"]]]

[?def render-svg scope=public impure [returns any] ($program::element $source::string)
  [?if [not [$admitted-top $program]]
    [then [$unrenderable $program]]
    [else
      [?let [= $r [?fallback [$process-run ("dot", "-Tsvg") null false null [$render-dot $program] null true :stdout "utf-8" true false false]
                    [recover-with [dot-failure code=$err@code]]]]
        [?if [$cap-denied $r]
          [then [$dot-denied-err "svg"]]
          [else
            [?if [$dot-ok $r]
              [then [$inject-svg-metadata [$string $r@stdout] $source]]
              [else [$svg-envelope $source]]]]]]]]]

[?def render-png scope=public impure [returns any] ($program::element $source::string)
  [?if [not [$admitted-top $program]]
    [then [$unrenderable $program]]
    [else
      [?let [= $r [?fallback [$process-run ("dot", "-Tpng") null false null [$render-dot $program] null true :stdout :bytes true false false]
                    [recover-with [dot-failure code=$err@code]]]]
        [?if [$cap-denied $r]
          [then [$dot-denied-err "png"]]
          [else
            [?if [$dot-ok $r]
              [then [$inject-png-chunk $r@stdout $source]]
              [else [$png-envelope $source]]]]]]]]]

[; ══ §9 WAVE 3 — the playground renderer (CFG / ERD / SEQ) ═══════════
   #889, RULED DRW3-1…DRW3-5 (ledger/rulings_2026_08_20_diagram_wave3.md).
   The SECOND renderer — auto-detecting: data → ERD, sequence-shape code
   → SEQ, other code → CFG — behind `cx code-diagram` and the wasm export
   `cx_code_diagram_with_level`. Ported from vcx/code/code_diagram.v,
   which is DELETED in the same landing (DR-9a, cutover-first).

   INGRESS (DRW3-3): unlike the reference renderer, this one starts from
   SOURCE TEXT — it strips `[?cx …]` PIs, applies the surviving DRW3-2
   parser patch, and degrades to a text-level classification when the
   parse fails. The text work is pure CX; the parse is the engine's, reached
   through the module's own native primitive
   `[$diagram-program-image SRC MODE]` (vcx/code/stdlib_diagram.v). MODE
   "code" adds the DRW3-4 `[?def]` expansion.

   BIT-FOR-BIT (DR-8a): pinned against
   vcx/tests/testdata/code_diagram_golden/ — 88 sources (46 graph-view
   conformance fixtures + 42 synthetic pins) × 3 levels, captured from
   the unmodified V emitter BEFORE the cutover. ]

[; ── §9.0 the sealed WAVE-3 rule table (DR-4a, gated by DR-5) ─────────
   One artifact for the playground renderer's classification, exactly as
   §1 is for the reference renderer: the sequence-trigger set, the set
   of directives that BREAK a CFG basic block, the SEQ inner-dispatch
   classes, and the ERD scalar-type map. The emitters below read THIS
   table — the sets are not written twice, so the drift finding 6 named
   cannot recur here either. `vcx/tests/code_diagram_completeness_gate_test.v`
   diffs it against the grammar registry, the live dispatch, and the
   golden corpus. ]
[?def code-rules scope=public pure [returns element] ()
  [code-rules
    [trigger directive=worker       rule="Actor lane; body emitted inside an activate/deactivate frame"]
    [trigger directive=channel      rule="Channel lane; the [?let] binding aliases it"]
    [trigger directive=http-service rule="Service lane plus the implicit client lane"]
    [trigger directive=select       rule="alt/else frame, one arm per case"]
    [trigger directive=async        rule="Detached async-N lane with a spawn arrow"]
    [breaks-block directive=if     rule="Diamond with true/false arm targets"]
    [breaks-block directive=match  rule="Dispatcher with one labeled edge per arm"]
    [breaks-block directive=modify rule="Single update block: modify @ FOCUS | action | …"]
    [breaks-block directive=def    rule="Own subgraph with a trapezoid entry and stadium exit"]
    [breaks-block directive=for    rule="Loop box with a binds $x edge and a back-edge"]
    [breaks-block directive=let    rule="Binding-setup node feeding the body's control flow"]
    [seq directive=send            class=send       rule="worker ->>+ channel : payload"]
    [seq directive=try-send        class=send       rule="worker ->>+ channel : payload (try)"]
    [seq directive=receive         class=receive    rule="channel -->>- worker : msg"]
    [seq directive=try-receive     class=receive    rule="channel -->>- worker : msg (try[, timeout])"]
    [seq directive=select          class=select     rule="alt/else frame with a per-arm interaction"]
    [seq directive=async           class=async      rule="worker ->> async-N : start"]
    [seq directive=await           class=await      rule="Note over worker : await TARGET"]
    [seq directive=await-all       class=await      rule="Note over worker : await-all TARGET"]
    [seq directive=await-any       class=await      rule="Note over worker : await-any TARGET"]
    [seq directive=await-race      class=await      rule="Note over worker : await-race TARGET"]
    [seq directive=cancel          class=cancel     rule="worker -x lane : cancel"]
    [seq directive=retry           class=resilience rule="Note over worker : retry[ max=N at full]"]
    [seq directive=timeout         class=resilience rule="Note over worker : timeout[ after=D at full]"]
    [seq directive=circuit-breaker class=resilience rule="Note over worker : breaker[ threshold=N at full]"]
    [seq directive=rate-limit      class=resilience rule="Note over worker : rate-limit[ rate=N at full]"]
    [seq directive=bulkhead        class=resilience rule="Note over worker : bulkhead[ max=N at full]"]
    [seq directive=fallback        class=resilience rule="Note over worker : fallback[ recover-with=E at full]"]
    [seq directive=let             class=let        rule="Descend into the bound values and the body"]
    [seq directive=if              class=branch     rule="Descend into then/else arm bodies"]
    [seq directive=match           class=branch     rule="Descend into case arm bodies"]
    [seq directive=modify          class=branch     rule="Descend into the action bodies"]
    [seq directive=for             class=for        rule="Descend into the yield body"]
    [erd-type kind=int      type=int]
    [erd-type kind=bigint   type=bigint]
    [erd-type kind=decimal  type=decimal]
    [erd-type kind=float    type=float]
    [erd-type kind=bool     type=bool]
    [erd-type kind=atom     type=atom]
    [erd-type kind=date     type=date]
    [erd-type kind=datetime type=datetime]
    [erd-type kind=dur      type=duration]
    [erd-type kind=period   type=period]
    [erd-type kind=str      type=string]]]

[; code-class — the SEQ inner-dispatch class of a directive local name;
   "generic" (a `Note over WORKER : [?name]` line) for everything the
   table does not name. The emitter dispatches on THIS, so a row added
   or removed here moves the rendering. ]
[?def code-class scope=public pure [returns string] ($local::string)
  [?let [= $hit [$first [?for [in $r [$code-rules]/*]
      [where [?if [= [$name $r] "seq"] [then [= [$string $r@directive] $local]] [else false]]]
      [yield [$string $r@class]]]]]
    [?if [$exists $hit] [then $hit] [else "generic"]]]]

[; code-breaks-block — is this directive one that BREAKS a CFG basic
   block (the §D4 branching set)? ]
[?def code-breaks-block pure [returns bool] ($local::string)
  [$exists [$first [?for [in $r [$code-rules]/*]
    [where [?if [= [$name $r] "breaks-block"] [then [= [$string $r@directive] $local]] [else false]]]
    [yield 1]]]]]

[; ── §9.1 the pre-parse text layer (DRW3-2) ───────────────────────────
   strip_cx_pis / patch_match_arms. `patch_paths` retired at #899
   (RULED: ISW-1) — see the note where its defs stood.
   Scanning JUMPS between structural characters (str-find-from)
   rather than walking codepoints — the CX per-character cost makes a
   byte loop untenable on a real source, and jumping is observationally
   identical (every delimiter is ASCII, so codepoint and byte positions
   agree on where they fall). Each pass is guarded by a `contains` fast
   path: a source with no PI head, no slash, or no match head takes the
   pass as the identity, exactly as the byte loop did. ]

[?def cd-ident-ch pure [returns bool] ($c::string)
  [?if [= $c ""]
    [then false]
    [else [$str-contains
      "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789_-" $c]]]]

[; cd-at — codepoint at $i, "" when out of range (the V byte loop's
   `if i == 0 { u8(0) }` guard). ]
[?def cd-at pure [returns string] ($s::string $i::int)
  [?if [< $i 0]
    [then ""]
    [else [?if [>= $i [$str-length $s]] [then ""] [else [$str-at $s $i]]]]]]

[; cd-minp — the earliest non-negative of two find results (-1 = none). ]
[?def cd-minp pure [returns int] ($a::int $b::int)
  [?if [< $a 0]
    [then $b]
    [else [?if [< $b 0] [then $a] [else [?if [< $a $b] [then $a] [else $b]]]]]]]

[; cd-bracket-close — index one PAST the closing bracket of a group at
   depth $depth (the `[?cx …]` skip: no string awareness, per V). ]
[?def cd-bracket-close pure [returns int] ($s::string $j::int $depth::int)
  [?if [<= $depth 0]
    [then $j]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $o [$str-find-from $s "[" $j]]
        [= $c [$str-find-from $s "]" $j]]
        [?if [< $c 0]
          [then [$str-length $s]]
          [else [?if [?if [< $o 0] [then false] [else [< $o $c]]]
            [then [$cd-bracket-close $s [+ $o 1] [+ $depth 1]]]
            [else [$cd-bracket-close $s [+ $c 1] [- $depth 1]]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-strip-pis pure [returns string] ($s::string)
  [?if [not [$str-contains $s "[?cx"]] [then $s] [else [$cd-strip-loop $s 0 ""]]]]

[?def cd-strip-loop pure [returns string] ($s::string $i::int $acc::string)
  [?let [= $len [$str-length $s]]
    [?if [>= $i $len]
      [then $acc]
      [else
        [?let [= $p [$str-find-from $s "[?cx" $i]]
          [?if [< $p 0]
            [then [$concat $acc [$str-slice $s $i $len]]]
            [else
              [?let [= $after [+ $p 4]]
                [?if [$cd-ident-ch [$cd-at $s $after]]
                  [then [$cd-strip-loop $s $after [$concat $acc [$str-slice $s $i $after]]]]
                  [else [$cd-strip-loop $s [$cd-bracket-close $s $after 1]
                          [$concat $acc [$str-slice $s $i $p]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[; The `/Name` → `//Name` source rewrite (patch_paths) is RETIRED
   (#899, RULED: ISW-1). It came from the V emitter, where it made an
   absolute path parse at all. Re-measured at this head it no longer
   does anything for parseability — `[?let [= $x /root/item] $x]`
   parses today and fails only at EVAL, for want of `$doc` — and it was
   output-visible in the wrong direction: it labelled an absolute path
   as a descendant-anchored one (`//users/user` where the source wrote
   `/users/user`). A workaround that outlived its reason and only lied
   is gone; its three defs (cd-patch-paths, cd-next-quote-or-slash,
   cd-pp) go with it. `cd-patch-match-arms` SURVIVES: measured again
   here, `[?match 12 [case [< 13] "small"] [else "big"]]` is still
   refused (CXER0100, "expected pattern head"), so that one is still
   load-bearing. ]

[; cd-match-close — find_matching_close: index of the closing bracket of
   bracket opened at $start, string-literal aware; -1 when unbalanced. ]
[?def cd-match-close pure [returns int] ($s::string $start::int)
  [$cd-mc $s $start 0 ""]]

[?def cd-next-struct pure [returns int] ($s::string $i::int)
  [$cd-minp [$cd-minp [$str-find-from $s "[" $i] [$str-find-from $s "]" $i]]
            [$cd-minp [$str-find-from $s "'" $i] [$str-find-from $s "\"" $i]]]]

[?def cd-mc pure [returns int] ($s::string $i::int $depth::int $q::string)
  [?if [>= $i [$str-length $s]]
    [then -1]
    [else [?if [not [= $q ""]]
      [then
        [?let [= $p [$str-find-from $s $q $i]]
          [?if [< $p 0]
            [then -1]
            [else [?if [= [$cd-at $s [- $p 1]] "\\"]
              [then [$cd-mc $s [+ $p 1] $depth $q]]
              [else [$cd-mc $s [+ $p 1] $depth ""]]]]]]]
      [else
        [?let [= $p [$cd-next-struct $s $i]]
          [?if [< $p 0]
            [then -1]
            [else
              [?let [= $ch [$str-at $s $p]]
                [?if [= $ch "["]
                  [then [$cd-mc $s [+ $p 1] [+ $depth 1] ""]]
                  [else [?if [= $ch "]"]
                    [then [?if [= $depth 1]
                      [then $p]
                      [else [$cd-mc $s [+ $p 1] [- $depth 1] ""]]]]
                    [else [$cd-mc $s [+ $p 1] $depth $ch]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[; cd-patch-match-arms — patch_match_arms: rewrite call/element-shaped
   `[case [< 13] B]` arm patterns into quoted-string arms so the source
   parses at all (still load-bearing at this head — DRW3-2). ]
[?def cd-patch-match-arms pure [returns string] ($s::string)
  [?if [not [$str-contains $s "[?match"]] [then $s] [else [$cd-pma $s 0 "" ""]]]]

[?def cd-next-quote-or-match pure [returns int] ($s::string $i::int)
  [$cd-minp [$cd-minp [$str-find-from $s "'" $i] [$str-find-from $s "\"" $i]]
            [$str-find-from $s "[?match" $i]]]

[?def cd-pma pure [returns string] ($s::string $i::int $q::string $acc::string)
  [?let [= $len [$str-length $s]]
    [?if [>= $i $len]
      [then $acc]
      [else [?if [not [= $q ""]]
        [then
          [?let [= $p [$str-find-from $s $q $i]]
            [?if [< $p 0]
              [then [$concat $acc [$str-slice $s $i $len]]]
              [else
                [?let [= $acc2 [$concat $acc [$str-slice $s $i [+ $p 1]]]]
                  [?if [= [$cd-at $s [- $p 1]] "\\"]
                    [then [$cd-pma $s [+ $p 1] $q $acc2]]
                    [else [$cd-pma $s [+ $p 1] "" $acc2]]]]]]]]
        [else
          [?let [= $p [$cd-next-quote-or-match $s $i]]
            [?if [< $p 0]
              [then [$concat $acc [$str-slice $s $i $len]]]
              [else
                [?let
                  [= $ch [$str-at $s $p]]
                  [= $acc2 [$concat $acc [$str-slice $s $i $p]]]
                  [?if [not [= $ch "["]]
                    [then [$cd-pma $s [+ $p 1] $ch [$concat $acc2 $ch]]]
                    [else
                      [?let [= $nxt [$cd-at $s [+ $p 7]]]
                        [?if [$cd-ident-ch $nxt]
                          [then [$cd-pma $s [+ $p 1] "" [$concat $acc2 "["]]]
                          [else
                            [?let [= $end [$cd-match-close $s $p]]
                              [?if [<= $end 0]
                                [then [$cd-pma $s [+ $p 1] "" [$concat $acc2 "["]]]
                                [else
                                  [?let [= $inner [$str-slice $s [+ $p 7] $end]]
                                    [$cd-pma $s [+ $end 1] ""
                                      [$concat $acc2 "[?match" [$cd-rewrite-inner $inner 0 "" ""] "]"]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[; cd-rewrite-inner — rewrite_match_inner: normalise `[case …]` /
   `[else …]` (and the retired `[:case …]` spelling) arms; quote a
   bracket-shaped case pattern. A non-keyword open advances ONE character,
   so a `[case …]` nested inside another element is still reached. ]
[?def cd-rewrite-inner pure [returns string] ($s::string $i::int $q::string $acc::string)
  [?let [= $len [$str-length $s]]
    [?if [>= $i $len]
      [then $acc]
      [else [?if [not [= $q ""]]
        [then
          [?let [= $p [$str-find-from $s $q $i]]
            [?if [< $p 0]
              [then [$concat $acc [$str-slice $s $i $len]]]
              [else
                [?let [= $acc2 [$concat $acc [$str-slice $s $i [+ $p 1]]]]
                  [?if [= [$cd-at $s [- $p 1]] "\\"]
                    [then [$cd-rewrite-inner $s [+ $p 1] $q $acc2]]
                    [else [$cd-rewrite-inner $s [+ $p 1] "" $acc2]]]]]]]]
        [else
          [?let [= $p [$cd-minp [$cd-minp [$str-find-from $s "'" $i]
                                          [$str-find-from $s "\"" $i]]
                                [$str-find-from $s "[" $i]]]
            [?if [< $p 0]
              [then [$concat $acc [$str-slice $s $i $len]]]
              [else
                [?let
                  [= $ch [$str-at $s $p]]
                  [= $acc2 [$concat $acc [$str-slice $s $i $p]]]
                  [?if [not [= $ch "["]]
                    [then [$cd-rewrite-inner $s [+ $p 1] $ch [$concat $acc2 $ch]]]
                    [else
                      [?let
                        [= $kwstart [?if [= [$cd-at $s [+ $p 1]] ":"] [then [+ $p 2]] [else [+ $p 1]]]]
                        [= $kwend [$cd-ident-end $s $kwstart]]
                        [= $kw [?if [> $kwend $kwstart] [then [$str-slice $s $kwstart $kwend]] [else ""]]]
                        [?if [not [or [= $kw "case"] [= $kw "else"]]]
                          [then [$cd-rewrite-inner $s [+ $p 1] "" [$concat $acc2 "["]]]
                          [else
                            [?let [= $end [$cd-match-close $s $p]]
                              [?if [<= $end 0]
                                [then [$cd-rewrite-inner $s [+ $p 1] "" [$concat $acc2 "["]]]
                                [else
                                  [?let [= $body [$str-trim [$str-slice $s $kwend $end]]]
                                    [?if [= $kw "case"]
                                      [then
                                        [?let
                                          [= $sp [$cd-split-head $body 0 0 ""]]
                                          [= $val [?if [< $sp 0] [then $body] [else [$str-slice $body 0 $sp]]]]
                                          [= $rest [?if [< $sp 0] [then ""]
                                            [else [$str-trim [$str-slice $body $sp [$str-length $body]]]]]]
                                          [= $vsafe [?if [and [>= [$str-length $val] 2]
                                                              [and [$str-starts-with $val "["]
                                                                   [$str-ends-with $val "]"]]]
                                            [then [$concat "'" [$str-slice $val 1 [- [$str-length $val] 1]] "'"]]
                                            [else $val]]]
                                          [$cd-rewrite-inner $s [+ $end 1] ""
                                            [$concat $acc2 "[case " $vsafe
                                              [?if [> [$str-length $rest] 0] [then [$concat " " $rest]] [else ""]]
                                              "]"]]]]
                                      [else
                                        [$cd-rewrite-inner $s [+ $end 1] ""
                                          [$concat $acc2 "[else"
                                            [?if [> [$str-length $body] 0] [then [$concat " " $body]] [else ""]]
                                            "]"]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-ident-end pure [returns int] ($s::string $j::int)
  [?if [$cd-ident-ch [$cd-at $s $j]]
    [then [$cd-ident-end $s [+ $j 1]]]
    [else $j]]]

[; cd-split-head — split_case_head: index of the first TOP-LEVEL
   whitespace (depth 0 over []/()/{} and string literals); -1 when the
   whole body is the pattern. ]
[?def cd-split-head pure [returns int] ($s::string $i::int $depth::int $q::string)
  [?if [>= $i [$str-length $s]]
    [then -1]
    [else
      [?let [= $c [$str-at $s $i]]
        [?if [not [= $q ""]]
          [then [?if [and [= $c $q] [not [= [$cd-at $s [- $i 1]] "\\"]]]
            [then [$cd-split-head $s [+ $i 1] $depth ""]]
            [else [$cd-split-head $s [+ $i 1] $depth $q]]]]
          [else [?if [or [= $c "'"] [= $c "\""]]
            [then [$cd-split-head $s [+ $i 1] $depth $c]]
            [else [?if [$str-contains "[({" $c]
              [then [$cd-split-head $s [+ $i 1] [+ $depth 1] ""]]
              [else [?if [$str-contains "])}" $c]
                [then [$cd-split-head $s [+ $i 1] [- $depth 1] ""]]
                [else [?if [and [= $depth 0] [$str-contains " \t\n" $c]]
                  [then $i]
                  [else [$cd-split-head $s [+ $i 1] $depth ""]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-patch-source pure [returns string] ($s::string)
  [$cd-patch-match-arms $s]]

[; ── §9.2 image readers + the auto-detect classification ──────────────
   The `"code"` image (DRW3-3/DRW3-4). Every child of an element is an
   element: directives carry `cx-node="directive"`, for-comprehensions
   `cx-node="for-comp"`, labeled slots ride as single-child `cx:LABEL`
   wraps, positional slots ride as the lowered value itself. ]

[?def cd-node-kind pure [returns string] ($n::any)
  [?if [$exists $n@cx-node] [then [$string $n@cx-node]] [else ""]]]

[?def cd-is-directive pure [returns bool] ($n::any)
  [= [$cd-node-kind $n] "directive"]]

[?def cd-is-forcomp pure [returns bool] ($n::any)
  [= [$cd-node-kind $n] "for-comp"]]

[; cd-labeled — is this child a labeled-slot wrapper? (cx:-local, no
   node mark, not a value tag, exactly one element child — the C8
   reading rule, sharpened by the wave-2 `cx-node` mark.) ]
[?def cd-labeled pure [returns bool] ($k::any)
  [?if [not [$is-cx $k]]
    [then false]
    [else [?if [not [= [$cd-node-kind $k] ""]]
      [then false]
      [else [?if [$value-tag [$local-of $k]]
        [then false]
        [else [= [$count $k/*] 1]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-slot-value pure [returns any] ($k::any)
  [?if [$cd-labeled $k]
    [then [$first [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]]
    [else $k]]]

[; cd-slots — every slot VALUE of a directive, in source order (the V
   `for slot in d.slots` walk). ]
[?def cd-slots pure [returns any] ($d::any)
  [?for [in $k $d/*] [yield [$cd-slot-value $k]]]]

[; cd-lab-of — the labeled slot named $l (single-child wrap), or (). ]
[?def cd-lab-of pure [returns any] ($d::any $l::string)
  [?let [= $tag [$concat "cx:" $l]]
    [$first [?for [in $k $d/*]
      [where [?if [= [$name $k] $tag] [then [$cd-labeled $k]] [else false]]]
      [yield [hit [?splice [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]]]]]]]

[; cd-stmts — top-level statements (top_level_statements). ]
[?def cd-stmts pure [returns any] ($img::any)
  [?if [= [$name $img] "cx:block"]
    [then [?for [in $k $img/*] [where [= [$name $k] "item"]]
      [yield [$first [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]]]]
    [else [?for [in $k ($img)] [yield $k]]]]]

[?def cd-in-list pure [returns bool] ($x::string $xs::any)
  [$exists [$first [?for [in $y $xs] [where [= $y $x]] [yield 1]]]]]

[; cd-is-data-stmt — is_data_statement: a plain data element or scalar
   literal (blocks, decimals, bigints, periods and node literals are
   NOT — the V match's `else` arm). ]
[?def cd-is-data-stmt pure [returns bool] ($n::any)
  [?if [not [= [$cd-node-kind $n] ""]]
    [then false]
    [else [?if [not [$is-cx $n]]
      [then true]
      [else [$cd-in-list [$local-of $n]
        ("int", "float", "bool", "str", "dur", "date", "datetime", "atom",
         "arr", "map", "seq", "op")]]]]]]

[?def cd-seq-trigger pure [returns bool] ($nm::string)
  [$exists [$first [?for [in $r [$code-rules]/*]
    [where [?if [= [$name $r] "trigger"] [then [= [$string $r@directive] $nm]] [else false]]]
    [yield 1]]]]]

[; cd-node-is-trigger — node_is_sequence_trigger: a trigger directive,
   a `[?let]` whose SLOT VALUES carry one, or a block containing one.
   (A `[= $ch [?channel …]]` clause-child does NOT qualify — the V walk
   does not descend into element items; the blind spot is preserved.) ]
[?def cd-node-is-trigger pure [returns bool] ($n::any)
  [?if [$cd-is-directive $n]
    [then
      [?let [= $l [$local-of $n]]
        [?if [$cd-seq-trigger $l]
          [then true]
          [else [?if [= $l "let"]
            [then [$exists [$first [?for [in $v [$cd-slots $n]]
              [where [$cd-node-is-trigger $v]] [yield 1]]]]]
            [else false]]]]]]
    [else [?if [= [$name $n] "cx:block"]
      [then [$exists [$first [?for [in $k $n/*]
        [where [$cd-node-is-trigger [$cd-block-item $k]]] [yield 1]]]]]
      [else false]]]]]

[?def cd-block-item pure [returns any] ($k::any)
  [?if [= [$name $k] "item"]
    [then [$first [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]]
    [else $k]]]

[?def cd-program-is-sequence pure [returns bool] ($img::any)
  [$exists [$first [?for [in $s [$cd-stmts $img]]
    [where [$cd-node-is-trigger $s]] [yield 1]]]]]

[?def cd-program-is-code pure [returns bool] ($img::any)
  [$exists [$first [?for [in $s [$cd-stmts $img]]
    [where [or [$cd-is-directive $s] [$cd-is-forcomp $s]]] [yield 1]]]]]

[; ── §9.2b the text-level fallbacks (parse failure) ───────────────────
   text_level_is_code / text_level_is_sequence_shape: scan TOP-LEVEL
   bracketed chunks and read the directive head name. ]
[?def cd-top-heads pure [returns element] ($s::string)
  [$cd-heads-loop $s 0 [heads]]]

[?def cd-heads-loop pure [returns element] ($s::string $i::int $acc::element)
  [?let [= $p [$str-find-from $s "[" $i]]
    [?if [< $p 0]
      [then $acc]
      [else
        [?let [= $end [$cd-match-close $s $p]]
          [?if [<= $end 0]
            [then $acc]
            [else
              [?let
                [= $head [?if [= [$cd-at $s [+ $p 1]] "?"]
                  [then [$str-slice $s [+ $p 2] [$cd-ident-end $s [+ $p 2]]]]
                  [else ""]]]
                [$cd-heads-loop $s [+ $end 1]
                  [?if [= $head ""]
                    [then $acc]
                    [else [heads [?splice [?for [in $h $acc/*] [yield $h]]] [h v=$head]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-text-is-code pure [returns bool] ($s::string)
  [$exists [$first [?for [in $h [$cd-top-heads $s]/*]
    [where [not [= [$string $h@v] "cx"]]] [yield 1]]]]]

[?def cd-text-is-sequence pure [returns bool] ($s::string)
  [$exists [$first [?for [in $h [$cd-top-heads $s]/*]
    [where [$cd-seq-trigger [$string $h@v]]] [yield 1]]]]]

[; ── §9.3 short_label (the shared node → one-line label) ──────────────
   The V twin renders a node's SOURCE SHAPE, not the reference
   renderer's expression label: strings keep their quotes, elements
   collapse to `[NAME items…]` (attributes and slots excluded), every
   other literal kind is `<lit>`. ]
[?def cd-label pure [returns string] ($n::any)
  [?if [?if [$is-cx $n] [then false] [else [= [$name $n] "cd-synth-block"]]]
    [then "<lit>"]
    [else [$cd-label2 $n]]]]

[; cd-synth-block is the multi-item clause body the V twin built as a
   block LITERAL (`clause_body`), which labels `<lit>` and composes into
   a basic block. It cannot be spelled `cx:block` here: authoring a
   `cx:`-prefixed element is refused (E210). ]
[?def cd-label2 pure [returns string] ($n::any)
  [?if [$cd-is-forcomp $n]
    [then "[?for]"]
    [else [?if [$cd-is-directive $n]
      [then [$concat "[?" [$local-of $n] "]"]]
      [else [?if [not [$is-cx $n]]
        [then [$cd-element-label $n]]
        [else
          [?let [= $l [$local-of $n]]
            [?if [= $l "str"] [then [$concat "'" [$string $n] "'"]]
            [else [?if [$cd-in-list $l ("int", "float", "bool", "dur",
                                        "decimal", "bigint", "date", "datetime", "period")]
              [; the verbatim-carrier scalars print their own image — the
                 graph showed `@ <lit>` for a decimal beside `@ -5` for an
                 int (playground report 2026-08-22), which read as a gap,
                 not a summary. ]
              [then [$string $n]]
            [else [?if [= $l "map"] [then [$cd-map-label $n]]
            [else [?if [= $l "atom"] [then [$concat ":" [$string $n]]]
            [else [?if [= $l "var"] [then [$cd-var-label $n]]
            [else [?if [= $l "call"] [then [$cd-call-label $n]]
            [else [?if [= $l "op"] [then [$cd-element-label $n]]
            [else [?if [= $l "pattern"] [then [$concat "[" [$string $n@value] "]"]]
            [else [?if [= $l "slice-access"]
              [then [$concat [$cd-label [$first [?for [in $k $n/*] [yield $k]]]] "[…]"]]
            [else [?if [= $l "slice"] [then "[slice]"]
            [else [?if [= $l "wildcard"]
              [then [?if [$exists $n@deep] [then "**"] [else "*"]]]
            [else [?if [= $l "path"] [then [$cd-path-label $n]]
            [else [?if [= $l "expr"] [then [$string $n]]
            [else "<lit>"]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[; cd-map-label — a map value's inline image: `{k: v, …}` capped at
   three entries (the graph is a summary, not the document; playground
   report 2026-08-22 — maps drew as `<lit>` / one collapsed node). A
   declaration-only entry shows its declared kind (`k: ::T`, MSS-4). ]
[?def cd-map-label pure [returns string] ($n::any)
  [?let
    [= $es [$cd-map-entries-of $n]]
    [= $cap [?if [> [$count $es] 3] [then 3] [else [$count $es]]]]
    [$concat "{" [$cd-map-entries $es 1 $cap ""]
      [?if [> [$count $es] 3] [then ", …"] [else ""]] "}"]]]

[?def cd-map-entries-of pure [returns any] ($n::any)
  [?for [in $e $n/*] [where [= [$name $e] "entry"]] [yield $e]]]

[?def cd-map-entries pure [returns string] ($es::any $i::int $cap::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i $cap]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $e [$nth $es $i]]
        [= $lbl [?if [$exists $e@decl]
          [then [$concat [$string $e@key] ": ::" [$string $e@decl]]]
          [else [$concat [$string $e@key] ": "
            [$cd-label [$first [?for [in $v $e/*] [yield $v]]]]]]]]
        [$cd-map-entries $es [+ $i 1] $cap
          [?if [= $acc ""] [then $lbl] [else [$concat $acc ", " $lbl]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-ismap pure [returns bool] ($n::any)
  [?if [not [$is-cx $n]] [then false] [else [= [$local-of $n] "map"]]]]

[; cd-path-label — render_path_or_fallback over the DRW3-6 structural
   path node: the leading marker plus the step NAMES joined by `/`
   (axes and predicates are NOT part of this label). ]
[?def cd-path-label pure [returns string] ($n::any)
  [?let
    [= $lead [?if [= [$string $n@leading] "absolute"] [then "/"]
      [else [?if [= [$string $n@leading] "descendant"] [then "//"] [else ""]]]]]
    [= $steps [?for [in $k $n/*] [where [= [$name $k] "cx:pstep"]] [yield [$string $k@name]]]]
    [$concat $lead [$cd-path-steps $steps 1 ""]]]]

[?def cd-path-steps pure [returns string] ($steps::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $steps]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$cd-path-steps $steps [+ $i 1]
      [?if [= $acc ""] [then [$nth $steps $i]] [else [$concat $acc "/" [$nth $steps $i]]]]]]]]

[; cd-src-name — the SOURCE name of an element image node, the one a
   label shows. An operator element recovers its symbol from the §4
   `cx:op` name. An element the image RENAMED (`[err …]`, which the
   evaluator would otherwise treat as an error VALUE — #898 / DRW3-9,
   RULED: ISW-1) carries its source name on `@cx-renamed-from`, which a
   source element cannot forge: source attributes become `cx:attr`
   CHILDREN in this projection, so a lifted element has none of its own.
   Everything else is its own tag. ]
[?def cd-src-name pure [returns string] ($n::any)
  [?if [$is-cx $n]
    [then [$op-symbol [$string $n@name]]]
    [else [?if [$exists $n@cx-renamed-from]
      [then [$string $n@cx-renamed-from]]
      [else [$name $n]]]]]]

[; cd-element-label — `[NAME item …]`: attribute and slot wrappers are
   NOT items (the V twin walks `lit.items` only). An operator element
   recovers its symbol from the §4 `cx:op` name. ]
[?def cd-element-label pure [returns string] ($n::any)
  [?let
    [= $nm [$cd-src-name $n]]
    [= $items [?for [in $k $n/*]
      [where [not [$cd-in-list [$name $k] ("cx:attr", "cx:slot")]]] [yield $k]]]
    [$concat "[" $nm [$cd-label-items $items 1 ""] "]"]]]

[?def cd-label-items pure [returns string] ($items::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $items]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$cd-label-items $items [+ $i 1]
      [$concat $acc " " [$cd-label [$nth $items $i]]]]]]]

[; cd-var-label — `$name` + compact path steps + one `[…]` per
   predicate (the V twin ignores kind-tests and uses the step name). ]
[?def cd-var-label pure [returns string] ($n::any)
  [?let
    [= $nm [?if [$exists $n@name] [then [$string $n@name]] [else [$string $n]]]]
    [= $steps [?for [in $k $n/*] [where [= [$name $k] "cx:step"]] [yield $k]]]
    [$concat "$" $nm [$cd-var-steps $steps 1 ""]]]]

[?def cd-var-steps pure [returns string] ($steps::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $steps]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $st [$nth $steps $i]]
        [= $kind [$string $st@kind]]
        [= $nt [$string $st@name]]
        [= $part
          [?if [= $kind "child"] [then [$concat "/" $nt]]
          [else [?if [= $kind "attr"] [then [$concat "@" $nt]]
          [else [?if [= $kind "member"] [then [$concat "." $nt]]
          [else [?if [= $kind "wildcard_children"] [then "/*"]
          [else [?if [= $kind "descendant"] [then [$concat "//" $nt]]
          [else [?if [= $kind "descendant_wildcard"] [then "//*"]
          [else [?if [= $kind "parent"] [then "/.."]
          [else ""]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]
        [= $preds [$cd-preds [$count [?for [in $p $st/*] [where [= [$name $p] "cx:pred"]] [yield $p]]] ""]]
        [$cd-var-steps $steps [+ $i 1] [$concat $acc $part $preds]]]]]]

[?def cd-preds pure [returns string] ($n::int $acc::string)
  [?if [<= $n 0] [then $acc] [else [$cd-preds [- $n 1] [$concat $acc "[…]"]]]]]

[; cd-call-label — `[fn arg …]`: labeled args unwrap, path steps are
   not arguments. ]
[?def cd-call-label pure [returns string] ($n::any)
  [?let
    [= $args [?for [in $k $n/*] [where [not [= [$name $k] "cx:step"]]]
      [yield [?if [= [$name $k] "cx:arg"]
        [then [$first [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]]
        [else $k]]]]]
    [$concat "[" [$string $n@fn] [$cd-label-items $args 1 ""] "]"]]]

[; cd-esc — mermaid_escape (the V twin's per-character escape; the same
   set as §2's `esc`). ]
[?def cd-esc pure [returns string] ($s::string) [$esc $s]]

[; cd-sanitize-id — sanitize_id: Mermaid-safe node-id suffix. ]
[?def cd-sanitize-id pure [returns string] ($s::string)
  [?let [= $out [$cd-sanitize-loop $s 0 ""]]
    [?if [or [= $out ""] [$str-contains "0123456789" [$cd-at $out 0]]]
      [then [$concat "_" $out]]
      [else $out]]]]

[?def cd-sanitize-loop pure [returns string] ($s::string $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [>= $i [$str-length $s]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $c [$str-at $s $i]]
        [$cd-sanitize-loop $s [+ $i 1]
          [$concat $acc [?if [$str-contains
            "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789_" $c]
            [then $c] [else "_"]]]]]]]]

[; ── §9.4 ERD (erDiagram) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
   §D3 containment inference: multiple same-named children → `||--o{`,
   singleton → `||--||`; entity boxes list attribute rows (carrying the
   CX `@` sigil in the one Mermaid comment a row admits) first and
   scalar child rows second. ]

[; cd-erd-entity — walk_entity's admission: a cx-element literal with a
   name (an operator element counts — its name is the symbol). ]
[?def cd-erd-entity pure [returns bool] ($n::any)
  [?if [not [= [$cd-node-kind $n] ""]]
    [then false]
    [else [?if [not [$is-cx $n]]
      [then [not [= [$name $n] ""]]]
      [else [= [$local-of $n] "op"]]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-name pure [returns string] ($n::any)
  [$cd-src-name $n]]

[; cd-erd-quote — erd_entity_name: bare when Mermaid ATTRIBUTE_WORD
   accepts it, quote-wrapped (with inner quotes and backslashes escaped)
   otherwise. ]
[?def cd-erd-quote pure [returns string] ($raw::string)
  [?if [= $raw ""]
    [then "\"_\""]
    [else [?if [$cd-erd-bare $raw 0]
      [then $raw]
      [else [$concat "\"" [$cd-erd-esc $raw 0 ""] "\""]]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-bare pure [returns bool] ($s::string $i::int)
  [?if [>= $i [$str-length $s]]
    [then true]
    [else
      [?let [= $c [$str-at $s $i]]
        [?if [= $i 0]
          [then [?if [$str-contains "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ_" $c]
            [then [$cd-erd-bare $s [+ $i 1]]] [else false]]]
          [else [?if [$cd-ident-ch $c]
            [then [$cd-erd-bare $s [+ $i 1]]] [else false]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-esc pure [returns string] ($s::string $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [>= $i [$str-length $s]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $c [$str-at $s $i]]
        [$cd-erd-esc $s [+ $i 1] [$concat $acc
          [?if [= $c "\""] [then "\\\""]
            [else [?if [= $c "\\"] [then "\\\\"] [else $c]]]]]]]]]]

[; cd-erd-kids — an element's ITEM children (attribute and slot wraps
   excluded), which is what `lit.items` means in the V walk. ]
[?def cd-erd-kids pure [returns any] ($n::any)
  [?for [in $k $n/*] [where [not [$cd-in-list [$name $k] ("cx:attr", "cx:slot")]]] [yield $k]]]

[?def cd-erd-attrs pure [returns any] ($n::any)
  [?for [in $k $n/*] [where [= [$name $k] "cx:attr"]] [yield $k]]]

[?def cd-erd-slots pure [returns any] ($n::any)
  [?for [in $k $n/*] [where [= [$name $k] "cx:slot"]] [yield $k]]]

[; cd-erd-scalar — is_scalar_child: no attributes, no slots, exactly one
   item, and that item a string/int/float/bool/atom literal. ]
[?def cd-erd-scalar pure [returns bool] ($c::any)
  [?if [> [$count [$cd-erd-attrs $c]] 0]
    [then false]
    [else [?if [> [$count [$cd-erd-slots $c]] 0]
      [then false]
      [else
        [?let [= $items [$cd-erd-kids $c]]
          [?if [not [= [$count $items] 1]]
            [then false]
            [else
              [?let [= $it [$first $items]]
                [?if [not [= [$cd-node-kind $it] ""]]
                  [then false]
                  [else [?if [not [$is-cx $it]]
                    [then false]
                    [else [$cd-in-list [$local-of $it] ("str", "int", "float", "bool", "atom")]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[; cd-erd-type — scalar_type_str: the ERD row's leading type token. ]
[?def cd-erd-type pure [returns string] ($n::any)
  [?if [not [$is-cx $n]]
    [then "string"]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $l [$local-of $n]]
        [= $hit [$first [?for [in $r [$code-rules]/*]
          [where [?if [= [$name $r] "erd-type"] [then [= [$string $r@kind] $l]] [else false]]]
          [yield [$string $r@type]]]]]
        [?if [$exists $hit] [then $hit] [else "string"]]]]]]

[; ── the ERD accumulator (ERDState) ──
   [erd [ents [ent name=… [rows [row t=… n=… a=…]…] [mx [c n=… v=…]…]]…]
        [rels [rel p=… c=… card=…]…]]  — order IS document order. ]
[?def cd-erd-empty pure [returns element] () [erd [ents] [rels]]]

[?def cd-erd-has pure [returns bool] ($st::element $nm::string)
  [$exists [$first [?for [in $e $st/ents/*] [where [= [$string $e@name] $nm]] [yield 1]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-ensure pure [returns element] ($st::element $nm::string)
  [?if [$cd-erd-has $st $nm]
    [then $st]
    [else
      [erd [ents [?splice [?for [in $e $st/ents/*] [yield $e]]] [ent name=$nm [rows] [mx]]]
           [rels [?splice [?for [in $r $st/rels/*] [yield $r]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-row-seen pure [returns bool] ($st::element $nm::string $key::string)
  [$exists [$first [?for [in $e $st/ents/*] [in $r $e/rows/*]
    [where [and [= [$string $e@name] $nm] [= [$string $r@k] $key]]]
    [yield 1]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-add-row pure [returns element] ($st::element $nm::string $key::string
                                             $t::string $n::string $a::bool)
  [?if [$cd-erd-row-seen $st $nm $key]
    [then $st]
    [else
      [erd
        [ents [?splice [?for [in $e $st/ents/*]
          [yield [?if [= [$string $e@name] $nm]
            [then [ent name=[$string $e@name]
              [rows [?splice [?for [in $r $e/rows/*] [yield $r]]] [row k=$key t=$t n=$n a=$a]]
              [mx [?splice [?for [in $c $e/mx/*] [yield $c]]]]]]
            [else $e]]]]]]
        [rels [?splice [?for [in $r $st/rels/*] [yield $r]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-maxchild pure [returns int] ($st::element $nm::string $cname::string)
  [?let [= $hits [?for [in $e $st/ents/*] [in $c $e/mx/*]
      [where [and [= [$string $e@name] $nm] [= [$string $c@n] $cname]]]
      [yield $c@v]]]
    [?if [= [$count $hits] 0] [then 0] [else [$first $hits]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-set-maxchild pure [returns element] ($st::element $nm::string $cname::string $v::int)
  [erd
    [ents [?splice [?for [in $e $st/ents/*]
      [yield [?if [= [$string $e@name] $nm]
        [then [ent name=[$string $e@name]
          [rows [?splice [?for [in $r $e/rows/*] [yield $r]]]]
          [mx [?splice [?for [in $c $e/mx/*] [where [not [= [$string $c@n] $cname]]] [yield $c]]]
              [c n=$cname v=$v]]]]
        [else $e]]]]]]
    [rels [?splice [?for [in $r $st/rels/*] [yield $r]]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-rel-card pure [returns string] ($st::element $p::string $c::string)
  [?let [= $hits [?for [in $r $st/rels/*]
      [where [?if [= [$string $r@p] $p] [then [= [$string $r@c] $c]] [else false]]]
      [yield [$string $r@card]]]]
    [?if [= [$count $hits] 0] [then ""] [else [$first $hits]]]]]

[; cd-erd-set-rel — first insertion appends (fixing the emit order);
   a later differing cardinality REPLACES in place. ]
[?def cd-erd-set-rel pure [returns element] ($st::element $p::string $c::string $card::string)
  [?if [= [$cd-erd-rel-card $st $p $c] ""]
    [then
      [erd [ents [?splice [?for [in $e $st/ents/*] [yield $e]]]]
           [rels [?splice [?for [in $r $st/rels/*] [yield $r]]] [rel p=$p c=$c card=$card]]]]
    [else
      [erd [ents [?splice [?for [in $e $st/ents/*] [yield $e]]]]
           [rels [?splice [?for [in $r $st/rels/*]
             [yield [?if [?if [= [$string $r@p] $p] [then [= [$string $r@c] $c]] [else false]]
               [then [rel p=$p c=$c card=$card]]
               [else $r]]]]]]]]]]

[; cd-erd-walk — walk_entity, in document order. ]
[?def cd-erd-walk pure [returns element] ($n::any $st::element)
  [?if [$cd-erd-ismap $n]
    [; a BARE map document is the `map` entity — before this the ERD of
       `{name: 'Alice', …}` came out EMPTY (playground report). ]
    [then [$cd-erd-map-rows [$cd-map-entries-of $n] 1 "map"
      [$cd-erd-ensure $st "map"]]]
  [else [?if [not [$cd-erd-entity $n]]
    [then $st]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $nm [$cd-erd-name $n]]
        [= $st1 [$cd-erd-ensure $st $nm]]
        [= $st2 [$cd-erd-walk-attrs [$cd-erd-attrs $n] 1 $nm $st1]]
        [= $st2b [$cd-erd-walk-cols [$cd-table-cols $n] 1 $nm $st2]]
        [= $st3 [$cd-erd-walk-items [$cd-erd-kids $n] 1 $nm $st2b]]
        [$cd-erd-walk-counts [$cd-erd-counts [$cd-erd-kids $n] 1 [counts]] 1 $nm $st3]]]]]]]

[; cd-erd-walk-cols — RULED: TI-1 (#914), render rule 1. A
   table-carrying element is an entity whose FIELDS are its COLUMNS,
   each typed by its DECLARED column type (the image spells the
   `::string` default explicitly, so there is no default to re-derive
   here). This is the mapping an erDiagram wants, and it is precisely
   what the lane never saw: the table element used to reach the walk as
   the `cx:data` source-text hatch, so the ERD came out empty. Column
   rows sit between the attribute rows and the scalar-child rows, in
   declaration order; the `a` flag is false — a column is not an
   attribute and carries no `@` sigil. ]
[?def cd-erd-walk-cols pure [returns element] ($cols::any $i::int $nm::string $st::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $cols]]
    [then $st]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $c [$nth $cols $i]]
        [= $cn [$string $c@name]]
        [$cd-erd-walk-cols $cols [+ $i 1] $nm
          [$cd-erd-add-row $st $nm $cn [$string $c@type] $cn false]]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-walk-attrs pure [returns element] ($attrs::any $i::int $nm::string $st::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $attrs]]
    [then $st]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $a [$nth $attrs $i]]
        [= $an [$string $a@name]]
        [= $av [$first [?for [in $v $a/*] [yield $v]]]]
        [$cd-erd-walk-attrs $attrs [+ $i 1] $nm
          [$cd-erd-add-row $st $nm [$concat "@" $an] [$cd-erd-type $av] $an true]]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-walk-items pure [returns element] ($items::any $i::int $nm::string $st::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $items]]
    [then $st]
    [else
      [?let [= $it [$nth $items $i]]
        [?if [$cd-erd-ismap $it]
          [; a MAP child contributes its ENTRIES as rows of the parent
             entity — `.key`-deduped, typed by the value's kind, value
             filled at full detail exactly like an attribute row
             (playground report 2026-08-22: maps were invisible in the
             ERD; a declared entry rows as its declared kind). ]
          [then [$cd-erd-walk-items $items [+ $i 1] $nm
            [$cd-erd-map-rows [$cd-map-entries-of $it] 1 $nm $st]]]
        [else [?if [not [$cd-erd-entity $it]]
          [then [$cd-erd-walk-items $items [+ $i 1] $nm $st]]
          [else [?if [$cd-erd-scalar $it]
            [then
              [?let
                [= $cn [$cd-erd-name $it]]
                [= $val [$first [$cd-erd-kids $it]]]
                [$cd-erd-walk-items $items [+ $i 1] $nm
                  [$cd-erd-add-row $st $nm $cn [$cd-erd-type $val] $cn false]]]]
            [else [$cd-erd-walk-items $items [+ $i 1] $nm [$cd-erd-walk $it $st]]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-map-rows pure [returns element] ($es::any $i::int $nm::string $st::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $es]]
    [then $st]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $e [$nth $es $i]]
        [= $k [$string $e@key]]
        [?if [$exists $e@decl]
          [then [$cd-erd-map-rows $es [+ $i 1] $nm
            [$cd-erd-add-row $st $nm [$concat "." $k] [$string $e@decl] $k false]]]
          [else
            [?let [= $v [$first [?for [in $x $e/*] [yield $x]]]]
              [$cd-erd-map-rows $es [+ $i 1] $nm
                [$cd-erd-add-row $st $nm [$concat "." $k] [$cd-erd-type $v] $k true]]]]]]]]]

[; cd-erd-counts — per-instance child-name counts for the non-scalar
   children, in first-appearance order (V's insertion-ordered map). ]
[?def cd-erd-counts pure [returns element] ($items::any $i::int $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $items]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $it [$nth $items $i]]
        [?if [not [$cd-erd-entity $it]]
          [then [$cd-erd-counts $items [+ $i 1] $acc]]
          [else [?if [$cd-erd-scalar $it]
            [then [$cd-erd-counts $items [+ $i 1] $acc]]
            [else
              [?let [= $cn [$cd-erd-name $it]]
                [$cd-erd-counts $items [+ $i 1] [$cd-count-bump $acc $cn]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-count-bump pure [returns element] ($acc::element $nm::string)
  [?if [$exists [$first [?for [in $c $acc/*] [where [= [$string $c@n] $nm]] [yield 1]]]]
    [then [counts [?splice [?for [in $c $acc/*]
      [yield [?if [= [$string $c@n] $nm]
        [then [c n=$nm v=[+ $c@v 1]]]
        [else $c]]]]]]]
    [else [counts [?splice [?for [in $c $acc/*] [yield $c]]] [c n=$nm v=1]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-walk-counts pure [returns element] ($counts::element $i::int $nm::string $st::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $counts/*]]
    [then $st]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $c [$nth [?for [in $x $counts/*] [yield $x]] $i]]
        [= $cn [$string $c@n]]
        [= $cv $c@v]
        [= $prev [$cd-erd-maxchild $st $nm $cn]]
        [= $newmax [?if [> $cv $prev] [then $cv] [else $prev]]]
        [= $card [?if [>= $newmax 2] [then "||--o{"] [else "||--||"]]]
        [$cd-erd-walk-counts $counts [+ $i 1] $nm
          [$cd-erd-set-rel [$cd-erd-set-maxchild $st $nm $cn $newmax] $nm $cn $card]]]]]]

[; cd-erd — code_diagram_erd (compact). ]
[?def cd-erd pure [returns string] ($img::any)
  [?let
    [= $st [$cd-erd-top [$cd-stmts $img] 1 [$cd-erd-empty]]]
    [= $rels [$cd-erd-rel-lines [?for [in $r $st/rels/*] [yield $r]] 1 ""]]
    [= $ents [$cd-erd-ent-lines [?for [in $e $st/ents/*] [yield $e]] 1 ""]]
    [$jn3 "erDiagram" $rels $ents]]]

[?def cd-erd-top pure [returns element] ($stmts::any $i::int $st::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $stmts]]
    [then $st]
    [else [$cd-erd-top $stmts [+ $i 1] [$cd-erd-walk [$nth $stmts $i] $st]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-rel-lines pure [returns string] ($rels::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $rels]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $r [$nth $rels $i]]
        [$cd-erd-rel-lines $rels [+ $i 1]
          [$jn $acc [$concat "  " [$cd-erd-quote [$string $r@p]] " " [$string $r@card]
                              " " [$cd-erd-quote [$string $r@c]] " : has"]]]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-ent-lines pure [returns string] ($ents::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ents]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $e [$nth $ents $i]]
        [= $rows [$cd-erd-row-lines [?for [in $r $e/rows/*] [yield $r]] 1 ""]]
        [$cd-erd-ent-lines $ents [+ $i 1]
          [$jn3 $acc [$jn [$concat "  " [$cd-erd-quote [$string $e@name]] " {"] $rows] "  }"]]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-row-lines pure [returns string] ($rows::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $rows]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $r [$nth $rows $i]]
        [$cd-erd-row-lines $rows [+ $i 1]
          [$jn $acc [$concat "    " [$string $r@t] " " [$string $r@n]
            [?if [= [$string $r@a] "true"] [then " \"@\""] [else ""]]]]]]]]]

[; cd-erd-min — code_diagram_erd_min: one empty box per top-level
   element name and per direct child element name, deduped. ]
[?def cd-erd-min pure [returns string] ($img::any)
  [?let [= $names [$cd-erd-min-names [$cd-stmts $img] 1 [names]]]
    [$jn "erDiagram" [$cd-erd-min-lines [?for [in $n $names/*] [yield [$string $n@v]]] 1 ""]]]]

[?def cd-erd-min-names pure [returns element] ($stmts::any $i::int $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $stmts]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $s [$nth $stmts $i]]
        [?if [not [$cd-erd-entity $s]]
          [then [$cd-erd-min-names $stmts [+ $i 1] $acc]]
          [else
            [?let
              [= $a1 [$cd-name-add $acc [$cd-erd-name $s]]]
              [= $a2 [$cd-erd-min-kids [$cd-erd-kids $s] 1 $a1]]
              [$cd-erd-min-names $stmts [+ $i 1] $a2]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-min-kids pure [returns element] ($kids::any $i::int $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $kids]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $k [$nth $kids $i]]
        [?if [$cd-erd-entity $k]
          [then [$cd-erd-min-kids $kids [+ $i 1] [$cd-name-add $acc [$cd-erd-name $k]]]]
          [else [$cd-erd-min-kids $kids [+ $i 1] $acc]]]]]]]

[?def cd-name-add pure [returns element] ($acc::element $nm::string)
  [?if [= $nm ""]
    [then $acc]
    [else [?if [$exists [$first [?for [in $n $acc/*] [where [= [$string $n@v] $nm]] [yield 1]]]]
      [then $acc]
      [else [names [?splice [?for [in $n $acc/*] [yield $n]]] [n v=$nm]]]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-min-lines pure [returns string] ($names::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $names]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$cd-erd-min-lines $names [+ $i 1]
      [$jn3 $acc [$concat "  " [$cd-erd-quote [$nth $names $i]] " {"] "  }"]]]]]
[; ── §9.5 CFG (flowchart TD) ──────────────────────────────────────────
   §D4 basic blocks: a run of sequential non-branching statements
   composes into one block node (10-line cap with a `(+K more)` row);
   if → diamond, match → dispatcher with one arm edge each, for → loop
   box with a `binds $x` edge, modify → one update block, def → its own
   subgraph. The V emitter mutated one `CFGState`; this threads the
   same fields as a record — out (the joined lines), exit (the current
   scope exit id), pfx (the sub-graph id prefix), arms (the match-arm
   counter), dname / dentry (the enclosing def, for self-recursion
   back-edges) — plus e / x, the entry and exit ids an emitter returns. ]

[?def cst pure [returns map] ($out::string $exit::string $pfx::string $arms::int
                              $dname::string $dentry::string)
  {out: $out, exit: $exit, pfx: $pfx, arms: $arms, dname: $dname, dentry: $dentry,
   e: "", x: ""}]

[?def cst-out pure [returns map] ($s::map $out::string)
  [$cst $out $s.exit $s.pfx $s.arms $s.dname $s.dentry]]

[?def cres pure [returns map] ($s::map $e::string $x::string)
  {out: $s.out, exit: $s.exit, pfx: $s.pfx, arms: $s.arms, dname: $s.dname,
   dentry: $s.dentry, e: $e, x: $x}]

[?def cd-edge pure [returns string] ($from::string $to::string)
  [$concat "  " $from " --> " $to]]

[?def cd-items pure [returns any] ($n::any)
  [?for [in $k $n/*] [where [not [$cd-in-list [$name $k] ("cx:attr", "cx:slot")]]] [yield $k]]]

[?def cd-is-def pure [returns bool] ($n::any)
  [?if [$cd-is-directive $n] [then [= [$local-of $n] "def"]] [else false]]]

[; cd-block-candidate — is_block_candidate. ]
[?def cd-block-candidate pure [returns bool] ($n::any)
  [?if [$cd-is-directive $n]
    [then [not [$code-breaks-block [$local-of $n]]]]
    [else [not [$cd-is-forcomp $n]]]]]

[; cd-block-node — emit_block_node over items[$from..$to]. ]
[?def cd-block-node pure [returns map] ($items::any $from::int $to::int $s::map)
  [?let
    [= $role [?if [$str-ends-with $s.exit "lh"] [then "lb"] [else "b"]]]
    [= $id [$concat $s.pfx $role]]
    [= $label [$cd-esc [$cd-block-label $items $from $to $from ""]]]
    [$cres [$cst-out $s [$jn $s.out [$concat "  " $id "[\"" $label "\"]"]]] $id $id]]]

[?def cd-block-label pure [returns string] ($items::any $from::int $to::int $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i $to]
    [then $acc]
    [else [?if [>= [- $i $from] 10]
      [then [$jn $acc [$str-format "(+{} more)" ([+ [- $to $i] 1])]]]
      [else [$cd-block-label $items $from $to [+ $i 1]
        [$jn $acc [$cd-label [$nth $items $i]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-group-end pure [returns int] ($items::any $i::int)
  [?if [> $i [$count $items]]
    [then $i]
    [else [?if [$cd-block-candidate [$nth $items $i]]
      [then [$cd-group-end $items [+ $i 1]]]
      [else $i]]]]]

[; cd-branching — emit_branching; a non-branching node answers the
   [cd-nobranch] sentinel, which the V twin spelled as an error the
   callers swallowed with `or { … }`. ]
[?def cd-branching pure [returns any] ($n::any $s::map)
  [?if [$cd-is-forcomp $n]
    [then [$cd-emit-for $n $s]]
    [else [?if [not [$cd-is-directive $n]]
      [then [cd-nobranch]]
      [else
        [?let [= $l [$local-of $n]]
          [?if [= $l "if"] [then [$cd-emit-if $n $s]]
          [else [?if [= $l "match"] [then [$cd-emit-match $n $s]]
          [else [?if [= $l "modify"] [then [$cd-emit-modify $n $s]]
          [else [?if [= $l "let"] [then [$cd-emit-let $n $s]]
          [else [cd-nobranch]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-nobranch-p pure [returns bool] ($r::any)
  [?if [$exists $r] [then [= [$name $r] "cd-nobranch"]] [else false]]]

[; cd-emit-let — emit_let: a `[= $x V]` clause-child (which the §4
   image spells `cx:op name="eq"`, exactly as the V AST spelled it a
   cx-element named `=`) is a binding label; every other slot is body. ]
[?def cd-emit-let pure [returns map] ($d::any $s::map)
  [?let
    [= $slots [$cd-slots $d]]
    [= $binds [?for [in $v $slots] [where [$cd-is-eq-clause $v]] [yield $v]]]
    [= $body [?for [in $v $slots] [where [not [$cd-is-eq-clause $v]]] [yield $v]]]
    [= $setup [?if [> [$count $binds] 0] [then [$concat $s.pfx "lt"]] [else ""]]]
    [= $s1 [?if [= $setup ""]
      [then $s]
      [else [$cst-out $s [$jn $s.out
        [$concat "  " $setup "[\"" [$cd-esc [$cd-bind-labels $binds 1 ""]] "\"]"]]]]]]
    [?if [and [= [$count $body] 1] [not [$cd-block-candidate [$first $body]]]]
      [then
        [?let [= $r [$cd-branching [$first $body] $s1]]
          [?if [$cd-nobranch-p $r]
            [then [$cres $s1 $setup $setup]]
            [else [?if [= $setup ""]
              [then [$cres $r $r.e $r.x]]
              [else [$cres [$cst-out $r [$jn $r.out [$cd-edge $setup $r.e]]] $setup $r.x]]]]]]]
      [else [?if [> [$count $body] 0]
        [then
          [?let [= $r [$cd-block-node $body 1 [$count $body] $s1]]
            [?if [= $setup ""]
              [then [$cres $r $r.e $r.e]]
              [else [$cres [$cst-out $r [$jn $r.out [$cd-edge $setup $r.e]]] $setup $r.e]]]]]
        [else [$cres $s1 $setup $setup]]]]]]]

[?def cd-is-eq-clause pure [returns bool] ($v::any)
  [?if [not [$is-cx $v]]
    [then false]
    [else [?if [not [= [$local-of $v] "op"]]
      [then false]
      [else [= [$string $v@name] "eq"]]]]]]

[?def cd-bind-labels pure [returns string] ($binds::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $binds]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$cd-bind-labels $binds [+ $i 1] [$jn $acc [$cd-label [$nth $binds $i]]]]]]]

[; cd-clause-body — clause_body: the single item of a `[then …]` /
   `[else …]` / `[case …]` clause-child, a synthetic block for several,
   or () when the clause carries neither items nor slots. ]
[?def cd-clause-body pure [returns any] ($lit::any)
  [?let
    [= $items [$cd-items $lit]]
    [= $slots [?for [in $k $lit/*] [where [= [$name $k] "cx:slot"]] [yield $k]]]
    [?if [and [= [$count $items] 0] [= [$count $slots] 0]]
      [then ()]
      [else [?if [= [$count $items] 1]
        [then [hit [$first $items]]]
        [else [hit [cd-synth-block [?splice [?for [in $it $items] [yield $it]]]]]]]]]]]

[; cd-arm-tail — arm_tail: a self-recursive arm loops back to the
   enclosing def's entry instead of threading through its exit. ]
[?def cd-arm-tail pure [returns string] ($n::any $s::map)
  [?if [= $s.dname ""]
    [then $s.exit]
    [else [?if [$cd-self-call $n $s.dname] [then $s.dentry] [else $s.exit]]]]]

[?def cd-self-call pure [returns bool] ($n::any $dname::string)
  [?if [$exists $n]
    [then [?if [$is-cx $n]
      [then [?if [= [$local-of $n] "call"] [then [= [$string $n@fn] $dname]] [else false]]]
      [else [= [$name $n] $dname]]]]
    [else false]]]

[; cd-emit-if — emit_if. ]
[?def cd-emit-if pure [returns map] ($d::any $s::map)
  [?let
    [= $id [$concat $s.pfx "i"]]
    [= $cond [$cd-if-cond [$cd-kids-of $d] 1 ""]]
    [= $then [$cd-if-arm $d "then"]]
    [= $else [$cd-if-arm $d "else"]]
    [= $lbl [?if [= $cond ""] [then "if"] [else [$concat "if " $cond]]]]
    [= $s1 [$cst-out $s [$jn $s.out [$concat "  " $id "{\"" [$cd-esc $lbl] "\"}"]]]]
    [= $s2 [?if [$exists $then]
      [then [$cd-if-arm-emit $s1 $id [$lab-val $then] "t" "true"]]
      [else $s1]]]
    [= $s3 [?if [$exists $else]
      [then [$cd-if-arm-emit $s2 $id [$lab-val $else]
        [?if [= $s.pfx ""] [then "e"] [else "r"]] "false"]]
      [else $s2]]]
    [$cres $s3 $id $s3.exit]]]

[?def cd-if-arm-emit pure [returns map] ($s::map $id::string $body::any
                                         $role::string $edge::string)
  [?let
    [= $aid [$concat $s.pfx $role]]
    [= $s1 [$cst-out $s [$jn $s.out [$concat "  " $aid "[\"" [$cd-label $body] "\"]"]]]]
    [= $s2 [$cst-out $s1 [$jn $s1.out
      [$concat "  " $id " -- \"" $edge "\" --> " $aid]]]]
    [$cst-out $s2 [$jn $s2.out [$cd-edge $aid [$cd-arm-tail $body $s2]]]]]]

[; cd-if-cond — the first positional that is not a then/else
   clause-child. ]
[?def cd-if-cond pure [returns string] ($ks::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [?if [not [= $acc ""]]
      [then $acc]
      [else
        [?let [= $k [$nth $ks $i]]
          [?if [$cd-labeled $k]
            [then [$cd-if-cond $ks [+ $i 1] $acc]]
            [else [?if [$cd-in-list [$name $k] ("then", "else")]
              [then [$cd-if-cond $ks [+ $i 1] $acc]]
              [else [$cd-if-cond $ks [+ $i 1] [$cd-label $k]]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-kids-of pure [returns any] ($d::any)
  [?for [in $k $d/*] [yield $k]]]

[; cd-if-arm — the then/else branch body: a labeled slot wins, else a
   positional `[then …]` / `[else …]` clause-child's body. ]
[?def cd-if-arm pure [returns any] ($d::any $which::string)
  [?let [= $lab [$cd-lab-of $d $which]]
    [?if [$exists $lab]
      [then $lab]
      [else
        [?let [= $cl [$first [?for [in $k $d/*]
            [where [?if [$cd-labeled $k] [then false] [else [= [$name $k] $which]]]]
            [yield [hit $k]]]]]
          [?if [not [$exists $cl]]
            [then ()]
            [else [$cd-clause-body [$lab-val $cl]]]]]]]]]

[; cd-emit-match — emit_match: the case / else / yield labeled-slot
   state machine, in child order. ]
[?def cd-emit-match pure [returns map] ($d::any $s::map)
  [?let
    [= $id [$concat $s.pfx "m"]]
    [= $subj [$cd-match-subj [$cd-kids-of $d] 1 ""]]
    [= $arms [$cd-match-arms2 [$cd-kids-of $d] 1 () false [arms]]]
    [= $lbl [?if [= $subj ""] [then "match"] [else [$concat "match " $subj]]]]
    [= $s1 [$cst-out $s [$jn $s.out [$concat "  " $id "{\"" [$cd-esc $lbl] "\"}"]]]]
    [= $s2 [$cd-match-emit [?for [in $a $arms/*] [yield $a]] 1 $id $s1]]
    [$cres $s2 $id $s2.exit]]]

[?def cd-match-subj pure [returns string] ($ks::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [?if [not [= $acc ""]]
      [then $acc]
      [else
        [?let [= $k [$nth $ks $i]]
          [?if [$cd-labeled $k]
            [then [$cd-match-subj $ks [+ $i 1] $acc]]
            [else [$cd-match-subj $ks [+ $i 1] [$cd-label $k]]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-match-arms2 pure [returns element] ($ks::any $i::int $pending::any
                                             $pending-else::bool $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $k [$nth $ks $i]]
        [?if [not [$cd-labeled $k]]
          [then [$cd-match-arms2 $ks [+ $i 1] $pending $pending-else $acc]]
          [else
            [?let [= $l [$local-of $k]] [= $v [$cd-slot-value $k]]
              [?if [= $l "case"]
                [then [$cd-match-arms2 $ks [+ $i 1] [hit $v] false $acc]]
                [else [?if [= $l "else"]
                  [then [$cd-match-arms2 $ks [+ $i 1] () true $acc]]
                  [else [?if [not [= $l "yield"]]
                    [then [$cd-match-arms2 $ks [+ $i 1] $pending $pending-else $acc]]
                    [else [?if $pending-else
                      [then [$cd-match-arms2 $ks [+ $i 1] () false
                        [arms [?splice [?for [in $a $acc/*] [yield $a]]]
                              [arm label="else" $v]]]]
                      [else [?if [not [$exists $pending]]
                        [then [$cd-match-arms2 $ks [+ $i 1] $pending $pending-else $acc]]
                        [else [$cd-match-arms2 $ks [+ $i 1] () false
                          [arms [?splice [?for [in $a $acc/*] [yield $a]]]
                                [arm label=[$cd-arm-pattern-label [$lab-val $pending]] $v]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[; cd-arm-pattern-label — arm_pattern_label: a string-shaped pattern
   reads as its bare text, truncated at 30 characters with an ellipsis. ]
[?def cd-arm-pattern-label pure [returns string] ($n::any)
  [?let
    [= $raw [?if [$is-cx $n]
      [then [?if [= [$local-of $n] "str"] [then [$string $n]] [else [$cd-label $n]]]]
      [else [$cd-label $n]]]]
    [?if [<= [$str-length $raw] 30]
      [then $raw]
      [else [$concat [$str-slice $raw 0 30] "…"]]]]]

[?def cd-match-emit pure [returns map] ($arms::any $i::int $id::string $s::map)
  [?if [> $i [$count $arms]]
    [then $s]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $arm [$nth $arms $i]]
        [= $n [+ $s.arms 1]]
        [= $role [?if [= $s.pfx ""] [then [$str-format "a{}" ($n)]] [else [$str-format "t{}" ($n)]]]]
        [= $aid [$concat $s.pfx $role]]
        [= $body [$first [?for [in $b $arm/*] [yield $b]]]]
        [= $out [$jn4 $s.out
          [$concat "  " $aid "[\"" [$cd-esc [$cd-label $body]] "\"]"]
          [$concat "  " $id " -- \"" [$cd-esc [$string $arm@label]] "\" --> " $aid]
          [$cd-edge $aid $s.exit]]]
        [$cd-match-emit $arms [+ $i 1] $id
          [$cst $out $s.exit $s.pfx $n $s.dname $s.dentry]]]]]]

[; cd-emit-for — emit_for: the loop box, its `binds $x` edge, and the
   body emitted with the loop header standing in as the scope exit. ]
[?def cd-emit-for pure [returns map] ($f::any $s::map)
  [?let
    [= $lh [$concat $s.pfx "lh"]]
    [= $gen [$first [?for [in $c $f/*]
      [where [?if [= [$name $c] "cx:clause"] [then [= [$string $c@kind] "generator"]] [else false]]]
      [yield [hit $c]]]]]
    [= $bind [?if [$exists $gen]
      [then [?if [$exists [$lab-val $gen]@bind] [then [$string [$lab-val $gen]@bind]] [else ""]]]
      [else ""]]]
    [= $srcw [?if [$exists $gen]
      [then [$first [?for [in $x [$lab-val $gen]/*] [where [= [$name $x] "cx:source"]]
        [yield [hit [$first [?for [in $v $x/*] [yield $v]]]]]]]]
      [else ()]]]
    [= $srclabel [?if [$exists $srcw] [then [$cd-label [$lab-val $srcw]]] [else ""]]]
    [= $header [?if [= $bind ""]
      [then "for"]
      [else [?if [= $srclabel ""]
        [then [$concat "for $" $bind]]
        [else [$concat "for $" $bind " :in " $srclabel]]]]]]
    [= $s1 [$cst-out $s [$jn $s.out [$concat "  " $lh "{{\"" [$cd-esc $header] "\"}}"]]]]
    [= $yield [$first [?for [in $k $f/*] [where [= [$name $k] "cx:yield"]]
      [yield [hit [$first [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]]]]]]
    [= $inner [$cst $s1.out $lh $s1.pfx $s1.arms $s1.dname $s1.dentry]]
    [= $rb [$cd-emit-body [$lab-val $yield] $inner]]
    [= $s2 [$cst $rb.out $s.exit $s.pfx $rb.arms $s.dname $s.dentry]]
    [$cres [$cst-out $s2 [$jn $s2.out
      [?if [= $bind ""]
        [then [$cd-edge $lh $rb.e]]
        [else [$concat "  " $lh " -- \"binds $" $bind "\" --> " $rb.e]]]]] $lh $lh]]]

[; cd-emit-body — emit_body: one basic block (with the back-edge to the
   loop header) or the nested branching shape. ]
[?def cd-emit-body pure [returns map] ($n::any $s::map)
  [?if [$cd-block-candidate $n]
    [then
      [?let [= $r [$cd-block-node ($n) 1 1 $s]]
        [$cres [$cst-out $r [$jn $r.out [$cd-edge $r.e $r.exit]]] $r.e $r.e]]]
    [else
      [?let [= $r [$cd-branching $n $s]]
        [?if [$cd-nobranch-p $r]
          [then
            [?let [= $b [$cd-block-node ($n) 1 1 $s]]
              [$cres [$cst-out $b [$jn $b.out [$cd-edge $b.e $b.exit]]] $b.e $b.e]]]
          [else [$cres $r $r.e $r.e]]]]]]]

[; cd-emit-modify — emit_modify: `modify @ FOCUS | action | …`. ]
[?def cd-emit-modify pure [returns map] ($d::any $s::map)
  [?let
    [= $id [$concat $s.pfx "u"]]
    [= $focus [$cd-modify-focus [$cd-kids-of $d] 1 ""]]
    [= $acts [$cd-modify-actions [$cd-kids-of $d] 1 ""]]
    [= $label [$concat "modify @ " $focus $acts]]
    [$cres [$cst-out $s [$jn $s.out
      [$concat "  " $id "[\"" [$cd-esc $label] "\"]"]]] $id $id]]]

[?def cd-modify-focus pure [returns string] ($ks::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $k [$nth $ks $i]]
        [?if [$cd-labeled $k]
          [then [$cd-modify-focus $ks [+ $i 1] $acc]]
          [else [$cd-modify-focus $ks [+ $i 1] [$cd-label $k]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-modify-actions pure [returns string] ($ks::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $k [$nth $ks $i]]
        [?if [$cd-labeled $k]
          [then [$cd-modify-actions $ks [+ $i 1] [$concat $acc " | " [$local-of $k]]]]
          [else [$cd-modify-actions $ks [+ $i 1] $acc]]]]]]]

[; cd-def-subgraph — emit_def_subgraph: `subgraph NAME … end` with a
   trapezoid entry and a stadium exit, in its own id scope. ]
[?def cd-def-subgraph pure [returns map] ($d::any $s::map)
  [?let
    [= $nb [$cd-def-name-body $d]]
    [?if [= [$name $nb] "err"]
      [then $nb]
      [else
        [?let
          [= $nm [$string $nb@name]]
          [= $body [$first [?for [in $b $nb/*] [yield $b]]]]
          [= $pfx [?if [> [$str-length $nm] 0] [then [$str-lower [$str-slice $nm 0 1]]] [else "x"]]]
          [= $entry [$concat $pfx "s"]]
          [= $exit [$concat $pfx "e"]]
          [= $s1 [$cst [$jn3 $s.out
                    [$concat "  subgraph " $nm]
                    [$concat "    " $entry "[/\"def " $nm "\"/]"]]
                  $exit $pfx 0 $nm $entry]]
          [= $s2 [$cst-out $s1 [$jn $s1.out [$concat "    " $exit "([exit])"]]]]
          [= $s3 [?if [$cd-block-candidate $body]
            [then [$cd-def-block $body $entry $exit $pfx $s2]]
            [else
              [?let [= $r [$cd-branching $body $s2]]
                [?if [$cd-nobranch-p $r]
                  [then [$cd-def-block $body $entry $exit $pfx $s2]]
                  [else [$cst-out $r [$jn $r.out [$cd-edge $entry $r.e]]]]]]]]]
          [$cst [$jn $s3.out "  end"] $s.exit $s.pfx $s.arms $s.dname $s.dentry]]]]]]

[?def cd-def-block pure [returns map] ($body::any $entry::string $exit::string
                                       $pfx::string $s::map)
  [?let [= $gid [$concat $pfx "b"]]
    [$cst-out $s [$jn4 $s.out
      [$concat "    " $gid "[\"" [$cd-esc [$cd-label $body]] "\"]"]
      [$cd-edge $entry $gid]
      [$cd-edge $gid $exit]]]]]

[; cd-def-name-body — def_name_and_body over the DRW3-4 `cx:def-image`
   (or, for a synthetic directive with no deferred source, the legacy
   positional / labeled shapes the V twin also accepted). ]
[?def cd-def-name-body pure [returns element] ($d::any)
  [?let [= $img [$first [?for [in $k $d/*] [where [= [$name $k] "cx:def-image"]] [yield $k]]]]
    [?if [not [$exists $img]]
      [then [$cd-def-legacy $d]]
      [else [?if [$exists $img@error]
        [then [err code='cx-err:CXER0100' message=[$string $img@error]]]
        [else [?if [$exists $img@absent]
          [then [$cd-def-legacy $d]]
          [else [def-nb name=[$string $img@name]
            [?splice [?for [in $b $img/*] [yield $b]]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-def-legacy pure [returns element] ($d::any)
  [?let
    [= $pos [?for [in $k $d/*] [where [not [$cd-labeled $k]]] [yield $k]]]
    [= $lname [$cd-lab-of $d "name"]]
    [= $lbody [$cd-lab-of $d "body"]]
    [= $nm0 [?if [$exists $lname] [then [$cd-def-legacy-name [$lab-val $lname]]] [else ""]]]
    [= $nm [?if [not [= $nm0 ""]]
      [then $nm0]
      [else [?if [= [$count $pos] 0]
        [then ""]
        [else [$cd-def-legacy-name [$first $pos]]]]]]]
    [= $body [?if [$exists $lbody]
      [then [hit [$lab-val $lbody]]]
      [else [?if [= [$count $pos] 1]
        [then [$cd-def-legacy-single [$first $pos]]]
        [else [?if [>= [$count $pos] 2]
          [then [hit [$nth $pos [$count $pos]]]]
          [else ()]]]]]]]
    [?if [not [$exists $body]]
      [then [err code='cx-err:CXER0100' message='[?def] missing body']]
      [else [def-nb name=[?if [= $nm ""] [then "anon"] [else $nm]]
        [?splice [?for [in $b ([$lab-val $body])] [yield $b]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-def-legacy-name pure [returns string] ($v::any)
  [?if [not [$exists $v]]
    [then ""]
    [else [?if [$is-cx $v]
      [then [?if [= [$local-of $v] "call"]
        [then [$string $v@fn]]
        [else [?if [= [$local-of $v] "str"] [then [$string $v]] [else ""]]]]]
      [else [$name $v]]]]]]

[?def cd-def-legacy-single pure [returns any] ($v::any)
  [?if [$is-cx $v]
    [then [hit $v]]
    [else
      [?let [= $items [$cd-items $v]]
        [?if [> [$count $items] 0]
          [then [hit [$nth $items [$count $items]]]]
          [else ()]]]]]]

[; cd-cfg — code_diagram_cfg (compact). ]
[?def cd-cfg pure [returns any] ($img::any)
  [?let
    [= $stmts [$cd-stmts $img]]
    [= $s1 [$cd-cfg-defs $stmts 1 [$cst "flowchart TD" "" "" 0 "" ""]]]
    [= $main [?for [in $x $stmts]
      [where [?if [$cd-is-def $x] [then false] [else [not [$cd-is-data-stmt $x]]]]]
      [yield $x]]]
    [?if [= [$count $main] 0]
      [then $s1.out]
      [else
        [?let
          [= $s2 [$cst [$jn3 $s1.out "  start([entry])" "  done([exit])"] "done" "" $s1.arms "" ""]]
          [= $s3 [$cd-cfg-main $main 1 "start" $s2]]
          [?if [= $s3.e $s3.exit]
            [then $s3.out]
            [else [$jn $s3.out [$cd-edge $s3.e $s3.exit]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-cfg-defs pure [returns map] ($stmts::any $i::int $s::map)
  [?if [> $i [$count $stmts]]
    [then $s]
    [else
      [?let [= $st [$nth $stmts $i]]
        [?if [$cd-is-def $st]
          [then [$cd-cfg-defs $stmts [+ $i 1] [$cd-def-subgraph $st $s]]]
          [else [$cd-cfg-defs $stmts [+ $i 1] $s]]]]]]]

[?def cd-cfg-main pure [returns map] ($main::any $i::int $prev::string $s::map)
  [?if [> $i [$count $main]]
    [then [$cres $s $prev ""]]
    [else
      [?let [= $st [$nth $main $i]]
        [?if [$cd-block-candidate $st]
          [then
            [?let
              [= $j [$cd-group-end $main $i]]
              [= $r [$cd-block-node $main $i [- $j 1] $s]]
              [$cd-cfg-main $main $j $r.e [$cst-out $r [$jn $r.out [$cd-edge $prev $r.e]]]]]]
          [else
            [?let [= $r [$cd-branching $st $s]]
              [$cd-cfg-main $main [+ $i 1] $r.x
                [$cst-out $r [$jn $r.out [$cd-edge $prev $r.e]]]]]]]]]]]

[; cd-cfg-min — code_diagram_cfg_min: one box per top-level def plus a
   `main` box with dashed call edges. ]
[?def cd-cfg-min pure [returns any] ($img::any)
  [?let
    [= $stmts [$cd-stmts $img]]
    [= $names [$cd-min-def-names $stmts 1 [names]]]
    [= $have-main [$exists [$first [?for [in $x $stmts]
      [where [?if [$cd-is-def $x] [then false]
        [else [or [$cd-is-directive $x] [or [$cd-is-forcomp $x] [$cd-is-call $x]]]]]]
      [yield 1]]]]]
    [= $boxes [$cd-min-def-lines [?for [in $n $names/*] [yield [$string $n@v]]] 1 ""]]
    [?if [not $have-main]
      [then [$jn "flowchart TD" $boxes]]
      [else [$jn3 [$jn "flowchart TD" $boxes] "  main[\"main\"]"
        [$cd-min-call-lines [?for [in $n $names/*] [yield [$string $n@v]]] 1 ""]]]]]]

[?def cd-is-call pure [returns bool] ($n::any)
  [?if [$is-cx $n] [then [= [$local-of $n] "call"]] [else false]]]

[?def cd-min-def-names pure [returns element] ($stmts::any $i::int $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $stmts]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $st [$nth $stmts $i]]
        [?if [not [$cd-is-def $st]]
          [then [$cd-min-def-names $stmts [+ $i 1] $acc]]
          [else
            [?let [= $nm [$cd-def-name-min $st]]
              [?if [= $nm ""]
                [then [$cd-min-def-names $stmts [+ $i 1] $acc]]
                [else [$cd-min-def-names $stmts [+ $i 1]
                  [names [?splice [?for [in $n $acc/*] [yield $n]]] [n v=$nm]]]]]]]]]]]]

[; cd-def-name-min — def_name_min_extract. ]
[?def cd-def-name-min pure [returns string] ($d::any)
  [?let [= $nb [$cd-def-name-body $d]]
    [?if [not [= [$name $nb] "err"]]
      [then [$string $nb@name]]
      [else [$cd-def-name-scan [$cd-kids-of $d] 1]]]]]

[?def cd-def-name-scan pure [returns string] ($ks::any $i::int)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then ""]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $k [$nth $ks $i]]
        [= $v [$cd-slot-value $k]]
        [= $nm [?if [?if [$cd-labeled $k] [then [= [$local-of $k] "name"]] [else false]]
          [then [$cd-def-legacy-name $v]]
          [else [$cd-def-elem-name $v]]]]
        [?if [= $nm ""]
          [then [$cd-def-name-scan $ks [+ $i 1]]]
          [else $nm]]]]]]

[?def cd-def-elem-name pure [returns string] ($v::any)
  [?if [$is-cx $v]
    [then [?if [= [$local-of $v] "call"] [then [$string $v@fn]] [else ""]]]
    [else [$name $v]]]]

[?def cd-min-def-lines pure [returns string] ($names::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $names]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$cd-min-def-lines $names [+ $i 1]
      [$jn $acc [$str-format "  def_{}[\"def {}\"]" ([$nth $names $i], [$nth $names $i])]]]]]]

[?def cd-min-call-lines pure [returns string] ($names::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $names]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$cd-min-call-lines $names [+ $i 1]
      [$jn $acc [$str-format "  main -.->|\"call\"| def_{}" ([$nth $names $i])]]]]]]

[; ── §9.5b CFG `full` (code_diagram_cfg_full) ─────────────────────────
   Compact's envelope plus the twelve colour classes, the INPUT/OUTPUT
   terminals, cross-def dashed call edges, yield sentinels, and the
   binding-introduction circles with their `resolves` edges. Layered
   over the compact TEXT exactly as the V emitter layered it. ]

[?def cd-classdefs pure [returns string] ()
  [$concat
    "  classDef input fill:#e0f7fa,stroke:#006064;\n"
    "  classDef output fill:#fff3e0,stroke:#e65100;\n"
    "  classDef callsite fill:#f3e5f5,stroke:#4a148c;\n"
    "  classDef cond fill:#fff9c4,stroke:#f57f17;\n"
    "  classDef loop fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#1b5e20;\n"
    "  classDef lit fill:#eceff1,stroke:#37474f;\n"
    "  classDef binding fill:#ede7f6,stroke:#311b92;\n"
    "  classDef param fill:#e1f5fe,stroke:#01579b;\n"
    "  classDef path fill:#e0f2f1,stroke:#004d40;\n"
    "  classDef yield fill:#fce4ec,stroke:#880e4f;\n"
    "  classDef accessor fill:#f1f8e9,stroke:#33691e;\n"
    "  classDef exit fill:#fafafa,stroke:#212121;"]]

[?def cd-lines-from pure [returns string] ($lines::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $lines]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$cd-lines-from $lines [+ $i 1] [$jn $acc [$nth $lines $i]]]]]]

[?def cd-cfg-full pure [returns any] ($img::any)
  [?let
    [= $compact [$cd-cfg $img]]
    [= $lines [$str-split-lines $compact]]
    [= $stmts [$cd-stmts $img]]
    [= $names [?for [in $n [$cd-min-def-names $stmts 1 [names]]/*] [yield [$string $n@v]]]]
    [= $out1 [$jn4 [$nth $lines 1] [$cd-classdefs]
      [$jn "  input([INPUT]):::input" "  output([OUTPUT]):::output"]
      [$cd-lines-from $lines 2 ""]]]
    [= $out2 [?if [$str-contains $compact "start([entry])"]
      [then [$jn $out1 "  input --> start"]] [else $out1]]]
    [= $out3 [?if [$str-contains $compact "done([exit])"]
      [then [$jn $out2 "  done --> output"]] [else $out2]]]
    [= $out4 [$cd-call-edges $stmts 1 $names $out3]]
    [= $out5 [$cd-yield-lines $stmts 1 0 $out4]]
    [= $target [$cd-resolve-target $out5 $names]]
    [$cd-binding-lines [$cd-binding-intros $img] 1 $target $out5]]]

[?def cd-def-entry-id pure [returns string] ($nm::string)
  [$concat [$str-lower [$str-slice $nm 0 1]] "s"]]

[?def cd-call-edges pure [returns string] ($stmts::any $i::int $names::any $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $stmts]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $st [$nth $stmts $i]]
        [?if [not [$cd-is-def $st]]
          [then [$cd-call-edges $stmts [+ $i 1] $names $acc]]
          [else
            [?let [= $nm [$cd-def-name-min $st]]
              [?if [= $nm ""]
                [then [$cd-call-edges $stmts [+ $i 1] $names $acc]]
                [else
                  [?let [= $nb [$cd-def-name-body $st]]
                    [?if [= [$name $nb] "err"]
                      [then [$cd-call-edges $stmts [+ $i 1] $names $acc]]
                      [else
                        [?let
                          [= $body [$first [?for [in $b $nb/*] [yield $b]]]]
                          [= $cs [$cd-callees $body $names $nm [names]]]
                          [$cd-call-edges $stmts [+ $i 1] $names
                            [$cd-call-edge-lines
                              [?for [in $c $cs/*] [yield [$string $c@v]]] 1
                              [$cd-def-entry-id $nm] $acc]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-call-edge-lines pure [returns string] ($cs::any $i::int $from::string $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $cs]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$cd-call-edge-lines $cs [+ $i 1] $from
      [$jn $acc [$concat "  " $from " -. \"call\" .-> " [$cd-def-entry-id [$nth $cs $i]]]]]]]]

[; cd-callees — collect_callees: def names referenced as bare-element
   calls or call nodes inside a def body, first-seen order, the
   enclosing def excluded. ]
[?def cd-callees pure [returns element] ($n::any $names::any $exclude::string $acc::element)
  [?if [not [$exists $n]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [?if [$cd-is-call $n]
      [then [$cd-callee-args [$cd-call-args $n] 1 $names $exclude
        [$cd-callee-add $acc [$string $n@fn] $names $exclude]]]
      [else [?if [$cd-is-directive $n]
        [then [$cd-callee-args [$cd-slots $n] 1 $names $exclude $acc]]
        [else [?if [$cd-is-forcomp $n]
          [then [$cd-callee-args [$cd-forcomp-parts $n] 1 $names $exclude $acc]]
          [else [?if [$cd-is-container $n]
            [then [$cd-callee-args [$cd-container-parts $n] 1 $names $exclude $acc]]
            [else [?if [$cd-is-elem-literal $n]
              [then [$cd-callee-args [$cd-elem-parts $n] 1 $names $exclude
                [$cd-callee-add $acc [$cd-erd-name $n] $names $exclude]]]
              [else $acc]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-callee-add pure [returns element] ($acc::element $nm::string $names::any $exclude::string)
  [?if [= $nm ""]
    [then $acc]
    [else [?if [not [$cd-in-list $nm $names]]
      [then $acc]
      [else [?if [= $nm $exclude]
        [then $acc]
        [else [$cd-name-add $acc $nm]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-callee-args pure [returns element] ($xs::any $i::int $names::any
                                             $exclude::string $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $xs]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$cd-callee-args $xs [+ $i 1] $names $exclude
      [$cd-callees [$nth $xs $i] $names $exclude $acc]]]]]

[?def cd-call-args pure [returns any] ($n::any)
  [?for [in $k $n/*] [where [not [= [$name $k] "cx:step"]]]
    [yield [?if [= [$name $k] "cx:arg"]
      [then [$first [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]]
      [else $k]]]]]

[?def cd-is-elem-literal pure [returns bool] ($n::any)
  [?if [not [= [$cd-node-kind $n] ""]]
    [then false]
    [else [?if [not [$is-cx $n]] [then true] [else [= [$local-of $n] "op"]]]]]]

[?def cd-is-container pure [returns bool] ($n::any)
  [?if [not [= [$cd-node-kind $n] ""]]
    [then false]
    [else [?if [not [$is-cx $n]]
      [then false]
      [else [$cd-in-list [$local-of $n] ("seq", "arr", "block", "map")]]]]]]

[?def cd-container-parts pure [returns any] ($n::any)
  [?for [in $k $n/*] [yield [$first [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]]]]

[?def cd-elem-parts pure [returns any] ($n::any)
  [?for [in $k $n/*] [where [not [= [$name $k] "cx:attr"]]]
    [yield [?if [= [$name $k] "cx:slot"]
      [then [$first [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]]
      [else $k]]]]]

[; cd-forcomp-parts — L100's for-comp children: generator sources,
   clause expressions, the yield and its value. ]
[?def cd-forcomp-parts pure [returns any] ($f::any)
  [?for [in $k $f/*] [in $part [$cd-fc-part-of $k]] [yield $part]]]

[?def cd-fc-part-of pure [returns any] ($k::any)
  [?if [= [$name $k] "cx:clause"]
    [then [?for [in $c $k/*] [yield [$first [?for [in $v $c/*] [yield $v]]]]]]
    [else [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]]]

[; cd-yield-lines — the yield-enumeration sentinels, one per yield site
   found in a top-level for-comprehension's yield body. ]
[?def cd-yield-lines pure [returns string] ($stmts::any $i::int $n::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $stmts]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $st [$nth $stmts $i]]
        [?if [not [$cd-is-forcomp $st]]
          [then [$cd-yield-lines $stmts [+ $i 1] $n $acc]]
          [else
            [?let
              [= $y [$first [?for [in $k $st/*] [where [= [$name $k] "cx:yield"]]
                [yield [hit [$first [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]]]]]]
              [= $c [?if [$exists $y] [then [$cd-yield-count [$lab-val $y]]] [else 0]]]
              [$cd-yield-lines $stmts [+ $i 1] [+ $n $c]
                [$cd-yield-emit $n $c $acc]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-yield-emit pure [returns string] ($base::int $c::int $acc::string)
  [?if [<= $c 0]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $k [+ $base 1]]
        [$cd-yield-emit $k [- $c 1]
          [$jn3 $acc [$str-format "  y{}[\"yield #{}\"]:::yield" ($k, $k)]
                     [$str-format "  lh --> y{}" ($k)]]]]]]]

[; cd-yield-count — walk_yields, counting sites. ]
[?def cd-yield-count pure [returns int] ($n::any)
  [?if [not [$exists $n]]
    [then 0]
    [else [?if [$cd-is-forcomp $n]
      [then 0]
      [else [?if [$cd-is-directive $n]
        [then [$cd-yield-clause-count [$cd-kids-of $n] 1 0]]
        [else [?if [$cd-is-call $n]
          [then 1]
          [else [?if [?if [$is-cx $n] [then false] [else [= [$name $n] "yield"]]]
            [then 1]
            [else [?if [?if [$is-cx $n] [then [= [$local-of $n] "block"]] [else false]]
              [then [$cd-yield-items [$cd-container-parts $n] 1 0]]
              [else [?if [$cd-yield-counts-as-site $n] [then 1] [else 0]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-yield-counts-as-site pure [returns bool] ($n::any)
  [?if [not [$is-cx $n]]
    [then true]
    [else [$cd-in-list [$local-of $n]
      ("str", "int", "float", "bool", "atom", "dur", "date", "datetime",
       "decimal", "bigint", "period", "data", "seq", "arr", "map", "op", "var")]]]]

[?def cd-yield-items pure [returns int] ($xs::any $i::int $acc::int)
  [?if [> $i [$count $xs]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$cd-yield-items $xs [+ $i 1] [+ $acc [$cd-yield-count [$nth $xs $i]]]]]]]

[?def cd-yield-clause-count pure [returns int] ($ks::any $i::int $acc::int)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $v [$cd-slot-value [$nth $ks $i]]]
        [$cd-yield-clause-count $ks [+ $i 1]
          [?if [?if [$is-cx $v] [then false]
                 [else [$cd-in-list [$name $v] ("then", "else", "case")]]]
            [then [+ $acc 1]] [else $acc]]]]]]]

[?def cd-var-name pure [returns string] ($n::any)
  [?if [$exists $n@name] [then [$string $n@name]] [else [$string $n]]]]

[; cd-resolve-target — the heuristic anchor for `resolves` edges:
   the `[?let]` setup node, else the loop body, else the main block,
   else the first def's entry. ]
[?def cd-resolve-target pure [returns string] ($out::string $names::any)
  [?if [or [$str-contains $out "  lt["] [$str-contains $out "  lt{"]]
    [then "lt"]
    [else [?if [or [$str-contains $out "lb["] [$str-contains $out "lb{"]]
      [then "lb"]
      [else [?if [or [$str-contains $out "  b["] [$str-contains $out "  b{"]]
        [then "b"]
        [else [?if [> [$count $names] 0]
          [then [$cd-def-entry-id [$first $names]]]
          [else ""]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-binding-lines pure [returns string] ($bs::any $i::int $target::string $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $bs]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $b [$nth $bs $i]]
        [= $bid [$concat "b_" [$cd-sanitize-id $b]]]
        [= $node [$str-format "  {}(((\"${}\"))):::binding" ($bid, $b)]]
        [$cd-binding-lines $bs [+ $i 1] $target
          [?if [= $target ""]
            [then [$jn $acc $node]]
            [else [$jn3 $acc $node
              [$str-format "  {} -. \"resolves\" .-> {}" ($bid, $target)]]]]]]]]]

[; ── §9.6 SEQ (sequenceDiagram) ───────────────────────────────────────
   code_diagram_seq and its family, ported byte-for-byte. The V emitter
   threads a mutable SeqState; here ONE `[sq …]` record is threaded
   functionally through every emitter:

     out    — the accumulated diagram text (newline-joined lines)
     async  — the anonymous `[?async]` lane counter
     worker — the current worker name during a body walk ("" outside)
     level  — min | compact | full
     parts  — the ordered participant list (also `participant_seen`)
     chans  — the channel-binding → lane-name registry
     acts   — the per-participant activation depth

   Emitters that must return BOTH a string and the advanced state use
   the `[p2 v=… STATE]` pair. ]

[?def cd-sq-mk pure [returns element]
    ($out::string $async::int $worker::string $level::string
     $parts::any $chans::any $acts::any)
  [sq out=$out async=$async worker=$worker level=$level
    [parts [?splice [?for [in $p $parts] [yield $p]]]]
    [chans [?splice [?for [in $c $chans] [yield $c]]]]
    [acts [?splice [?for [in $a $acts] [yield $a]]]]]]

[?def cd-sq-ps pure [returns any] ($s::element) [?for [in $p $s/parts/*] [yield $p]]]
[?def cd-sq-cs pure [returns any] ($s::element) [?for [in $c $s/chans/*] [yield $c]]]
[?def cd-sq-as pure [returns any] ($s::element) [?for [in $a $s/acts/*] [yield $a]]]

[?def cd-sq-out pure [returns string] ($s::element) [$string $s@out]]

[?def cd-sq-line pure [returns element] ($s::element $ln::string)
  [$cd-sq-mk [$concat [$string $s@out] "\n" $ln] $s@async [$string $s@worker]
    [$string $s@level] [$cd-sq-ps $s] [$cd-sq-cs $s] [$cd-sq-as $s]]]

[?def cd-sq-setw pure [returns element] ($s::element $w::string)
  [$cd-sq-mk [$string $s@out] $s@async $w [$string $s@level]
    [$cd-sq-ps $s] [$cd-sq-cs $s] [$cd-sq-as $s]]]

[?def cd-sq-bump pure [returns element] ($s::element)
  [$cd-sq-mk [$string $s@out] [+ $s@async 1] [$string $s@worker] [$string $s@level]
    [$cd-sq-ps $s] [$cd-sq-cs $s] [$cd-sq-as $s]]]

[?def cd-worker-or pure [returns string] ($s::element $dflt::string)
  [?let [= $w [$string $s@worker]]
    [?if [= $w ""] [then $dflt] [else $w]]]]

[; add_participant — declared once, in first-seen order. ]
[?def cd-sq-has pure [returns bool] ($s::element $n::string)
  [$exists [$first [?for [in $p $s/parts/*] [where [= [$string $p@n] $n]] [yield 1]]]]]

[?def cd-sq-part pure [returns element] ($s::element $n::string)
  [?if [= $n ""]
    [then $s]
    [else [?if [$cd-sq-has $s $n]
      [then $s]
      [else
        [?let [= $np [parts [?splice [?for [in $p $s/parts/*] [yield $p]]] [p n=$n]]]
          [$cd-sq-line
            [$cd-sq-mk [$string $s@out] $s@async [$string $s@worker] [$string $s@level]
              [?for [in $x $np/*] [yield $x]] [$cd-sq-cs $s] [$cd-sq-as $s]]
            [$concat "  participant " $n]]]]]]]]

[; the channel-binding → lane registry. ]
[?def cd-sq-chan pure [returns string] ($s::element $k::string)
  [?let [= $h [?for [in $c $s/chans/*] [where [= [$string $c@k] $k]] [yield [$string $c@v]]]]
    [?if [= [$count $h] 0] [then ""] [else [$first $h]]]]]

[?def cd-sq-setchan pure [returns element] ($s::element $k::string $v::string)
  [?let [= $nc [chans
      [?splice [?for [in $c $s/chans/*] [where [not [= [$string $c@k] $k]]] [yield $c]]]
      [c k=$k v=$v]]]
    [$cd-sq-mk [$string $s@out] $s@async [$string $s@worker] [$string $s@level]
      [$cd-sq-ps $s] [?for [in $x $nc/*] [yield $x]] [$cd-sq-as $s]]]]

[; per-participant activation depth. ]
[?def cd-sq-act pure [returns int] ($s::element $n::string)
  [?let [= $h [?for [in $a $s/acts/*] [where [= [$string $a@n] $n]] [yield $a@v]]]
    [?if [= [$count $h] 0] [then 0] [else [$first $h]]]]]

[?def cd-sq-setact pure [returns element] ($s::element $n::string $v::int)
  [?let [= $na [acts
      [?splice [?for [in $a $s/acts/*] [where [not [= [$string $a@n] $n]]] [yield $a]]]
      [a n=$n v=$v]]]
    [$cd-sq-mk [$string $s@out] $s@async [$string $s@worker] [$string $s@level]
      [$cd-sq-ps $s] [$cd-sq-cs $s] [?for [in $x $na/*] [yield $x]]]]]

[; activate_safe / deactivate_safe. ]
[?def cd-sq-activate pure [returns element] ($s::element $n::string)
  [?if [= $n ""]
    [then $s]
    [else [$cd-sq-line [$cd-sq-setact $s $n [+ [$cd-sq-act $s $n] 1]]
      [$concat "  activate " $n]]]]]

[?def cd-sq-deactivate pure [returns element] ($s::element $n::string)
  [?if [= $n ""]
    [then $s]
    [else
      [?let [= $d [$cd-sq-act $s $n]]
        [?if [<= $d 0]
          [then $s]
          [else [$cd-sq-line [$cd-sq-setact $s $n [- $d 1]]
            [$concat "  deactivate " $n]]]]]]]]

[; send_arrow_kind / receive_arrow_kind — split into the arrow SPELLING
   and the activation-depth side effect (both read the pre-arrow depth). ]
[?def cd-sq-sendk pure [returns string] ($s::element $dst::string $dashed::bool)
  [?if [> [$cd-sq-act $s $dst] 0]
    [then [?if $dashed [then "-->>"] [else "->>"]]]
    [else [?if $dashed [then "-->>+"] [else "->>+"]]]]]

[?def cd-sq-sendk-s pure [returns element] ($s::element $dst::string)
  [?let [= $d [$cd-sq-act $s $dst]]
    [?if [> $d 0] [then $s] [else [$cd-sq-setact $s $dst [+ $d 1]]]]]]

[?def cd-sq-recvk pure [returns string] ($s::element $src::string $dashed::bool)
  [?if [> [$cd-sq-act $s $src] 0]
    [then [?if $dashed [then "-->>-"] [else "->>-"]]]
    [else [?if $dashed [then "-->>"] [else "->>"]]]]]

[?def cd-sq-recvk-s pure [returns element] ($s::element $src::string)
  [?let [= $d [$cd-sq-act $s $src]]
    [?if [> $d 0] [then [$cd-sq-setact $s $src [- $d 1]]] [else $s]]]]

[; p2 — the (string, state) pair. ]
[?def cd-p2 pure [returns element] ($v::string $s::element) [p2 v=$v $s]]
[?def cd-p2v pure [returns string] ($r::element) [$string $r@v]]
[?def cd-p2s pure [returns element] ($r::element) [$first [?for [in $x $r/*] [yield $x]]]]

[; ── image readers the SEQ half needs ───────────────────────────────── ]

[; cd-sq-kids / cd-sq-slots — the err-SAFE twins of cd-erd-kids /
   cd-erd-slots. A program image can carry an element literally named
   `err` (a `[err code=…]` handler in a `[?select]` arm is the corpus
   case), and in CX such an element IS an error VALUE: `[$name …]` on
   it — indeed ANY call with it as an operand — propagates. Reading the
   name through an inline `[?else]` keeps the filter honest (an err
   element's name IS "err") without ever handing the value to a call.
   Path navigation and `[?splice]` are safe; the value only becomes
   dangerous as a call operand or a dynamic child. ]
[?def cd-sq-kids pure [returns any] ($n::any)
  [?for [in $k $n/*]
    [where [not [$cd-in-list [?else [$name $k] "err"] ("cx:attr", "cx:slot")]]]
    [yield $k]]]

[?def cd-sq-slots pure [returns any] ($n::any)
  [?for [in $k $n/*] [where [= [?else [$name $k] "err"] "cx:slot"]] [yield $k]]]

[; cd-sq-lbl — the LABEL of a raw directive child, "" for a positional. ]
[?def cd-sq-lbl pure [returns string] ($k::any)
  [?if [$cd-labeled $k] [then [$local-of $k]] [else ""]]]

[; cd-sq-pos — positional slot values, in source order. ]
[?def cd-sq-pos pure [returns any] ($d::any)
  [?for [in $k $d/*] [where [not [$cd-labeled $k]]] [yield $k]]]

[; cd-sq-vals — every slot VALUE in source order (labeled wraps unwrapped). ]
[?def cd-sq-vals pure [returns any] ($d::any)
  [?for [in $k $d/*] [yield [$cd-slot-value $k]]]]

[; cd-el-named — a plain (non-`cx:`) element literal with this name. ]
[?def cd-el-named pure [returns bool] ($n::any $nm::string)
  [?if [$is-cx $n] [then false] [else [= [$name $n] $nm]]]]

[; cd-is-elem-lit — a cx-element LITERAL (a bareword element, or the
   `cx:op` image of an operator element). Directives, for-comps and the
   value tags are not. ]
[?def cd-is-elem-lit pure [returns bool] ($n::any)
  [?if [$is-cx $n]
    [then [= [$local-of $n] "op"]]
    [else [= [$cd-node-kind $n] ""]]]]

[; cd-is-lit — the V `ProgramLiteral` arm: scalars, containers, elements.
   Bindings, calls, patterns, wildcards and slices are NOT literals. ]
[?def cd-is-lit pure [returns bool] ($n::any)
  [?if [not [= [$cd-node-kind $n] ""]]
    [then false]
    [else [?if [not [$is-cx $n]]
      [then true]
      [else [$cd-in-list [$local-of $n]
        ("int", "bigint", "decimal", "float", "bool", "str", "atom", "dur",
         "period", "date", "datetime", "op", "seq", "arr", "map", "block",
         "data")]]]]]]

[; cd-is-dir-named — a directive element with this local name. ]
[?def cd-is-dir-named pure [returns bool] ($n::any $nm::string)
  [?if [$cd-is-directive $n] [then [= [$local-of $n] $nm]] [else false]]]

[; cd-is-var0 — a `$name` binding with an EMPTY path (the image spells
   it as `cx:var` carrying the name as TEXT; a stepped binding carries
   an @name attribute instead). ]
[?def cd-is-var0 pure [returns bool] ($n::any)
  [?if [$is-cx $n]
    [then [?if [= [$local-of $n] "var"] [then [not [$exists $n@name]]] [else false]]]
    [else false]]]

[?def cd-is-str-ne pure [returns bool] ($n::any)
  [?if [$is-cx $n]
    [then [?if [= [$local-of $n] "str"] [then [not [= [$string $n] ""]]] [else false]]]
    [else false]]]

[; cd-is-eq — the `[= $x V]` clause-child: an operator element whose
   symbol is `=`. ]
[?def cd-is-eq pure [returns bool] ($n::any)
  [?if [$is-cx $n]
    [then [?if [= [$local-of $n] "op"]
      [then [= [$op-symbol [$string $n@name]] "="]]
      [else false]]]
    [else false]]]

[; let_binding_name — the `$name` on the LHS of a `[= $name V]`. ]
[?def cd-let-bind pure [returns string] ($n::any)
  [?if [$cd-is-var0 $n] [then [$string $n]] [else ""]]]

[; cd-var-name — a binding's name from either spelling. ]

[; directive_name_attr — the `name=` labeled slot's string value, else
   the first positional string / call name, else the default. ]
[?def cd-nameattr pure [returns string] ($d::any $dflt::string)
  [$cd-nameattr-loop [?for [in $k $d/*] [yield $k]] 1 $dflt]]

[?def cd-nameattr-loop pure [returns string] ($ks::any $i::int $dflt::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then $dflt]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $k [$nth $ks $i]]
        [= $hit [?if [$cd-labeled $k]
          [then [?if [= [$name $k] "cx:name"]
            [then [$cd-nameattr-val [$cd-slot-value $k] false]]
            [else ""]]]
          [else [$cd-nameattr-val $k true]]]]
        [?if [= $hit ""]
          [then [$cd-nameattr-loop $ks [+ $i 1] $dflt]]
          [else $hit]]]]]]

[?def cd-nameattr-val pure [returns string] ($v::any $pos::bool)
  [?if [not [$is-cx $v]]
    [then ""]
    [else
      [?let [= $l [$local-of $v]]
        [?if [= $l "str"] [then [$string $v]]
        [else [?if [= $l "call"] [then [$string $v@fn]]
        [else [?if [= $l "var"]
          [then [?if $pos [then ""] [else [$cd-var-name $v]]]]
          [else ""]]]]]]]]]]

[; seq_directive_body — labeled `body=`, else a positional `[body …]`
   clause-child, else the LAST positional slot value. ]
[?def cd-seq-bodyof pure [returns any] ($d::any)
  [?let [= $lb [$cd-lab-of $d "body"]]
    [?if [$exists $lb]
      [then $lb]
      [else
        [?let [= $bel [$first [?for [in $v [$cd-sq-pos $d]]
            [where [$cd-el-named $v "body"]] [yield $v]]]]
          [?if [$exists $bel]
            [then [hit [$cd-body-node $bel]]]
            [else
              [?let [= $ps [$cd-sq-pos $d]]
                [?if [= [$count $ps] 0]
                  [then ()]
                  [else [hit [$nth $ps [$count $ps]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[; a multi-item `[body A B]` collapses to a block; `cd-block` is the
   image-shaped twin of a `.block` literal (same `item` children). ]
[?def cd-body-node pure [returns any] ($bel::any)
  [?let [= $its [$cd-sq-kids $bel]]
    [?if [= [$count $its] 1]
      [then [$first $its]]
      [else [cd-block [?splice [?for [in $it $its] [yield [item $it]]]]]]]]]

[; channel_lane_for. ]
[?def cd-chan-lane pure [returns element] ($n::any $s::element)
  [?if [$cd-is-var0 $n]
    [then
      [?let
        [= $nm [$string $n]]
        [= $lane [$cd-sq-chan $s $nm]]
        [?if [not [= $lane ""]]
          [then [$cd-p2 $lane [$cd-sq-part $s $lane]]]
          [else [$cd-p2 $nm [$cd-sq-setchan [$cd-sq-part $s $nm] $nm $nm]]]]]]
    [else [?if [$cd-is-str-ne $n]
      [then [?let [= $v [$string $n]] [$cd-p2 $v [$cd-sq-part $s $v]]]]
      [else [$cd-p2 "channel" [$cd-sq-part $s "channel"]]]]]]]

[; ── the flatten pass (flatten_let_seq_aliasing) ──────────────────────
   Peers through `[?let [= $x V] BODY]` chains, recording a
   `$bind → lane` alias for every `[?channel]`-valued binding. Threads
   `[fl [items …] [chans …]]`. ]
[?def cd-fl-push pure [returns element] ($acc::element $n::any)
  [fl [items [?splice [?for [in $x $acc/items/*] [yield $x]]] $n]
      [chans [?splice [?for [in $c $acc/chans/*] [yield $c]]]]]]

[?def cd-fl-chan pure [returns element] ($acc::element $k::string $v::string)
  [fl [items [?splice [?for [in $x $acc/items/*] [yield $x]]]]
      [chans [?splice [?for [in $c $acc/chans/*] [where [not [= [$string $c@k] $k]]] [yield $c]]]
             [c k=$k v=$v]]]]

[?def cd-seq-flat pure [returns element] ($n::any $acc::element)
  [?if [$cd-is-dir-named $n "let"]
    [then [$cd-flat-let [$cd-sq-vals $n] 1 $acc]]
    [else [?if [= [$name $n] "cx:block"]
      [then [$cd-flat-block [?for [in $k $n/*] [yield [$cd-block-item $k]]] 1 $acc]]
      [else [$cd-fl-push $acc $n]]]]]]

[?def cd-flat-block pure [returns element] ($ns::any $i::int $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ns]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$cd-flat-block $ns [+ $i 1] [$cd-seq-flat [$nth $ns $i] $acc]]]]]

[?def cd-flat-let pure [returns element] ($vs::any $i::int $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $vs]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $v [$nth $vs $i]]
        [?if [$cd-is-eq $v]
          [then
            [?let [= $its [$cd-sq-kids $v]]
              [?if [>= [$count $its] 2]
                [then
                  [?let
                    [= $bn [$cd-let-bind [$nth $its 1]]]
                    [= $vn [$nth $its 2]]
                    [= $acc2 [?if [= $bn ""]
                      [then $acc]
                      [else [?if [$cd-is-dir-named $vn "channel"]
                        [then [$cd-fl-chan $acc $bn [$cd-nameattr $vn $bn]]]
                        [else $acc]]]]]
                    [$cd-flat-let $vs [+ $i 1] [$cd-seq-flat $vn $acc2]]]]
                [else [$cd-flat-let $vs [+ $i 1] $acc]]]]]
          [else [$cd-flat-let $vs [+ $i 1] [$cd-seq-flat $v $acc]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-flat-top pure [returns element] ($ns::any $i::int $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ns]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$cd-flat-top $ns [+ $i 1] [$cd-seq-flat [$nth $ns $i] $acc]]]]]

[; ── pass 1: actor lanes ────────────────────────────────────────────── ]
[?def cd-seq-pass1 pure [returns element] ($ns::any $i::int $s::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ns]]
    [then $s]
    [else
      [?let [= $n [$nth $ns $i]]
        [$cd-seq-pass1 $ns [+ $i 1]
          [?if [not [$cd-is-directive $n]]
            [then $s]
            [else
              [?let [= $l [$local-of $n]]
                [?if [= $l "worker"]
                  [then [$cd-sq-part $s [$cd-nameattr $n "producer"]]]
                [else [?if [= $l "channel"]
                  [then [?let [= $nm [$cd-nameattr $n "channel"]]
                    [$cd-sq-setchan [$cd-sq-part $s $nm] $nm $nm]]]
                [else [?if [= $l "http-service"]
                  [then [?let [= $nm [$cd-nameattr $n "svc"]]
                    [$cd-sq-part [$cd-sq-part $s $nm] "client"]]]
                [else [?if [= $l "async"]
                  [then [?let [= $s1 [$cd-sq-bump $s]]
                    [$cd-sq-part
                      [$cd-sq-part $s1 [$concat "async-" [$string $s1@async]]]
                      "caller"]]]
                [else $s]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[; ── the top-level directive dispatch ──────────────────────────────── ]
[?def cd-seq-topall pure [returns element] ($ns::any $i::int $s::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ns]]
    [then $s]
    [else
      [?let [= $n [$nth $ns $i]]
        [$cd-seq-topall $ns [+ $i 1]
          [?if [$cd-is-directive $n] [then [$cd-seq-top $n $s]] [else $s]]]]]]]

[?def cd-seq-top pure [returns element] ($d::any $s::element)
  [?let [= $l [$local-of $d]]
    [?if [= $l "worker"]
      [then
        [?let
          [= $nm [$cd-nameattr $d "worker"]]
          [= $s1 [$cd-sq-activate [$cd-sq-setw $s $nm] $nm]]
          [= $b [$cd-seq-bodyof $d]]
          [= $s2 [?if [$exists $b] [then [$cd-seq-body [$lab-val $b] $s1]] [else $s1]]]
          [$cd-sq-setw [$cd-sq-deactivate $s2 $nm] ""]]]
    [else [?if [= $l "channel"] [then $s]
    [else [?if [= $l "http-service"]
      [then [$cd-seq-http $d [$cd-nameattr $d "svc"] $s]]
    [else [?if [= $l "async"] [then [$cd-seq-async-top $s]]
    [else [?if [= $l "select"] [then [$cd-seq-select $d $s]]
    [else [?if [$cd-in-list $l ("send", "try-send")]
      [then [$cd-seq-send $d "main" [$cd-sq-part $s "main"]]]
    [else [?if [$cd-in-list $l ("receive", "try-receive")]
      [then [$cd-seq-recv $d "main" [$cd-sq-part $s "main"]]]
    [else [$cd-sq-line [$cd-sq-part $s "main"]
      [$concat "  Note over main : [?" $l "]"]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[; ── the body walk ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── ]
[?def cd-seq-body pure [returns element] ($n::any $s::element)
  [?if [$cd-is-directive $n]
    [then [$cd-seq-inner $n $s]]
    [else [?if [$cd-is-forcomp $n]
      [then [$cd-seq-body [$cd-fc-yield $n] $s]]
      [else [?if [$cd-in-list [$name $n] ("cx:block", "cd-block")]
        [then [$cd-seq-body-items [?for [in $k $n/*] [yield [$cd-block-item $k]]] 1 $s]]
        [else
          [?let [= $w [$cd-worker-or $s "main"]]
            [$cd-sq-line $s
              [$concat "  Note over " $w " : " [$cd-esc [$cd-label $n]]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-seq-body-items pure [returns element] ($ns::any $i::int $s::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ns]]
    [then $s]
    [else [$cd-seq-body-items $ns [+ $i 1] [$cd-seq-body [$nth $ns $i] $s]]]]]

[; the comprehension's yield body. ]
[?def cd-fc-yield pure [returns any] ($f::any)
  [$first [?for [in $k $f/*] [where [= [$name $k] "cx:yield"]]
    [yield [$first [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]]]]]

[; ── the inner-directive mapping (§10.1.2) ─────────────────────────── ]
[?def cd-seq-inner pure [returns element] ($d::any $s::element)
  [?let [= $w [$cd-worker-or $s "main"]] [= $l [$local-of $d]] [= $c [$code-class $l]]
    [?if [= $c "send"] [then [$cd-seq-send $d $w $s]]
    [else [?if [= $c "receive"] [then [$cd-seq-recv $d $w $s]]
    [else [?if [= $c "select"] [then [$cd-seq-select $d $s]]
    [else [?if [= $c "async"] [then [$cd-seq-async-inner $s]]
    [else [?if [= $c "await"]
      [then [$cd-seq-await $d $w $s]]
    [else [?if [= $c "cancel"] [then [$cd-seq-cancel $d $w $s]]
    [else [?if [= $c "resilience"]
      [then [$cd-seq-resil $d $w $s]]
    [else [?if [= $c "let"] [then [$cd-inner-let [$cd-sq-vals $d] 1 $s]]
    [else [?if [= $c "branch"]
      [then [$cd-inner-if [?for [in $k $d/*] [yield $k]] 1 $s]]
    [else [?if [= $c "for"]
      [then [$cd-inner-for [?for [in $k $d/*] [yield $k]] 1 $s]]
    [else [$cd-sq-line $s [$concat "  Note over " $w " : [?" $l "]"]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-inner-let pure [returns element] ($vs::any $i::int $s::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $vs]]
    [then $s]
    [else
      [?let [= $v [$nth $vs $i]]
        [?if [$cd-is-eq $v]
          [then
            [?let [= $its [$cd-sq-kids $v]]
              [$cd-inner-let $vs [+ $i 1]
                [?if [>= [$count $its] 2] [then [$cd-seq-body [$nth $its 2] $s]] [else $s]]]]]
          [else [$cd-inner-let $vs [+ $i 1] [$cd-seq-body $v $s]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-inner-if pure [returns element] ($ks::any $i::int $s::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then $s]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $k [$nth $ks $i]]
        [= $lb [$cd-sq-lbl $k]]
        [= $v [$cd-slot-value $k]]
        [?if [$cd-arm-clause $v]
          [then [$cd-inner-if $ks [+ $i 1] [$cd-seq-body-items [$cd-sq-kids $v] 1 $s]]]
          [else [$cd-inner-if $ks [+ $i 1]
            [?if [$cd-in-list $lb ("body", "yield", "then", "else", "do")]
              [then [$cd-seq-body $v $s]]
              [else $s]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-arm-clause pure [returns bool] ($v::any)
  [?if [$is-cx $v]
    [then false]
    [else [$cd-in-list [$name $v] ("then", "else", "case")]]]]

[?def cd-inner-for pure [returns element] ($ks::any $i::int $s::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then $s]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $k [$nth $ks $i]]
        [= $lb [$cd-sq-lbl $k]]
        [= $v [$cd-slot-value $k]]
        [?if [$cd-el-named $v "yield"]
          [then [$cd-inner-for $ks [+ $i 1] [$cd-seq-body-items [$cd-sq-kids $v] 1 $s]]]
          [else [$cd-inner-for $ks [+ $i 1]
            [?if [= $lb "yield"] [then [$cd-seq-body $v $s]] [else $s]]]]]]]]]

[; ── send / receive ────────────────────────────────────────────────── ]
[?def cd-seq-send pure [returns element] ($d::any $worker::string $s::element)
  [?let
    [= $pos [$cd-sq-pos $d]]
    [= $np [$count $pos]]
    [= $lto [$cd-lab-of $d "to"]]
    [= $lval [$cd-lab-of $d "value"]]
    [= $target [?if [$exists $lto]
      [then $lto]
      [else [?if [>= $np 2] [then [hit [$nth $pos 1]]] [else ()]]]]]
    [= $value [?if [$exists $lto]
      [then [?if [$exists $lval]
        [then $lval]
        [else [?if [> $np 0] [then [hit [$nth $pos 1]]] [else ()]]]]]
      [else [?if [>= $np 2]
        [then [hit [$nth $pos 2]]]
        [else [?if [= $np 1] [then [hit [$nth $pos 1]]] [else $lval]]]]]]]
    [= $r [?if [$exists $target]
      [then [$cd-chan-lane [$lab-val $target] $s]]
      [else [$cd-p2 "channel" $s]]]]
    [= $ch [$cd-p2v $r]]
    [= $s1 [$cd-p2s $r]]
    [= $vl [?if [$exists $value] [then [$cd-label [$lab-val $value]]] [else "msg"]]]
    [= $dashed [= [$local-of $d] "try-send"]]
    [= $ar [$cd-sq-sendk $s1 $ch $dashed]]
    [= $s2 [$cd-sq-sendk-s $s1 $ch]]
    [= $sfx [?if $dashed [then " (try)"] [else ""]]]
    [$cd-sq-line $s2
      [$concat "  " $worker " " $ar " " $ch " : " [$cd-esc $vl] $sfx]]]]

[?def cd-seq-recv pure [returns element] ($d::any $worker::string $s::element)
  [?let
    [= $sc [$cd-recv-scan [?for [in $k $d/*] [yield $k]] 1 [rs tl=""]]]
    [= $tg [?for [in $x $sc/*] [yield $x]]]
    [= $r [?if [> [$count $tg] 0]
      [then [$cd-chan-lane [$first $tg] $s]]
      [else [$cd-p2 "channel" $s]]]]
    [= $ch [$cd-p2v $r]]
    [= $s1 [$cd-p2s $r]]
    [= $tl [$string $sc@tl]]
    [= $tail [?if [= [$local-of $d] "try-receive"]
      [then [?if [= $tl ""] [then "msg (try)"] [else [$concat "msg (try, " $tl ")"]]]]
      [else "msg"]]]
    [= $ar [$cd-sq-recvk $s1 $ch true]]
    [= $s2 [$cd-sq-recvk-s $s1 $ch]]
    [$cd-sq-line $s2
      [$concat "  " $ch " " $ar " " $worker " : " [$cd-esc $tail]]]]]

[; cd-recv-scan — the receive slot walk: labeled `from` (last wins),
   labeled `timeout` (label text), else the FIRST positional. The
   accumulator carries the timeout text as @tl and the target as its
   single child. ]
[?def cd-recv-scan pure [returns element] ($ks::any $i::int $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $k [$nth $ks $i]]
        [= $lb [$cd-sq-lbl $k]]
        [?if [= $lb "from"]
          [then [$cd-recv-scan $ks [+ $i 1] [rs tl=[$string $acc@tl] [$cd-slot-value $k]]]]
          [else [?if [= $lb "timeout"]
            [then [$cd-recv-scan $ks [+ $i 1]
              [rs tl=[$cd-label [$cd-slot-value $k]]
                [?splice [?for [in $t $acc/*] [yield $t]]]]]]
            [else [?if [not [= $lb ""]]
              [then [$cd-recv-scan $ks [+ $i 1] $acc]]
              [else [?if [= [$count [?for [in $t $acc/*] [yield $t]]] 0]
                [then [$cd-recv-scan $ks [+ $i 1] [rs tl=[$string $acc@tl] $k]]]
                [else [$cd-recv-scan $ks [+ $i 1] $acc]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[; ── http-service resources ────────────────────────────────────────── ]
[?def cd-seq-http pure [returns element] ($d::any $svc::string $s::element)
  [?let [= $res [?for [in $v [$cd-sq-pos $d]]
      [where [$cd-el-named $v "resource"]] [yield $v]]]
    [?if [= [$count $res] 0]
      [then [$cd-sq-line $s [$concat "  Note over " $svc " : no routes"]]]
      [else [$cd-http-loop $res 1 $svc $s]]]]]

[?def cd-http-loop pure [returns element] ($res::any $i::int $svc::string $s::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $res]]
    [then $s]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $mp [$cd-http-mp [$cd-sq-kids [$nth $res $i]] 1 [mp m="GET" p="/"]]]
        [= $ra [$cd-sq-sendk $s $svc false]]
        [= $s1 [$cd-sq-line [$cd-sq-sendk-s $s $svc]
          [$concat "  client " $ra " " $svc " : " [$string $mp@m] " " [$string $mp@p]]]]
        [= $pa [$cd-sq-recvk $s1 $svc true]]
        [= $s2 [$cd-sq-line [$cd-sq-recvk-s $s1 $svc]
          [$concat "  " $svc " " $pa " client : response"]]]
        [$cd-http-loop $res [+ $i 1] $svc $s2]]]]]

[; http_resource_method_path — the FIRST element item gives the method
   (upper-cased element name) and, when its first item is a string, the
   path. ]
[?def cd-http-mp pure [returns element] ($its::any $i::int $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $its]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $it [$nth $its $i]]
        [?if [not [$cd-is-elem-lit $it]]
          [then [$cd-http-mp $its [+ $i 1] $acc]]
          [else
            [?let [= $sub [$cd-sq-kids $it]]
              [mp m=[$str-upper [$cd-erd-name $it]]
                  p=[?if [> [$count $sub] 0]
                    [then [?let [= $f [$first $sub]]
                      [?if [$cd-is-str $f] [then [$string $f]] [else "/"]]]]
                    [else "/"]]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-is-str pure [returns bool] ($n::any)
  [?if [$is-cx $n] [then [= [$local-of $n] "str"]] [else false]]]

[; ── select → the alt frame ────────────────────────────────────────── ]
[?def cd-seq-select pure [returns element] ($d::any $s::element)
  [?let
    [= $w [$cd-worker-or $s "main"]]
    [= $r [$cd-select-loop [?for [in $k $d/*] [yield $k]] 1 $w true
      [$cd-sq-part $s $w]]]
    [= $sf [$cd-p2s $r]]
    [?if [= [$cd-p2v $r] "first"]
      [then $sf]
      [else [$cd-sq-line $sf "  end"]]]]]

[?def cd-select-loop pure [returns element]
    ($ks::any $i::int $w::string $first::bool $s::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then [$cd-p2 [?if $first [then "first"] [else "more"]] $s]]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $k [$nth $ks $i]]
        [= $lb [$cd-sq-lbl $k]]
        [= $cv [?if [= $lb "case"]
          [then [hit [$cd-slot-value $k]]]
          [else [?if [= $lb ""]
            [then [?if [$cd-el-named $k "case"] [then [hit $k]] [else ()]]]
            [else ()]]]]]
        [?if [not [$exists $cv]]
          [then [$cd-select-loop $ks [+ $i 1] $w $first $s]]
          [else
            [?let [= $c [$lab-val $cv]]
              [?if [not [$cd-is-elem-lit $c]]
                [then [$cd-select-loop $ks [+ $i 1] $w $first $s]]
                [else [$cd-select-emit $ks $i $w $first $s $c]]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-select-emit pure [returns element]
    ($ks::any $i::int $w::string $first::bool $s::element $c::any)
  [?let
    [= $h0 [$cd-case-slots [$cd-sq-slots $c] 1 [ch k="from" n="channel" t="" $s]]]
    [= $h1 [$cd-case-items $c $h0]]
    [= $hk [$string $h1@k]]
    [= $cn [$string $h1@n]]
    [= $tl [$string $h1@t]]
    [= $s2 [$cd-chs $h1]]
    [= $lbl
      [?if [= $hk "from"] [then [$concat "msg from " $cn]]
      [else [?if [= $hk "timeout"]
        [then [?if [= $tl ""] [then "timeout"] [else [$concat "timeout (" $tl ")"]]]]
      [else [?if [= $hk "default"] [then "default"] [else "case"]]]]]]]
    [= $s3 [$cd-sq-line $s2
      [?if $first [then [$concat "  alt " $lbl]] [else [$concat "  else " $lbl]]]]]
    [= $s4
      [?if [= $hk "from"]
        [then [$cd-sq-line $s3 [$concat "    " $cn " ->> " $w " : msg"]]]
      [else [?if [= $hk "timeout"]
        [then [$cd-sq-line $s3 [$concat "    " $w " ->> " $w " : " $lbl]]]
      [else [?if [= $hk "default"]
        [then [$cd-sq-line $s3 [$concat "    Note over " $w ": default"]]]
      [else $s3]]]]]]]
    [$cd-select-loop $ks [+ $i 1] $w false $s4]]]

[; cd-chs — the state child of a `[ch …]` case-head accumulator. ]
[?def cd-chs pure [returns element] ($acc::element)
  [$first [?for [in $x $acc/*] [yield $x]]]]

[?def cd-case-slots pure [returns element] ($sls::any $i::int $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $sls]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $sl [$nth $sls $i]]
        [= $lb [$string $sl@label]]
        [?if [= $lb "from"]
          [then
            [?let [= $r [$cd-chan-lane
                [$first [?for [in $x $sl/*] [yield $x]]] [$cd-chs $acc]]]
              [$cd-case-slots $sls [+ $i 1]
                [ch k=[$string $acc@k] n=[$cd-p2v $r] t=[$string $acc@t] [$cd-p2s $r]]]]]
          [else [?if [= $lb "timeout"]
            [then [$cd-case-slots $sls [+ $i 1]
              [ch k="timeout" n=[$string $acc@n]
                t=[$cd-label [$first [?for [in $x $sl/*] [yield $x]]]] [$cd-chs $acc]]]]
            [else [$cd-case-slots $sls [+ $i 1] $acc]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-case-items pure [returns element] ($c::any $acc::element)
  [?let [= $its [$cd-sq-kids $c]]
    [?if [= [$count $its] 0]
      [then $acc]
      [else
        [?let [= $f [$first $its]]
          [?if [not [$cd-is-elem-lit $f]]
            [then $acc]
            [else
              [?let [= $fn [$cd-erd-name $f]] [= $fi [$cd-sq-kids $f]]
                [?if [= $fn "from"]
                  [then [?if [> [$count $fi] 0]
                    [then [?let [= $r [$cd-chan-lane [$first $fi] [$cd-chs $acc]]]
                      [ch k=[$string $acc@k] n=[$cd-p2v $r] t=[$string $acc@t] [$cd-p2s $r]]]]
                    [else $acc]]]
                [else [?if [= $fn "timeout"]
                  [then [?if [> [$count $fi] 0]
                    [then [ch k="timeout" n=[$string $acc@n]
                      t=[$cd-label [$first $fi]] [$cd-chs $acc]]]
                    [else [ch k="timeout" n=[$string $acc@n] t=[$string $acc@t]
                      [$cd-chs $acc]]]]]
                [else [?if [= $fn "default"]
                  [then [ch k="default" n=[$string $acc@n] t=[$string $acc@t]
                    [$cd-chs $acc]]]
                  [else $acc]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[; ── async / await / cancel ────────────────────────────────────────── ]
[?def cd-seq-async-top pure [returns element] ($s::element)
  [?let
    [= $s1 [$cd-sq-bump $s]]
    [= $lane [$concat "async-" [$string $s1@async]]]
    [$cd-sq-line [$cd-sq-part [$cd-sq-part $s1 $lane] "caller"]
      [$concat "  caller ->> " $lane " : start"]]]]

[?def cd-seq-async-inner pure [returns element] ($s::element)
  [?let
    [= $s1 [$cd-sq-bump $s]]
    [= $lane [$concat "async-" [$string $s1@async]]]
    [= $s2 [$cd-sq-part $s1 $lane]]
    [$cd-sq-line $s2
      [$concat "  " [$cd-worker-or $s2 "caller"] " ->> " $lane " : start"]]]]

[?def cd-seq-await pure [returns element] ($d::any $w::string $s::element)
  [?let
    [= $l [$local-of $d]]
    [= $t [$cd-await-target [$cd-sq-pos $d] 1]]
    [= $lbl [?if [= $t ""] [then $l] [else [$concat $l " " $t]]]]
    [$cd-sq-line $s [$concat "  Note over " $w " : " [$cd-esc $lbl]]]]]

[?def cd-await-target pure [returns string] ($pos::any $i::int)
  [?if [> $i [$count $pos]]
    [then ""]
    [else
      [?let [= $t [$cd-label [$nth $pos $i]]]
        [?if [= $t ""] [then [$cd-await-target $pos [+ $i 1]]] [else $t]]]]]]

[?def cd-seq-cancel pure [returns element] ($d::any $w::string $s::element)
  [?let [= $r [$cd-cancel-scan [$cd-sq-pos $d] 1 [$cd-p2 "async" $s]]]
    [$cd-sq-line [$cd-p2s $r]
      [$concat "  " $w " -x " [$cd-p2v $r] " : cancel"]]]]

[?def cd-cancel-scan pure [returns element] ($pos::any $i::int $r::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $pos]]
    [then $r]
    [else
      [?let [= $v [$nth $pos $i]]
        [?if [not [$cd-is-var0 $v]]
          [then [$cd-cancel-scan $pos [+ $i 1] $r]]
          [else
            [?let
              [= $nm [$string $v]]
              [= $s0 [$cd-p2s $r]]
              [= $lane [$cd-sq-chan $s0 $nm]]
              [?if [not [= $lane ""]]
                [then [$cd-cancel-scan $pos [+ $i 1] [$cd-p2 $lane $s0]]]
                [else [$cd-cancel-scan $pos [+ $i 1]
                  [$cd-p2 $nm [$cd-sq-part $s0 $nm]]]]]]]]]]]]

[; ── resilience wrappers ───────────────────────────────────────────── ]
[?def cd-seq-resil pure [returns element] ($d::any $w::string $s::element)
  [?let
    [= $l [$local-of $d]]
    [= $policy [?if [= $l "circuit-breaker"] [then "breaker"] [else $l]]]
    [= $pp
      [?if [= $l "retry"] [then [$cd-resil-param $d "max"]]
      [else [?if [= $l "timeout"] [then [$cd-resil-param $d "after"]]
      [else [?if [= $l "circuit-breaker"] [then [$cd-resil-param $d "threshold"]]
      [else [?if [= $l "rate-limit"] [then [$cd-resil-param $d "rate"]]
      [else [?if [= $l "bulkhead"] [then [$cd-resil-param $d "max"]]
      [else [?if [= $l "fallback"] [then [$cd-resil-param $d "recover-with"]]
      [else ""]]]]]]]]]]]]]
    [= $lbl [?if [= [$string $s@level] "full"]
      [then [?if [= $pp ""] [then $policy] [else [$concat $policy " " $pp]]]]
      [else $policy]]]
    [= $s1 [$cd-sq-line $s [$concat "  Note over " $w " : " [$cd-esc $lbl]]]]
    [$cd-resil-rec [?for [in $k $d/*] [yield $k]] 1 $s1]]]

[?def cd-resil-param pure [returns string] ($d::any $key::string)
  [?let [= $h [$cd-lab-of $d $key]]
    [?if [$exists $h]
      [then [$concat $key "=" [$cd-label [$lab-val $h]]]]
      [else ""]]]]

[?def cd-resil-rec pure [returns element] ($ks::any $i::int $s::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then $s]
    [else
      [?let [= $k [$nth $ks $i]] [= $lb [$cd-sq-lbl $k]]
        [$cd-resil-rec $ks [+ $i 1]
          [?if [$cd-in-list $lb ("body", "do")]
            [then [$cd-seq-body [$cd-slot-value $k] $s]]
            [else [?if [= $lb ""] [then [$cd-seq-body $k $s]] [else $s]]]]]]]]]

[; ── collect_binding_intros (shared with the CFG `full` rung) ───────── ]
[?def cd-binding-intros pure [returns any] ($img::any)
  [?let [= $acc [$cd-walk-intros $img [names]]]
    [?for [in $n $acc/*] [yield [$string $n@v]]]]]

[?def cd-walk-intros pure [returns element] ($n::any $acc::element)
  [?if [$cd-is-directive $n]
    [then
      [?let
        [= $vs [$cd-sq-vals $n]]
        [= $a1 [?if [= [$local-of $n] "let"] [then [$cd-intros-let $vs 1 $acc]] [else $acc]]]
        [$cd-intros-all $vs 1 $a1]]]
    [else [?if [$cd-is-forcomp $n]
      [then
        [?let
          [= $a1 [$cd-intros-clauses
            [?for [in $c $n/*] [where [= [$name $c] "cx:clause"]] [yield $c]] 1 $acc]]
          [$cd-intros-all [$cd-fc-children $n] 1 $a1]]]
      [else [?if [$cd-is-lit $n]
        [then [$cd-intros-all [$cd-lit-children $n] 1 $acc]]
        [else $acc]]]]]]]

[; an `err`-named node cannot be handed to a call at all, so its literal
   walk (items + slot values, attributes excluded) is inlined here. ]
[?def cd-intros-all pure [returns element] ($ns::any $i::int $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ns]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $x [$nth $ns $i]]
        [$cd-intros-all $ns [+ $i 1]
          [?if [= [?else [$name $x] "err"] "err"]
            [then [$cd-intros-all
              [?for [in $y $x/*]
                [where [not [= [?else [$name $y] "err"] "cx:attr"]]]
                [yield [?if [= [?else [$name $y] "err"] "cx:slot"]
                  [then [$first [?for [in $v $y/*] [yield $v]]]]
                  [else $y]]]]
              1 $acc]]
            [else [$cd-walk-intros $x $acc]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-intros-let pure [returns element] ($vs::any $i::int $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $vs]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $v [$nth $vs $i]]
        [$cd-intros-let $vs [+ $i 1]
          [?if [not [$cd-is-eq $v]]
            [then $acc]
            [else
              [?let [= $its [$cd-sq-kids $v]]
                [?if [>= [$count $its] 1]
                  [then [$cd-name-add $acc [$cd-let-bind [$first $its]]]]
                  [else $acc]]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-intros-clauses pure [returns element] ($cs::any $i::int $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $cs]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $c [$nth $cs $i]] [= $k [$string $c@kind]]
        [$cd-intros-clauses $cs [+ $i 1]
          [?if [$cd-in-list $k ("generator", "binding")]
            [then [?if [$exists $c@bind] [then [$cd-name-add $acc [$string $c@bind]]] [else $acc]]]
            [else $acc]]]]]]]

[; cd-lit-children — a literal's ITEM nodes plus its SLOT values (the V
   walk reads `n.items` + `n.slots`; attributes are NOT walked). The
   `item` / `entry` wrappers of a seq / arr / block / map read back as
   plain element literals, so the recursion reaches the wrapped node. ]
[?def cd-lit-children pure [returns any] ($n::any)
  [?for [in $k $n/*]
    [where [not [= [?else [$name $k] "err"] "cx:attr"]]]
    [yield [?if [= [?else [$name $k] "err"] "cx:slot"]
      [then [$first [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]]
      [else $k]]]]]

[; cd-fc-children — for_comp_children (L100): per clause source then
   expr, then the yield node, then the map-yield value. ]
[?def cd-fc-children pure [returns any] ($f::any)
  [?for [in $k $f/*] [in $v [$cd-fc-kid $k]] [yield $v]]]

[?def cd-fc-kid pure [returns any] ($k::any)
  [?if [= [$name $k] "cx:clause"]
    [then [?for [in $c $k/*]
      [where [$cd-in-list [$name $c] ("cx:source", "cx:expr-clause")]]
      [yield [$first [?for [in $v $c/*] [yield $v]]]]]]
    [else [?if [$cd-in-list [$name $k] ("cx:yield", "cx:yield-value")]
      [then [?for [in $v $k/*] [yield $v]]]
      [else ()]]]]]

[; ── code_diagram_seq ──────────────────────────────────────────────── ]
[?def cd-seq pure [returns any] ($img::any $level::string)
  [?let
    [= $fl [$cd-flat-top [$cd-stmts $img] 1 [fl [items] [chans]]]]
    [= $stmts [?for [in $x $fl/items/*] [yield $x]]]
    [= $s0 [$cd-sq-mk "sequenceDiagram" 0 "" $level ()
      [?for [in $c $fl/chans/*] [yield $c]] ()]]
    [= $s1 [?if [= $level "full"] [then [$cd-sq-part $s0 "INPUT"]] [else $s0]]]
    [= $s2 [$cd-seq-pass1 $stmts 1 $s1]]
    [?if [= $level "min"]
      [then [$cd-sq-out $s2]]
      [else
        [?let
          [= $s3 [?if [= $level "full"] [then [$cd-sq-part $s2 "OUTPUT"]] [else $s2]]]
          [= $s4 [$cd-seq-topall $stmts 1 $s3]]
          [?if [= $level "full"]
            [then [$cd-sq-out [$cd-seq-binds [$cd-binding-intros $img] 1 $s4]]]
            [else [$cd-sq-out $s4]]]]]]]]

[; the `full` rung's binding-resolution notes: one per introduced
   binding, on the current worker lane / the first participant / main. ]
[?def cd-seq-binds pure [returns element] ($ns::any $i::int $s::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ns]]
    [then $s]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $ps [$cd-sq-ps $s]]
        [= $p1 [?if [> [$count $ps] 0] [then [$first $ps]] [else [p n="main"]]]]
        [= $lane [?if [not [= [$string $s@worker] ""]]
          [then [$string $s@worker]]
          [else [$string $p1@n]]]]
        [$cd-seq-binds $ns [+ $i 1]
          [$cd-sq-line $s [$concat "  Note over " $lane " : bind $" [$nth $ns $i]]]]]]]]
[; ── §9.4b ERD `full` (code_diagram_erd_full) ─────────────────────────
   Compact ERD + the synthetic DOCUMENT root, inferred-FK edges,
   per-attribute value enumeration, and the occurrence badge. Layered
   over the compact TEXT exactly as the V emitter layered it — the row
   surgery IS the contract. ]

[; cd-erd-stats — collect_erd_full_stats: per element NAME (every
   element the walk reaches, scalar children included) the occurrence
   count and max depth, plus per `Entity@attr` key the value list
   (≤ 10 distinct kept verbatim, an empty sentinel past the cap). ]
[?def cd-erd-stats-top pure [returns element] ($stmts::any $i::int $st::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $stmts]]
    [then $st]
    [else [$cd-erd-stats-top $stmts [+ $i 1] [$cd-erd-stats [$nth $stmts $i] 0 $st]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-stats pure [returns element] ($n::any $depth::int $st::element)
  [?if [$cd-erd-ismap $n]
    [; the bare-map document's entry values feed the full-level value
       slots under the `map` entity, mirroring the attribute walk. ]
    [then [$cd-erd-stats-map [$cd-map-entries-of $n] 1 "map"
      [$cd-occ-bump $st "map" $depth]]]
  [else [?if [not [$cd-erd-entity $n]]
    [then $st]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $nm [$cd-erd-name $n]]
        [= $st1 [$cd-occ-bump $st $nm $depth]]
        [= $st2 [$cd-erd-stats-attrs [$cd-erd-attrs $n] 1 $nm $st1]]
        [= $st2b [$cd-erd-stats-mapkids [$cd-erd-kids $n] 1 $nm $st2]]
        [$cd-erd-stats-items [$cd-erd-kids $n] 1 [+ $depth 1] $st2b]]]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-stats-mapkids pure [returns element] ($items::any $i::int $nm::string $st::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $items]]
    [then $st]
    [else
      [?let [= $it [$nth $items $i]]
        [$cd-erd-stats-mapkids $items [+ $i 1] $nm
          [?if [$cd-erd-ismap $it]
            [then [$cd-erd-stats-map [$cd-map-entries-of $it] 1 $nm $st]]
            [else $st]]]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-stats-map pure [returns element] ($es::any $i::int $nm::string $st::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $es]]
    [then $st]
    [else
      [?let [= $e [$nth $es $i]]
        [$cd-erd-stats-map $es [+ $i 1] $nm
          [?if [$exists $e@decl]
            [then $st]
            [else [$cd-av-add $st [$concat $nm "@" [$string $e@key]]
              [$cd-label [$first [?for [in $v $e/*] [yield $v]]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-stats-items pure [returns element] ($items::any $i::int $depth::int $st::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $items]]
    [then $st]
    [else [$cd-erd-stats-items $items [+ $i 1] $depth
      [$cd-erd-stats [$nth $items $i] $depth $st]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-stats-attrs pure [returns element] ($attrs::any $i::int $nm::string $st::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $attrs]]
    [then $st]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $a [$nth $attrs $i]]
        [= $key [$concat $nm "@" [$string $a@name]]]
        [= $val [$cd-label [$first [?for [in $v $a/*] [yield $v]]]]]
        [$cd-erd-stats-attrs $attrs [+ $i 1] $nm [$cd-av-add $st $key $val]]]]]]

[?def cd-occ-bump pure [returns element] ($st::element $nm::string $depth::int)
  [?if [$exists [$first [?for [in $o $st/occ/*] [where [= [$string $o@n] $nm]] [yield 1]]]]
    [then
      [stats
        [occ [?splice [?for [in $o $st/occ/*]
          [yield [?if [= [$string $o@n] $nm]
            [then [o n=$nm v=[+ $o@v 1]
                     d=[?if [> $depth $o@d] [then $depth] [else $o@d]]]]
            [else $o]]]]]]
        [av [?splice [?for [in $a $st/av/*] [yield $a]]]]]]
    [else
      [stats
        [occ [?splice [?for [in $o $st/occ/*] [yield $o]]] [o n=$nm v=1 d=$depth]]
        [av [?splice [?for [in $a $st/av/*] [yield $a]]]]]]]]

[; cd-av-add — the value-list append with the V cap rule: below 11
   entries a NEW distinct value is appended, at or above the cap an
   empty sentinel is appended instead. ]
[?def cd-av-add pure [returns element] ($st::element $key::string $val::string)
  [?if [not [$exists [$first [?for [in $a $st/av/*] [where [= [$string $a@k] $key]] [yield 1]]]]]
    [then
      [stats
        [occ [?splice [?for [in $o $st/occ/*] [yield $o]]]]
        [av [?splice [?for [in $a $st/av/*] [yield $a]]] [a k=$key [vals [v t=$val]]]]]]
    [else
      [stats
        [occ [?splice [?for [in $o $st/occ/*] [yield $o]]]]
        [av [?splice [?for [in $a $st/av/*]
          [yield [?if [not [= [$string $a@k] $key]]
            [then $a]
            [else
              [?let
                [= $n [$count $a/vals/*]]
                [= $seen [$exists [$first [?for [in $v $a/vals/*]
                  [where [= [$string $v@t] $val]] [yield 1]]]]]
                [?if [< $n 11]
                  [then [?if $seen
                    [then $a]
                    [else [a k=$key [vals [?splice [?for [in $v $a/vals/*] [yield $v]]] [v t=$val]]]]]]
                  [else [a k=$key [vals [?splice [?for [in $v $a/vals/*] [yield $v]]] [v t=""]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-occ-count pure [returns int] ($st::element $nm::string)
  [?let [= $hits [?for [in $o $st/occ/*] [where [= [$string $o@n] $nm]] [yield $o@v]]]
    [?if [= [$count $hits] 0] [then -1] [else [$first $hits]]]]]

[?def cd-occ-depth pure [returns int] ($st::element $nm::string)
  [?let [= $hits [?for [in $o $st/occ/*] [where [= [$string $o@n] $nm]] [yield $o@d]]]
    [?if [= [$count $hits] 0] [then 0] [else [$first $hits]]]]]

[; cd-strip-id-suffix — strip_id_suffix: `foo-id` / `foo_id` / `fooId`
   → `foo`; a bare `id` (or no suffix) drives no inference. ]
[?def cd-strip-id-suffix pure [returns string] ($s::string)
  [?let [= $n [$str-length $s]]
    [?if [and [$str-ends-with $s "-id"] [> $n 3]]
      [then [$str-slice $s 0 [- $n 3]]]
      [else [?if [and [$str-ends-with $s "_id"] [> $n 3]]
        [then [$str-slice $s 0 [- $n 3]]]
        [else [?if [and [$str-ends-with $s "Id"] [> $n 2]]
          [then [$str-slice $s 0 [- $n 2]]]
          [else ""]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-fk-lines pure [returns string] ($st::element)
  [$cd-fk-outer [?for [in $o $st/occ/*] [yield $o]] 1 $st ""]]

[?def cd-fk-outer pure [returns string] ($occs::any $i::int $st::element $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $occs]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $ent [$string [$nth $occs $i]@n]]
        [$cd-fk-outer $occs [+ $i 1] $st
          [$cd-fk-inner [?for [in $a $st/av/*] [yield $a]] 1 $ent $st $acc]]]]]]

[?def cd-fk-inner pure [returns string] ($avs::any $i::int $ent::string $st::element $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $avs]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $key [$string [$nth $avs $i]@k]]
        [= $at [$str-find $key "@"]]
        [?if [< $at 0]
          [then [$cd-fk-inner $avs [+ $i 1] $ent $st $acc]]
          [else
            [?let
              [= $owner [$str-slice $key 0 $at]]
              [= $attr [$str-slice $key [+ $at 1] [$str-length $key]]]
              [?if [not [= $owner $ent]]
                [then [$cd-fk-inner $avs [+ $i 1] $ent $st $acc]]
                [else
                  [?let [= $cand [$cd-strip-id-suffix $attr]]
                    [?if [or [= $cand ""] [= $cand $ent]]
                      [then [$cd-fk-inner $avs [+ $i 1] $ent $st $acc]]
                      [else [?if [>= [$cd-occ-count $st $cand] 0]
                        [then [$cd-fk-inner $avs [+ $i 1] $ent $st
                          [$jn $acc [$concat "  " [$cd-erd-quote $ent] " }o--o{ "
                                                [$cd-erd-quote $cand] " : FK"]]]]
                        [else [$cd-fk-inner $avs [+ $i 1] $ent $st $acc]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[; cd-erd-suppress — should_suppress_document_root. ]
[?def cd-erd-suppress pure [returns bool] ($stmts::any)
  [?if [not [= [$count $stmts] 1]]
    [then false]
    [else
      [?let [= $s [$first $stmts]]
        [?if [not [$cd-erd-entity $s]]
          [then false]
          [else [?if [> [$count [$cd-erd-slots $s]] 0]
            [then false]
            [else [not [$exists [$first [?for [in $k [$cd-erd-kids $s]]
              [where [$cd-erd-entity $k]] [yield 1]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-strip-quoted pure [returns string] ($s::string)
  [?let [= $n [$str-length $s]]
    [?if [and [>= $n 2] [and [$str-starts-with $s "\""] [$str-ends-with $s "\""]]]
      [then [$str-slice $s 1 [- $n 1]]]
      [else $s]]]]

[?def cd-value-enum pure [returns string] ($vals::any)
  [?let [= $d [?for [in $x [$cd-distinct-vals $vals 1 [names]]/*] [yield [$string $x@v]]]]
    [?if [<= [$count $d] 10]
      [then [$str-replace [$cd-join-comma $d 1 ""] "\"" "\\\""]]
      [else [$str-replace
        [$concat [$cd-join-comma [$cd-take3 $d] 1 ""]
                 ", …, (" [?str '{[$count $d]}'] " unique)"]
        "\"" "\\\""]]]]]

[?def cd-take3 pure [returns any] ($xs::any)
  [?for [in $i (1, 2, 3)] [yield [$nth $xs $i]]]]

[?def cd-distinct-vals pure [returns element] ($vals::any $i::int $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $vals]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $t [$string [$nth $vals $i]@t]]
        [?if [= $t ""]
          [then [$cd-distinct-vals $vals [+ $i 1] $acc]]
          [else [$cd-distinct-vals $vals [+ $i 1] [$cd-name-add $acc $t]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-join-comma pure [returns string] ($xs::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $xs]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$cd-join-comma $xs [+ $i 1]
      [?if [= $acc ""] [then [$nth $xs $i]] [else [$concat $acc ", " [$nth $xs $i]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-av-vals pure [returns any] ($st::element $key::string)
  [$first [?for [in $a $st/av/*] [where [= [$string $a@k] $key]]
    [yield [hit [?splice [?for [in $v $a/vals/*] [yield $v]]]]]]]]

[; cd-erd-document — the synthetic DOCUMENT root, POPULATED (RULED:
   DGX-2, ledger/rulings_2026_08_21_diagram_capabilities.md; #901 item
   4). It shipped listing four stat FIELDS and never their VALUES — a
   schema of statistics rather than the statistics, which is why it read
   as noise, while every real entity beside it already uses the value
   slot (`int id "@ 1"`). The three countable rows now carry their
   numbers, read off the stats the full-level walk ALREADY collects for
   the occurrence badges: no new traversal.

   The fourth row, `string source_path`, is DROPPED rather than
   populated: this renderer's ingress is source TEXT — `code-diagram`
   has never been handed a path, and the one caller that has one
   (`cx code-diagram FILE`) does not pass it. A row that can only ever
   be empty is the same defect at one quarter scale. ]
[?def cd-erd-document pure [returns string] ($stats::element)
  [?let
    [= $os [?for [in $o $stats/occ/*] [yield $o]]]
    [; the braces are literal Mermaid entity-block syntax, so this is
       built with [$concat] rather than [$str-format] — `{` opens a
       placeholder in the format grammar. ]
    [$concat "  DOCUMENT {\n    int node_count \"" [$string [$cd-doc-nodes $os 1 0]]
             "\"\n    int type_count \"" [$string [$count $os]]
             "\"\n    int max_depth \"" [$string [$cd-doc-depth $os 1 0]]
             "\"\n  }"]]]

[?def cd-doc-nodes pure [returns int] ($os::any $i::int $acc::int)
  [?if [> $i [$count $os]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $o [$nth $os $i]]
        [$cd-doc-nodes $os [+ $i 1] [+ $acc [$cast $o@v :int]]]]]]]

[?def cd-doc-depth pure [returns int] ($os::any $i::int $acc::int)
  [?if [> $i [$count $os]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $o [$nth $os $i]] [= $d [$cast $o@d :int]]
        [$cd-doc-depth $os [+ $i 1] [?if [> $d $acc] [then $d] [else $acc]]]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-full pure [returns any] ($img::any)
  [?let
    [= $stmts [$cd-stmts $img]]
    [= $stats [$cd-erd-stats-top $stmts 1 [stats [occ] [av]]]]
    [= $tbl [$cd-tbl-top $stmts 1 [tbls]]]
    [= $compact [$cd-erd $img]]
    [= $lines [$str-split-lines $compact]]
    [= $doc [?if [$cd-erd-suppress $stmts]
      [then ""]
      [else [$cd-erd-document $stats]]]]
    [$jn4 [$nth $lines 1] $doc [$cd-erd-fk-lines $stats]
      [$cd-erd-full-body $lines 2 $stats $tbl ""]]]]

[; ── the TI-1 row COUNT, `full` rung only ──
   RULED: TI-1 (#914), render rule 1's second half. The table's row
   count is the one piece of row information a diagram carries, and it
   rides the SAME Mermaid comment slot the DGX-2 stat rows use
   (`int node_count "N"`), on the `full` rung only — the rung where
   attribute VALUES already appear. `cd-tbl-*` collects it in one pass
   over the same statement list the stats walk reads, keyed by entity
   name, first occurrence winning (the same rule `cd-erd-add-row` uses
   for a repeated field). ]
[?def cd-tbl-top pure [returns element] ($stmts::any $i::int $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $stmts]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$cd-tbl-top $stmts [+ $i 1] [$cd-tbl-walk [$nth $stmts $i] $acc]]]]]

[?def cd-tbl-walk pure [returns element] ($n::any $acc::element)
  [?if [not [$cd-erd-entity $n]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $a1 [?if [$cd-has-table $n]
          [then [$cd-tbl-add $acc [$cd-erd-name $n] [$cd-table-rows $n]]]
          [else $acc]]]
        [$cd-tbl-items [$cd-erd-kids $n] 1 $a1]]]]]

[?def cd-tbl-items pure [returns element] ($items::any $i::int $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $items]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$cd-tbl-items $items [+ $i 1] [$cd-tbl-walk [$nth $items $i] $acc]]]]]

[?def cd-tbl-add pure [returns element] ($acc::element $nm::string $rows::string)
  [?if [$exists [$first [?for [in $t $acc/*] [where [= [$string $t@n] $nm]] [yield 1]]]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [tbls [?splice [?for [in $t $acc/*] [yield $t]]] [t n=$nm v=$rows]]]]]

[?def cd-tbl-rows-of pure [returns string] ($acc::element $nm::string)
  [?let [= $hits [?for [in $t $acc/*] [where [= [$string $t@n] $nm]]
      [yield [$string $t@v]]]]
    [?if [= [$count $hits] 0] [then ""] [else [$first $hits]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-full-body pure [returns string] ($lines::any $i::int $stats::element
                                              $tbl::element $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $lines]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $ln [$nth $lines $i]]
        [= $t [$str-trim $ln]]
        [?if [and [$str-ends-with $t " {"] [not [$str-starts-with $t "DOCUMENT"]]]
          [then
            [?let
              [= $ent [$str-trim [$str-slice $t 0 [- [$str-length $t] 2]]]]
              [= $r [$cd-erd-full-rows $lines [+ $i 1] $stats $tbl [$cd-strip-quoted $ent] [$jn $acc $ln]]]
              [$cd-erd-full-body $lines $r.i $stats $tbl $r.out]]]
          [else [$cd-erd-full-body $lines [+ $i 1] $stats $tbl [$jn $acc $ln]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-full-rows pure [returns map] ($lines::any $i::int $stats::element
                                           $tbl::element $ent::string $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $lines]]
    [then {i: $i, out: $acc}]
    [else
      [?let [= $ln [$nth $lines $i]] [= $t [$str-trim $ln]]
        [?if [= $t "}"]
          [then
            [?let
              [= $cnt [$cd-occ-count $stats $ent]]
              [= $rows [$cd-tbl-rows-of $tbl $ent]]
              [= $trow [?if [= $rows ""]
                [then ""]
                [else [$concat "    int row_count \"" $rows "\""]]]]
              [= $badge [?if [< $cnt 0]
                [then ""]
                [else [?if [?if [= $cnt 1] [then [= [$cd-occ-depth $stats $ent] 0]] [else false]]
                [; a 1×-at-depth-0 badge carries no information — drop it
                   (playground report 2026-08-22). ]
                [then ""]
                [else [?if [> $cnt 100]
                  [then [$str-format "    string note \"appears ×{}\"" ($cnt)]]
                  [else [$str-format "    string note \"appears {}× depth {}\""
                          ($cnt, [$cd-occ-depth $stats $ent])]]]]]]]]
              {i: [+ $i 1], out: [$jn3 $acc [$jn $trow $badge] $ln]}]]
          [else
            [$cd-erd-full-rows $lines [+ $i 1] $stats $tbl $ent
              [$jn $acc [$cd-erd-enrich-row $ln $t $stats $ent]]]]]]]]]

[?def cd-erd-enrich-row pure [returns string] ($ln::string $t::string $stats::element $ent::string)
  [?if [not [$str-ends-with $t " \"@\""]]
    [then $ln]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $bare-t [$str-slice $t 0 [- [$str-length $t] 4]]]
        [= $parts [$str-split $bare-t " "]]
        [?if [not [= [$count $parts] 2]]
          [then $ln]
          [else
            [?let
              [= $key [$concat $ent "@" [$nth $parts 2]]]
              [= $w [$cd-av-vals $stats $key]]
              [?if [not [$exists $w]]
                [then $ln]
                [else
                  [?let [= $bare [$str-slice $ln 0 [- [$str-length $ln] 4]]]
                    [$concat $bare " \"@ " [$cd-value-enum [?for [in $v $w/*] [yield $v]]] "\""]]]]]]]]]]]

[; ── §9.7 of-source — the caller-facing entry (#889, owner "a") ───────
   The module's twelve wave-1/2 functions all expect the engine-injected
   program image, which no CX spelling produced: a frozen stdlib module
   was, in practice, uncallable from a CX program. `of-source` closes
   that: source text in, rendered diagram out, with the lift done
   INTERNALLY through the module's own ingress primitive (DRW3-3). The
   CLI (`cx diagram`) routes through this same entry — one lift path, no
   twin — so its output and a CX caller's are the same bytes.

   `detail` is the DR-11 rung and defaults to `min`, the same
   compatibility default a bare `mermaid` target carries.

   Declared IMPURE because `svg` / `png` reach the graphviz hop
   (`subprocess`, DRW2-1 posture unchanged); `mermaid` / `dot` perform
   no effect. ]
[; ── §9.7 of-source — the caller-facing entry (#889, owner "a") ───────
   The module's twelve wave-1/2 functions all expect the engine-injected
   program image, which no CX spelling produced: a frozen stdlib module
   was, in practice, uncallable from a CX program. `of-source` closes
   that: source text in, rendered diagram out, with the lift done
   INTERNALLY through the module's own ingress primitive (DRW3-3). The
   CLI (`cx diagram`) routes through this same entry — one lift path, no
   twin — so its output and a CX caller's are the same bytes.

   `detail` is the DR-11 rung and defaults to `min`, the same
   compatibility default a bare `mermaid` target carries.

   Declared IMPURE because `svg` / `png` reach the graphviz hop
   (`subprocess`, DRW2-1 posture unchanged); `mermaid` / `dot` perform
   no effect. ]
[; THE VECTOR ARMS OF `of-source` DELEGATE to `render-svg` / `render-png`
   (RULED: SPF-2, #897). There is now exactly ONE `dot` hop per format in
   this module, and therefore exactly one place where the `subprocess`
   capability is decided.

   THE BUG THIS CLOSES. Wave 2 INLINED the hop into `of-source`'s vector
   arms, and also left two private near-copies (`of-source-svg` /
   `of-source-png`, called by nothing) — four copies of one effect. When
   DSC-1c charged `svg`/`png` to `subprocess`, it added the `cap-denied`
   arm to `render-svg` / `render-png` ONLY. The other copies kept the
   pre-DSC-1 shape (`[?else … [dot-unavailable]]`, no `cap-denied`
   test), so an UNGRANTED caller arriving through `of-source` was handed
   the dot-less envelope instead of the refusal — while the same caller
   through `cx diagram` was refused. `of-source` is the arm every
   ABI/binding/embedding caller reaches via `eval_code(target='svg')`,
   so that is precisely the capability bypass DSC-1c exists to close
   ("the denial is NOT the envelope"). Duplication is what made the
   regression possible; de-duplication, not a fourth repair, is the fix.

   WHY THE ARMS STAY INLINE — RE-MEASURED, wave 2 was right. Collapsing
   them to `[$render-svg $img $src]` / `[$render-png $img $src]` was
   built and run: `eval_semantics_umbrella` REFUSES it, exactly as the
   wave-2 note predicted —

     these stdlib defs DECLARE impure but reach no callee the engine
     classifies impure … (#788): diagram:of-source

   The #788/#818 parity check counts impure BUILTINS only; an impure
   `[?def]` callee does not satisfy it (`classify_callee`'s recursion
   into `checker.defs` serves the OTHER direction — keeping a *pure* def
   from reaching an impure one). Delegating would leave `of-source`
   declaring `impure` while reaching nothing the engine calls impure,
   and a pure-required context would then silently admit a def that
   shells out. So the hop stays inline, which is also the honest shape:
   the capability is visible at the entry point that charges it.

   The duplication is therefore DELIBERATE and must be GUARDED, not
   trusted: `test_every_dot_hop_carries_the_dsc1c_refusal`
   (vcx/tests/code_diagram_roundtrip_test.v) scans this file and fails
   if any graphviz call site lacks its `cap-denied` → `dot-denied-err`
   arm. That gate is what makes a fifth copy — or a future wave
   re-inlining a stale one — red instead of silent. ]
[?def of-source scope=public impure [returns any] ($src::string $format::string $detail="min")
  [?let [= $img [?else [$diagram-program-image $src "ref"] [cd-unparsed]]]
    [?if [= [$name $img] "cd-unparsed"]
      [then [$diagram-program-image $src "ref"]]
      [else [?if [= $format "mermaid"]
        [then [$render-mermaid $img $src $detail]]
        [else [?if [= $format "dot"]
          [; RULED: D913-1 — the detail rung reaches the DOT text too;
             render-dot-detail routes a structure-free document to the
             data-tree walk and everything else to the shipped walk. ]
          [then [$render-dot-detail $img $detail]]
          [else [?if [= $format "svg"]
            [then [?if [not [$admitted-top $img]]
              [then [$unrenderable $img]]
              [else
                [?let [= $r [?fallback [$process-run ("dot", "-Tsvg") null false null [$render-dot-detail $img $detail] null true :stdout "utf-8" true false false]
                              [recover-with [dot-failure code=$err@code]]]]
                  [?if [$cap-denied $r]
                    [then [$dot-denied-err "svg"]]
                    [else
                      [?if [$dot-ok $r]
                        [then [$inject-svg-metadata [$string $r@stdout] $src]]
                        [else [$svg-envelope $src]]]]]]]]]
            [else [?if [= $format "png"]
              [then [?if [not [$admitted-top $img]]
                [then [$unrenderable $img]]
                [else
                  [?let [= $r [?fallback [$process-run ("dot", "-Tpng") null false null [$render-dot-detail $img $detail] null true :stdout :bytes true false false]
                                [recover-with [dot-failure code=$err@code]]]]
                    [?if [$cap-denied $r]
                      [then [$dot-denied-err "png"]]
                      [else
                        [?if [$dot-ok $r]
                          [then [$inject-png-chunk $r@stdout $src]]
                          [else [$png-envelope $src]]]]]]]]]
              [else [err code="cx-err:CXER0100"
                         message=[$concat "cx-err:CXER0100: diagram/of-source: format '" $format
                                          "' not recognised (mermaid|dot|svg|png)"]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[; ── §9.8 the public wave-3 surface ───────────────────────────────────
   code-diagram is the ONE entry the CLI (`cx code-diagram`), the wasm
   export `cx_code_diagram_with_level`, and any CX caller share. ]

[?def cd-erd-level pure [returns any] ($img::any $level::string)
  [?if [= $level "min"]
    [then [$cd-erd-min $img]]
    [else [?if [= $level "full"] [then [$cd-erd-full $img]] [else [$cd-erd $img]]]]]]

[?def cd-cfg-level pure [returns any] ($img::any $level::string)
  [?if [= $level "min"]
    [then [$cd-cfg-min $img]]
    [else [?if [= $level "full"] [then [$cd-cfg-full $img]] [else [$cd-cfg $img]]]]]]

[?def code-diagram scope=public pure [returns any] ($src::string $level::string)
  [?let [= $stripped [$str-trim [$cd-strip-pis $src]]]
    [?if [= [$str-length $stripped] 0]
      [then "erDiagram"]
      [else
        [?let
          [= $img1 [?else [$diagram-program-image [$cd-patch-source $stripped] "code"] [cd-unparsed]]]
          [= $img [?if [= [$name $img1] "cd-unparsed"]
            [then [?else [$diagram-program-image $stripped "code"] [cd-unparsed]]]
            [else $img1]]]
          [?if [= [$name $img] "cd-unparsed"]
            [then [?if [$cd-text-is-sequence $stripped]
              [then "sequenceDiagram"]
              [else [?if [$cd-text-is-code $stripped] [then "flowchart TD"] [else "erDiagram"]]]]]
            [else [?if [$cd-program-is-sequence $img]
              [then [$cd-seq $img $level]]
              [else [?if [$cd-program-is-code $img]
                [then [$cd-cfg-level $img $level]]
                [else [$cd-erd-level $img $level]]]]]]]]]]]]

[; ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   §11 the effect/capability graph — RULED: DGX-1
   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ ]

[; ── §11.1 the sealed rule table (DGX-1b) ─────────────────────────────
   What is rendering POLICY lives here and is gated against the spec
   and the engine in both directions. What is a FACT ABOUT THE ENGINE —
   the primitive→capability map — is NOT copied here: it is read live
   through [$diagram-effect-table] (DGX-1a), because a stale copy could
   only ever fail by omitting a newly-gated effect point, and a
   capability diagram that quietly under-reports is worse than none. ]
[?def effect-rules scope=public pure [returns element] ()
  [effect-rules
    [cap name=read          flag="--allow-read"]
    [cap name=write         flag="--allow-write"]
    [cap name=net           flag="--allow-net"]
    [cap name=env           flag="--allow-env"]
    [cap name=clock         flag="--allow-clock"]
    [cap name=random        flag="--allow-random"]
    [cap name=subprocess    flag="--allow-subprocess"]
    [cap name=eval          flag="--allow-eval"]
    [cap name=secret-reveal flag="--allow-secret-reveal"]
    [dir directive=eval         cap=eval]
    [dir directive=reveal       cap=secret-reveal]
    [dir directive=http-client  cap=net]
    [dir directive=http-service cap=net]
    [dir directive=sleep        cap=clock]
    [arm carrier=then         under=if]
    [arm carrier=else         under=if]
    [arm carrier=case         under=match]
    [arm carrier=else         under=match]
    [arm carrier=yield        under=match]
    [arm carrier=case         under=select]
    [arm carrier=default      under=select]
    [arm carrier=recover-with under=fallback]
    [opaque kind=eval    label="[?eval] — executes a tree the image does not hold"]
    [opaque kind=call    label="unresolved callee"]
    [opaque kind=dynamic label="source-text hatch — its inner calls are not in the image"]
    [opaque kind=lib     label="[?lib] — module body not in the image"]
    [opaque kind=ring2   label="Ring-2 pack verb — charge registered at runtime"]]]

[; ef-caps — the roster, in order. ]
[?def ef-caps pure [returns any] ()
  [?for [in $r [$effect-rules]/*] [where [= [$name $r] "cap"]]
    [yield [$string $r@name]]]]

[?def ef-cap-flag pure [returns string] ($c::string)
  [?let [= $xs [?for [in $r [$effect-rules]/*]
      [where [?if [= [$name $r] "cap"] [then [= [$string $r@name] $c]] [else false]]]
      [yield [$string $r@flag]]]]
    [?if [> [$count $xs] 0] [then [$first $xs]] [else ""]]]]

[; ef-dir-cap — the capability a DIRECTIVE HEAD charges ("" for none). ]
[?def ef-dir-cap pure [returns string] ($loc::string)
  [?let [= $xs [?for [in $r [$effect-rules]/*]
      [where [?if [= [$name $r] "dir"] [then [= [$string $r@directive] $loc]] [else false]]]
      [yield [$string $r@cap]]]]
    [?if [> [$count $xs] 0] [then [$first $xs]] [else ""]]]]

[; ef-is-arm — is $carrier an arm of a branch directive $under? The
   `under` column is load-bearing: `yield` is a match ARM under
   [?match] and an iteration BODY under a for-comprehension, and only
   the first makes what it holds conditional. ]
[?def ef-is-arm pure [returns bool] ($carrier::string $under::string)
  [$exists [$first [?for [in $r [$effect-rules]/*]
    [where [?if [= [$name $r] "arm"]
      [then [?if [= [$string $r@carrier] $carrier]
        [then [= [$string $r@under] $under]]
        [else false]]]
      [else false]]]
    [yield 1]]]]]

[; ── §11.2 the engine tables, read LIVE (DGX-1a) ──────────────────────
   Every lookup takes the table as a parameter: the value is materialized
   ONCE per render and threaded, never re-requested per call site. ]

[?def ef-prim-cap pure [returns string] ($tbl::element $nm::string)
  [?let [= $xs [?for [in $r $tbl/*]
      [where [?if [= [$name $r] "prim"] [then [= [$string $r@name] $nm]] [else false]]]
      [yield [$string $r@cap]]]]
    [?if [> [$count $xs] 0] [then [$first $xs]] [else ""]]]]

[?def ef-has-row pure [returns bool] ($tbl::element $cls::string $nm::string)
  [$exists [$first [?for [in $r $tbl/*]
    [where [?if [= [$name $r] $cls] [then [= [$string $r@name] $nm]] [else false]]]
    [yield 1]]]]]

[; effect-cap — the capability a PRIMITIVE charges, "" for none. The
   module's public probe of the live engine table. ]
[?def effect-cap scope=public pure [returns string] ($prim::string)
  [$ef-prim-cap [$diagram-effect-table] $prim]]

[; ── §11.3 resolution context ─────────────────────────────────────────
   Collected in two pre-passes: the `[?def]` names the image holds, and
   the module aliases `[?lib]` binds (DGX-1e's lib-image). ]

[?def ef-names-add pure [returns element] ($acc::element $nm::string)
  [?if [= $nm ""]
    [then $acc]
    [else [?if [$exists [$first [?for [in $n $acc/*] [where [= [$string $n@v] $nm]] [yield 1]]]]
      [then $acc]
      [else [names [?splice [?for [in $n $acc/*] [yield $n]]] [n v=$nm]]]]]]]

[?def ef-defnames pure [returns element] ($n::any $acc::element)
  [?let [= $a1 [?if [= [$name $n] "cx:def-image"]
                  [then [$ef-names-add $acc [$string $n@name]]]
                  [else $acc]]]
    [$ef-defnames-kids [?for [in $k $n/*] [yield $k]] 1 $a1]]]

[?def ef-defnames-kids pure [returns element] ($ks::any $i::int $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$ef-defnames-kids $ks [+ $i 1] [$ef-defnames [$nth $ks $i] $acc]]]]]

[; ef-aliases — [a p=ALIAS m=RESOLVER] for every [?lib … as=NAME]. ]
[?def ef-aliases pure [returns element] ($n::any $acc::element)
  [?let [= $a1 [?if [= [$name $n] "cx:lib-image"]
                  [then [?if [= [$string $n@alias] ""]
                    [then $acc]
                    [else [aliases [?splice [?for [in $a $acc/*] [yield $a]]]
                            [a p=[$string $n@alias] m=[$string $n@module]]]]]]
                  [else $acc]]]
    [$ef-aliases-kids [?for [in $k $n/*] [yield $k]] 1 $a1]]]

[?def ef-aliases-kids pure [returns element] ($ks::any $i::int $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$ef-aliases-kids $ks [+ $i 1] [$ef-aliases [$nth $ks $i] $acc]]]]]

[; ef-prefix-of — the PRIM PREFIX a call qualifier resolves to, or ""
   when it resolves to nothing the walk can see. An alias expands to its
   resolver; a bundled `cx-stdlib/X` resolver contributes prefix X; an
   unaliased qualifier that IS a bundled module name is itself. ]
[?def ef-prefix-of pure [returns string] ($ctx::element $tbl::element $q::string)
  [?let [= $res [?let [= $xs [?for [in $a $ctx/aliases/*]
                    [where [= [$string $a@p] $q]] [yield [$string $a@m]]]]
                  [?if [> [$count $xs] 0] [then [$first $xs]] [else ""]]]]
    [?if [= $res ""]
      [then [?if [$ef-has-row $tbl "module" $q] [then $q] [else ""]]]
      [else [?if [$str-starts-with $res "cx-stdlib/"]
        [then [?let [= $seg [$str-slice $res 10 [$str-length $res]]]
                [?if [$ef-has-row $tbl "module" $seg] [then $seg] [else ""]]]]
        [else ""]]]]]]

[; ── §11.4 callee resolution ──────────────────────────────────────────
   MIRRORS THE ENGINE's own classifier (purity_checker.v classify_callee):
   a name in the capability-gated map CHARGES; a name in the §6.5.1
   impure-without-capability set is an UNCHARGED effect; a Ring-2 pack
   verb's charge is registered at runtime and is therefore OPAQUE to any
   static table, this one included; a `[?def]` in the image is a call
   edge; anything else the engine itself classifies pure.

   Returns [res kind=… name=… cap=…] with kind in
   prim | uncharged | ring2 | def | pure | unknown. ]
[?def ef-resolve pure [returns element] ($fn::string $ctx::element $tbl::element)
  [?if [$str-contains $fn ":"]
    [then [$ef-resolve-q $fn $ctx $tbl]]
    [else [?if [$exists [$first [?for [in $d $ctx/defs/*]
             [where [= [$string $d@v] $fn]] [yield 1]]]]
      [then [res kind=def name=$fn]]
      [else [$ef-classify $fn $fn $tbl]]]]]]

[?def ef-resolve-q pure [returns element] ($fn::string $ctx::element $tbl::element)
  [?let
    [= $i [$str-find $fn ":"]]
    [= $q [$str-slice $fn 0 $i]]
    [= $l [$str-slice $fn [+ $i 1] [$str-length $fn]]]
    [= $p [$ef-prefix-of $ctx $tbl $q]]
    [?if [= $p ""]
      [then [res kind=unknown name=$fn]]
      [else [$ef-classify [$concat $p "-" $l] $fn $tbl]]]]]

[?def ef-classify pure [returns element] ($cand::string $shown::string $tbl::element)
  [?let [= $cap [$ef-prim-cap $tbl $cand]]
    [?if [not [= $cap ""]]
      [then [res kind=prim name=$cand cap=$cap]]
      [else [?if [$ef-has-row $tbl "impure" $cand]
        [then [res kind=uncharged name=$cand]]
        [else [?if [$ef-has-row $tbl "ring2" $cand]
          [then [res kind=ring2 name=$cand]]
          [else [res kind=pure name=$shown]]]]]]]]]

[; ── §11.5 the walk ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
   One pass over the "effects" image. Sites accumulate flat; every
   record carries the def it sits in (`via`, `main` for top level) and
   whether its position is under a branch arm (`cond`). ]

[?def ef-site pure [returns element] ($acc::element $s::element)
  [sites [?splice [?for [in $x $acc/*] [yield $x]]] $s]]

[; ef-yn — flags ride as "y"/"n" STRINGS, not booleans: every consumer
   below compares them as attribute text and a bool attribute's text
   projection is not the renderer's business to depend on. ]
[?def ef-yn pure [returns string] ($b::bool) [?if $b [then "y"] [else "n"]]]

[?def ef-walk pure [returns element] ($n::any $via::string $cond::bool
                                      $den::string $ctx::element $tbl::element $acc::element)
  [?if [= [$name $n] ""]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $loc [$local-of $n]]
        [?if [= [$name $n] "cx:call"]
          [then [$ef-walk-kids $n $loc $via $cond $den $ctx $tbl
                  [$ef-call-site $n $via $cond $den $ctx $tbl $acc]]]
          [else [?if [= [$name $n] "cx:def-image"]
            [then [$ef-walk-kids $n $loc
                    [?if [= [$string $n@name] ""] [then $via] [else [$string $n@name]]]
                    false $den $ctx $tbl $acc]]
            [else [?if [= [$name $n] "cx:with-caps"]
              [then [$ef-walk-kids $n $loc $via $cond [$ef-denies $n $den] $ctx $tbl $acc]]
              [else [?if [= [$name $n] "cx:lib-image"]
                [then [$ef-lib-site $n $via $cond $tbl $acc]]
                [else [?if [= [$name $n] "cx:expr"]
                  [then [$ef-walk-kids $n $loc $via $cond $den $ctx $tbl
                          [$ef-site $acc [site kind=unknown ukind=dynamic
                                               what=[$ef-opaque-label "dynamic"]
                                               via=$via cond=[$ef-yn $cond]]]]]
                  [else [$ef-walk-kids $n $loc $via $cond $den $ctx $tbl
                          [$ef-dir-site $n $loc $via $cond $den $acc]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[; ef-dir-site — a directive head that charges a capability (the `dir`
   rows). [?eval] charges `eval` AND is the archetypal opacity source:
   the tree it executes is not in the image, so it also fans to `any`. ]
[?def ef-dir-site pure [returns element] ($n::any $loc::string $via::string
                                          $cond::bool $den::string $acc::element)
  [?if [not [= [$cd-node-kind $n] "directive"]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $cap [$ef-dir-cap $loc]]
        [?if [= $cap ""]
          [then $acc]
          [else
            [?let [= $a1 [$ef-site $acc
                  [site kind=dir name=$loc show=[$concat "[?" $loc "]"] cap=$cap via=$via
                        cond=[$ef-yn $cond] denied=[$ef-denied $den $cap]]]]
              [?if [= $loc "eval"]
                [then [$ef-site $a1 [site kind=unknown ukind=eval
                                          what=[$ef-opaque-label "eval"]
                                          via=$via cond=[$ef-yn $cond]]]]
                [else $a1]]]]]]]]]

[; ef-call-site — resolve one call and record what it reaches. ]
[?def ef-call-site pure [returns element] ($n::any $via::string $cond::bool
                                           $den::string $ctx::element $tbl::element $acc::element)
  [?let
    [= $fn [$string $n@fn]]
    [= $r [$ef-resolve $fn $ctx $tbl]]
    [= $k [$string $r@kind]]
    [?if [= $k "pure"]
      [then $acc]
      [else [?if [= $k "def"]
        [then [$ef-site $acc [site kind=call name=[$string $r@name] show=[$string $r@name]
                                 cap="" via=$via cond=[$ef-yn $cond] denied="n"]]]
        [else [?if [= $k "prim"]
          [then [$ef-site $acc [site kind=prim name=[$string $r@name] show=[$string $r@name]
                                     cap=[$string $r@cap] via=$via cond=[$ef-yn $cond]
                                     denied=[$ef-denied $den [$string $r@cap]]]]]
          [else [?if [= $k "uncharged"]
            [then [$ef-site $acc [site kind=uncharged name=[$string $r@name]
                                       show=[$string $r@name] cap="" via=$via
                                       cond=[$ef-yn $cond] denied="n"]]]
            [else [?if [= $k "ring2"]
              [then [$ef-site $acc [site kind=unknown ukind=ring2
                                         what=[$concat [$ef-opaque-label "ring2"] ": " $fn]
                                         via=$via cond=[$ef-yn $cond]]]]
              [else [$ef-site $acc [site kind=unknown ukind=call
                                         what=[$concat [$ef-opaque-label "call"] ": " $fn]
                                         via=$via cond=[$ef-yn $cond]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[; ef-lib-site — an import whose body the image does not hold. A
   bundled `cx-stdlib` module resolves BY NAME through the engine
   tables, so it is not opaque; anything else is. An https resolver
   also charges `net` (security.md §2, `[?lib]` over https). ]
[?def ef-lib-site pure [returns element] ($n::any $via::string $cond::bool
                                          $tbl::element $acc::element)
  [?let
    [= $m [$string $n@module]]
    [= $kd [$string $n@kind]]
    [= $a1 [?if [= $kd "https"]
      [then [$ef-site $acc [site kind=dir name="lib-https" show="[?lib] over https"
                                 cap="net" via=$via cond=[$ef-yn $cond] denied="n"]]]
      [else $acc]]]
    [?if [$ef-bundled $tbl $m]
      [then $a1]
      [else [$ef-site $a1 [site kind=unknown ukind=lib
                                what=[$concat [$ef-opaque-label "lib"] ": " $m]
                                via=$via cond=[$ef-yn $cond]]]]]]]

[?def ef-bundled pure [returns bool] ($tbl::element $m::string)
  [$exists [$first [?for [in $r $tbl/*]
    [where [?if [= [$name $r] "module"] [then [= [$string $r@resolver] $m]] [else false]]]
    [yield 1]]]]]

[; ef-denies — [?with-caps [deny CAP] … BODY] narrows for the body's
   extent. The deny set rides as a "|"-fenced STRING rather than a
   sequence: it is threaded through every arm of the walk, and a fenced
   string concatenates and tests in one primitive each where a sequence
   would need an accumulator hop per node.

   There is no "unreadable narrowing" case to report: the parser
   REFUSES a non-literal deny operand outright (`[?with-caps] [deny …]
   requires a capability name`), so a with-caps that reaches the image
   at all has a readable deny list. Measured at landing — the DGX-1c
   draft carried a `caps` opacity class for this and it is removed. ]
[?def ef-denies pure [returns string] ($n::any $den::string)
  [$ef-denies-i [?for [in $k $n/*] [where [= [$name $k] "cx:deny"]] [yield $k]] 1 $den]]

[?def ef-denies-i pure [returns string] ($ks::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $c [$ef-deny-lit [$nth $ks $i]]]
        [$ef-denies-i $ks [+ $i 1]
          [?if [= $c ""] [then $acc] [else [$concat $acc $c "|"]]]]]]]]

[?def ef-denied pure [returns string] ($den::string $cap::string)
  [?if [= $cap "" ] [then "n"]
    [else [?if [$str-contains $den [$concat "|" $cap "|"]] [then "y"] [else "n"]]]]]

[?def ef-deny-lit pure [returns string] ($k::any)
  [?let [= $xs [?for [in $v $k/*] [where [= [$name $v] "cx:str"]] [yield [$string $v]]]]
    [?if [> [$count $xs] 0] [then [$first $xs]] [else ""]]]]

[?def ef-walk-kids pure [returns element] ($n::any $ploc::string $via::string $cond::bool
                                           $den::string $ctx::element $tbl::element $acc::element)
  [$ef-walk-kids-i [?for [in $k $n/*] [yield $k]] 1 $ploc $via $cond $den $ctx $tbl $acc]]

[?def ef-walk-kids-i pure [returns element] ($ks::any $i::int $ploc::string $via::string
                                             $cond::bool $den::string $ctx::element
                                             $tbl::element $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $k [$nth $ks $i]]
        [= $c2 [?if $cond [then true] [else [$ef-is-arm [$local-of $k] $ploc]]]]
        [$ef-walk-kids-i $ks [+ $i 1] $ploc $via $cond $den $ctx $tbl
          [$ef-walk $k $via $c2 $den $ctx $tbl $acc]]]]]]

[; ── §11.6 reachability closure ───────────────────────────────────────
   Conditionality is a PATH property, not a position property: an effect
   written outside a branch, in a def that is only ever called from
   inside one, is conditionally reached. The closure computes two sets
   over the call edges — reached-at-all and reached-through-unconditional
   -edges-only — starting from `main`, so the `min` rung's verdict is
   about the whole path and not just the call site. ]

[?def ef-add-uniq pure [returns element] ($acc::element $e::element)
  [?if [$exists [$first [?for [in $x $acc/*] [where [= [$string $x@k] [$string $e@k]]] [yield 1]]]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [lst [?splice [?for [in $x $acc/*] [yield $x]]] $e]]]]

[?def ef-in-set pure [returns bool] ($set::element $nm::string)
  [$exists [$first [?for [in $x $set/*] [where [= [$string $x@k] $nm]] [yield 1]]]]]

[?def ef-closure-step pure [returns element] ($ss::any $i::int $ou::bool $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ss]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $s [$nth $ss $i]]
        [= $skip [?if [not [= [$string $s@kind] "call"]]
          [then true]
          [else [?if [?if $ou [then [= [$string $s@cond] "y"]] [else false]]
            [then true]
            [else [not [$ef-in-set $acc [$string $s@via]]]]]]]]
        [$ef-closure-step $ss [+ $i 1] $ou
          [?if $skip [then $acc] [else [$ef-add-uniq $acc [x k=[$string $s@name]]]]]]]]]]

[?def ef-closure pure [returns element] ($ss::any $ou::bool $acc::element $n::int)
  [?if [<= $n 0]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $a2 [$ef-closure-step $ss 1 $ou $acc]]
        [?if [= [$count $a2/*] [$count $acc/*]]
          [then $acc]
          [else [$ef-closure $ss $ou $a2 [- $n 1]]]]]]]]

[; ── §11.7 per-capability verdict ─────────────────────────────────────
   "" = the source charges it nowhere; "x" = it is charged, but only
   inside a def NOTHING CALLS, so no path from the program's entry
   reaches it; "d" = every reaching site sits inside a [?with-caps]
   narrowing that DENIES it, so the effect refuses rather than performs;
   "u" = reached through unconditional edges only; "c" = reached, but
   every path to it passes a branch arm.

   "x" exists because the alternative is a lie by omission: a program
   whose only [$process:run] sits in an uncalled def would otherwise
   render as "no capability-charging effect reached", which is true of
   the entry and false of the file. ]
[?def ef-cap-status pure [returns string] ($ss::any $cap::string $reach::element $unc::element)
  [?let
    [= $all [?for [in $s $ss] [where [$ef-charges $s $cap]] [yield $s]]]
    [= $hit [?for [in $s $all]
      [where [$ef-in-set $reach [$string $s@via]]] [yield $s]]]
    [?if [= [$count $all] 0]
      [then ""]
      [else [?if [= [$count $hit] 0]
      [then "x"]
      [else
        [?let
          [= $live [?for [in $s $hit] [where [not [= [$string $s@denied] "y"]]] [yield $s]]]
          [?if [= [$count $live] 0]
            [then "d"]
            [else
              [?let [= $u [?for [in $s $live]
                    [where [?if [= [$string $s@cond] "n"] [then [$ef-in-set $unc [$string $s@via]]] [else false]]]
                    [yield 1]]]
                [?if [> [$count $u] 0] [then "u"] [else "c"]]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def ef-charges pure [returns bool] ($s::any $cap::string)
  [?if [$cd-in-list [$string $s@kind] ("prim", "dir")]
    [then [= [$string $s@cap] $cap]]
    [else false]]]

[; ── §11.8 emit ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Node shapes reuse the reference renderer's vocabulary: the program is
   a stadium, a def a rect, an effect site a subroutine capsule, a
   capability a hexagon, an opacity source a lean parallelogram. Edges:
   `-->` reached, `-.->` reached only under a branch, `==>` unknown,
   `--x` denied by a [?with-caps] narrowing. ]

[?def ef-cap-id pure [returns string] ($c::string) [$concat "cap_" [$cd-sanitize-id $c]]]
[?def ef-def-id pure [returns string] ($d::string) [$concat "def_" [$cd-sanitize-id $d]]]
[?def ef-eff-id pure [returns string] ($e::string) [$concat "eff_" [$cd-sanitize-id $e]]]
[?def ef-via-id pure [returns string] ($v::string)
  [?if [= $v "main"] [then "prog"] [else [$ef-def-id $v]]]]

[?def ef-opaque-label pure [returns string] ($k::string)
  [?let [= $xs [?for [in $r [$effect-rules]/*]
      [where [?if [= [$name $r] "opaque"] [then [= [$string $r@kind] $k]] [else false]]]
      [yield [$string $r@label]]]]
    [?if [> [$count $xs] 0] [then [$first $xs]] [else $k]]]]

[?def ef-opaque-kinds pure [returns any] ()
  [?for [in $r [$effect-rules]/*] [where [= [$name $r] "opaque"]] [yield [$string $r@kind]]]]

[; the MIN rung — the auditor's one glance. ]
[?def ef-min pure [returns string] ($ss::any $reach::element $unc::element)
  [?let
    [= $capl [$ef-min-caps [$ef-caps] 1 $ss $reach $unc ""]]
    [= $ks [?for [in $k [$ef-opaque-kinds]]
      [where [> [$count [?for [in $s $ss]
        [where [?if [= [$string $s@kind] "unknown"] [then [= [$string $s@ukind] $k]] [else false]]]
        [yield 1]]] 0]]
      [yield $k]]]
    [= $unkl [$ef-min-unks $ks 1 ""]]
    [= $sink [?if [= [$count $ks] 0]
      [then ""]
      [else [$jn "  any{{\"any granted capability\"}}" [$ef-min-any $ks 1 ""]]]]]
    [?if [?if [= $capl ""] [then [= [$count $ks] 0]] [else false]]
      [then [$ef-nothing]]
      [else [$jn4 "flowchart TD" "  prog([\"program\"])" $capl [$jn $unkl $sink]]]]]]

[?def ef-min-caps pure [returns string] ($cs::any $i::int $ss::any
                                         $reach::element $unc::element $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $cs]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $c [$nth $cs $i]]
        [= $st [$ef-cap-status $ss $c $reach $unc]]
        [$ef-min-caps $cs [+ $i 1] $ss $reach $unc
          [?if [= $st ""]
            [then $acc]
            [else [$jn3 $acc
              [$str-format "  {}{{{{\"{}\"}}}}" ([$ef-cap-id $c], [$esc $c])]
              [?if [= $st "u"]
                [then [$concat "  prog --> " [$ef-cap-id $c]]]
                [else [?if [= $st "d"]
                  [then [$concat "  prog --x|\"denied by [?with-caps]\"| " [$ef-cap-id $c]]]
                  [else [?if [= $st "x"]
                    [then [$concat "  prog -.->|\"charged only in a def nothing calls\"| " [$ef-cap-id $c]]]
                    [else [$concat "  prog -.->|\"conditional\"| " [$ef-cap-id $c]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def ef-min-unks pure [returns string] ($ks::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $k [$nth $ks $i]] [= $id [$concat "unk_" [$cd-sanitize-id $k]]]
        [$ef-min-unks $ks [+ $i 1]
          [$jn3 $acc
            [$str-format "  {}[/\"{}\"/]" ($id, [$esc [$ef-opaque-label $k]])]
            [$concat "  prog ==> " $id]]]]]]]

[?def ef-min-any pure [returns string] ($ks::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ks]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$ef-min-any $ks [+ $i 1]
      [$jn $acc [$concat "  unk_" [$cd-sanitize-id [$nth $ks $i]] " ==> any"]]]]]]

[; ── §11.9 the COMPACT / FULL rungs — the call paths ──────────────────
   min answers "which capabilities"; compact answers "through what".
   Every list below is built in first-appearance order so the render is
   deterministic and diffable across runs — an auditor property. ]

[?def ef-upgrade pure [returns element] ($acc::element $e::element)
  [?if [not [$exists [$first [?for [in $x $acc/*] [where [= [$string $x@k] [$string $e@k]]] [yield 1]]]]]
    [then [lst [?splice [?for [in $x $acc/*] [yield $x]]] $e]]
    [else
      [lst [?splice [?for [in $x $acc/*]
        [yield [?if [not [= [$string $x@k] [$string $e@k]]]
          [then $x]
          [else [?if [= [$string $e@cond] "n"] [then $e] [else $x]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def ef-effs pure [returns element] ($ss::any $i::int $full::bool $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ss]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $s [$nth $ss $i]]
        [= $keep [?if [$cd-in-list [$string $s@kind] ("prim", "dir")]
          [then true]
          [else [?if [= [$string $s@kind] "uncharged"] [then $full] [else false]]]]]
        [$ef-effs $ss [+ $i 1] $full
          [?if [not $keep]
            [then $acc]
            [else [$ef-add-uniq $acc
              [x k=[$string $s@name] show=[$string $s@show]
                 cap=[$string $s@cap] kind=[$string $s@kind]]]]]]]]]]

[?def ef-edges pure [returns element] ($ss::any $i::int $full::bool $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ss]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $s [$nth $ss $i]]
        [= $keep [?if [$cd-in-list [$string $s@kind] ("prim", "dir", "call")]
          [then true]
          [else [?if [= [$string $s@kind] "uncharged"] [then $full] [else false]]]]]
        [$ef-edges $ss [+ $i 1] $full
          [?if [not $keep]
            [then $acc]
            [else [$ef-upgrade $acc
              [x k=[$concat [$string $s@via] "|" [$string $s@kind] "|" [$string $s@name]]
                 via=[$string $s@via] name=[$string $s@name] kind=[$string $s@kind]
                 cond=[$string $s@cond] denied=[$string $s@denied]]]]]]]]]]

[?def ef-capedges pure [returns element] ($es::any $i::int $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $es]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $e [$nth $es $i]]
        [$ef-capedges $es [+ $i 1]
          [?if [= [$string $e@cap] ""]
            [then $acc]
            [else [$ef-add-uniq $acc
              [x k=[$concat [$string $e@k] "|" [$string $e@cap]]
                 name=[$string $e@k] cap=[$string $e@cap]]]]]]]]]]

[?def ef-node-lines pure [returns string] ($es::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $es]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $e [$nth $es $i]]
        [$ef-node-lines $es [+ $i 1]
          [$jn $acc [$str-format "  {}[[\"{}\"]]"
            ([$ef-eff-id [$string $e@k]], [$esc [$string $e@show]])]]]]]]]

[?def ef-def-lines pure [returns string] ($ds::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ds]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$ef-def-lines $ds [+ $i 1]
      [$jn $acc [$str-format "  {}[\"def {}\"]"
        ([$ef-def-id [$nth $ds $i]], [$esc [$nth $ds $i]])]]]]]]

[?def ef-unk-nodes pure [returns string] ($us::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $us]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$ef-unk-nodes $us [+ $i 1]
      [$jn $acc [$str-format "  unk_{}[/\"{}\"/]"
        ($i, [$esc [$string [$nth $us $i]@what]])]]]]]]

[?def ef-unk-edges pure [returns string] ($us::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $us]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $u [$nth $us $i]]
        [$ef-unk-edges $us [+ $i 1]
          [$jn3 $acc
            [$str-format "  {} ==> unk_{}" ([$ef-via-id [$string $u@via]], $i)]
            [$str-format "  unk_{} ==> any" ($i)]]]]]]]

[?def ef-capnode-lines pure [returns string] ($cs::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $cs]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $c [$nth $cs $i]]
        [$ef-capnode-lines $cs [+ $i 1]
          [$jn $acc [$str-format "  {}{{{{\"{} {}\"}}}}"
            ([$ef-cap-id $c], [$esc $c], [$esc [$ef-cap-flag $c]])]]]]]]]

[?def ef-edge-lines pure [returns string] ($es::any $i::int $full::bool $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $es]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $e [$nth $es $i]]
        [= $from [$ef-via-id [$string $e@via]]]
        [= $to [?if [= [$string $e@kind] "call"]
          [then [$ef-def-id [$string $e@name]]]
          [else [$ef-eff-id [$string $e@name]]]]]
        [= $lbl [?if [= [$string $e@kind] "call"] [then "|\"call\"|"] [else ""]]]
        [= $arrow [?if [?if $full [then [= [$string $e@denied] "y"]] [else false]]
          [then "--x"]
          [else [?if [= [$string $e@cond] "y"] [then "-.->"] [else "-->"]]]]]
        [$ef-edge-lines $es [+ $i 1] $full
          [$jn $acc [$concat "  " $from " " $arrow $lbl " " $to]]]]]]]

[?def ef-capedge-lines pure [returns string] ($es::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $es]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $e [$nth $es $i]]
        [$ef-capedge-lines $es [+ $i 1]
          [$jn $acc [$concat "  " [$ef-eff-id [$string $e@name]] " --> "
                              [$ef-cap-id [$string $e@cap]]]]]]]]]

[?def ef-unchg-lines pure [returns string] ($es::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $es]]
    [then $acc]
    [else
      [?let [= $e [$nth $es $i]]
        [$ef-unchg-lines $es [+ $i 1]
          [?if [not [= [$string $e@kind] "uncharged"]]
            [then $acc]
            [else [$jn $acc [$concat "  " [$ef-eff-id [$string $e@k]] " --> nocharge"]]]]]]]]]

[?def ef-unk-class-lines pure [returns string] ($us::any $i::int $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $us]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$ef-unk-class-lines $us [+ $i 1]
      [$jn $acc [$str-format "  class unk_{} unknown;" ($i)]]]]]]

[?def ef-classdefs pure [returns string] ()
  [$concat
    "  classDef entry fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#1b5e20;\n"
    "  classDef effect fill:#e8eaf6,stroke:#1a237e;\n"
    "  classDef cap fill:#ffebee,stroke:#b71c1c;\n"
    "  classDef unknown fill:#fff8e1,stroke:#ff6f00;"]]

[?def ef-class-lines pure [returns string] ($ids::any $i::int $cls::string $acc::string)
  [?if [> $i [$count $ids]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$ef-class-lines $ids [+ $i 1] $cls
      [$jn $acc [$concat "  class " [$nth $ids $i] " " $cls ";"]]]]]]

[?def ef-compact pure [returns string] ($ss::any $ctx::element $full::bool)
  [?let
    [= $ds [?for [in $d $ctx/defs/*] [yield [$string $d@v]]]]
    [= $effs [?for [in $e [$ef-effs $ss 1 $full [lst]]/*] [yield $e]]]
    [= $edges [?for [in $e [$ef-edges $ss 1 $full [lst]]/*] [yield $e]]]
    [= $ces [?for [in $e [$ef-capedges $effs 1 [lst]]/*] [yield $e]]]
    [= $us [?for [in $s $ss] [where [= [$string $s@kind] "unknown"]] [yield $s]]]
    [= $cs [?for [in $c [$ef-caps]]
      [where [> [$count [?for [in $e $ces] [where [= [$string $e@cap] $c]] [yield 1]]] 0]]
      [yield $c]]]
    [= $sink [?if [= [$count $us] 0] [then ""] [else "  any{{\"any granted capability\"}}"]]]
    [= $ncn [?if [?if $full
                   [then [> [$count [?for [in $e $effs]
                     [where [= [$string $e@kind] "uncharged"]] [yield 1]]] 0]]
                   [else false]]
      [then "  nocharge{{\"uncharged effect\"}}"]
      [else ""]]]
    [= $body
      [$jn4
        [$jn4 "  prog([\"program\"])" [$ef-def-lines $ds 1 ""] [$ef-node-lines $effs 1 ""]
              [$ef-unk-nodes $us 1 ""]]
        [$jn3 [$ef-capnode-lines $cs 1 ""] $sink $ncn]
        [$jn [$ef-edge-lines $edges 1 $full ""] [$ef-capedge-lines $ces 1 ""]]
        [$jn [$ef-unk-edges $us 1 ""]
             [?if $full [then [$ef-unchg-lines $effs 1 ""]] [else ""]]]]]
    [?if [not $full]
      [then [$jn "flowchart TD" $body]]
      [else
        [$jn4 "flowchart TD" [$ef-classdefs] $body
          [$jn4
            [$ef-class-lines ("prog") 1 "entry" ""]
            [$ef-class-lines [?for [in $e $effs] [yield [$ef-eff-id [$string $e@k]]]] 1 "effect" ""]
            [$ef-class-lines [?for [in $c $cs] [yield [$ef-cap-id $c]]] 1 "cap" ""]
            [$ef-unk-class-lines $us 1 ""]]]]]]]

[; ── §11.10 the entry point ───────────────────────────────────────────
   Same ingress contract as `code-diagram`: source text in, Mermaid out,
   `[?cx …]` PIs stripped first. A source the parser REFUSES returns the
   ingress primitive's own `[err]` — degrading to a placeholder would be
   a claim about a program nobody has read. ]
[?def effect-graph scope=public pure [returns any] ($src::string $level::string)
  [?let [= $stripped [$str-trim [$cd-strip-pis $src]]]
    [?if [= [$str-length $stripped] 0]
      [then [$ef-nothing]]
      [else
        [?let [= $img [?else [$diagram-program-image $stripped "effects"] [ef-unparsed]]]
          [?if [= [$name $img] "ef-unparsed"]
            [then [$diagram-program-image $stripped "effects"]]
            [else [$ef-render $img $level]]]]]]]]

[; ef-nothing — the empty-program answer, and the answer for a program
   the walk finds no effect in. It is the load-bearing case: "this
   source is statically capability-free" is the claim the diagram
   exists to be able to make, and it has to be sayable in one node. ]
[?def ef-nothing pure [returns string] ()
  [$jn3 "flowchart TD" "  prog([\"program\"])"
    [$jn "  nocap[\"no capability-charging effect reached\"]" "  prog --> nocap"]]]

[?def ef-render pure [returns string] ($img::any $level::string)
  [?let
    [= $tbl [$diagram-effect-table]]
    [= $ctx [ctx
      [defs [?splice [?for [in $d [$ef-defnames $img [names]]/*] [yield $d]]]]
      [aliases [?splice [?for [in $a [$ef-aliases $img [aliases]]/*] [yield $a]]]]]]
    [= $stmts [$cd-stmts $img]]
    [= $ss [?for [in $s [$ef-walk-top $stmts 1 $ctx $tbl [sites]]/*] [yield $s]]]
    [= $nd [+ [$count $ctx/defs/*] 1]]
    [= $reach [$ef-closure $ss false [lst [x k="main"]] $nd]]
    [= $unc [$ef-closure $ss true [lst [x k="main"]] $nd]]
    [?if [= $level "min"]
      [then [$ef-min $ss $reach $unc]]
      [else [$ef-compact $ss $ctx [= $level "full"]]]]]]

[?def ef-walk-top pure [returns element] ($stmts::any $i::int $ctx::element
                                          $tbl::element $acc::element)
  [?if [> $i [$count $stmts]]
    [then $acc]
    [else [$ef-walk-top $stmts [+ $i 1] $ctx $tbl
      [$ef-walk [$nth $stmts $i] "main" false "|" $ctx $tbl $acc]]]]]

[; co-located docs (std-lib colocated-docs contract). ]
[module-doc name=diagram]
  [scope """The §10.1.2 reference diagram renderer as a pure CX program (RULED #758, DR-1…DR-11). Renders a CX program's engine-injected program-as-data image to Mermaid text carrying the verbatim source as round-trip metadata, and recovers that source from Mermaid, SVG, and PNG renderings. The render-rules table is a sealed data value: the completeness gate diffs it against the spec table, the golden corpus, and the grammar registry. Engine-invoked via `cx diagram` / `cx eval --target=mermaid`; the injected tree means user programs normally reach it through those surfaces rather than [?lib]."""]
[fn-doc name=render-mermaid scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> string | err"""]
  [summary """Render the engine-injected program image to Mermaid text (detail rung min|compact|full), refusing non-table top-level directives with CXER0281."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/diagram' as=diagram]
[$diagram:extract-mermaid [$diagram:render-mermaid [greet] "[greet]" "min"]]"""] [expect """'[greet]'"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=rules scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """The sealed §10.1.2 render-rules table as data: rows, registry aliases, scaffolding, and nested-only emitters."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/diagram' as=diagram]
[$count [?for [in $r [$diagram:rules]/*] [where [= [$name $r] "row"]] [yield $r]]]"""] [expect """26"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=admitted scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> bool"""]
  [summary """Whether a directive local name is admitted at top level (table rows, aliases, and scaffolding; nested-only emitters are not)."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/diagram' as=diagram]
[$diagram:admitted "secret"]"""] [expect """false"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=extract-mermaid scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> string | err"""]
  [summary """Recover the verbatim embedded CX source from a rendered Mermaid diagram."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/diagram' as=diagram]
[$diagram:extract-mermaid "%%cx:W3hd%%"]"""] [expect """'[x]'"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=extract-svg scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> string | err"""]
  [summary """Recover the verbatim embedded CX source from an SVG rendering's <cx:source> metadata block."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/diagram' as=diagram]
[$diagram:extract-svg "<svg><metadata><cx:source>W3hd</cx:source></metadata></svg>"]"""] [expect """'[x]'"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=extract-png scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> string | err"""]
  [summary """Recover the verbatim embedded CX source from a PNG rendering's cx-source tEXt chunk."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/diagram' as=diagram]
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/bytes' as=bytes]
[?else [$diagram:extract-png [$bytes:from-base64 "iVBORw0KGgo="]] "no cx-source chunk"]"""] [expect """'no cx-source chunk'"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=render-dot scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> string"""]
  [summary """Emit the DOT (graphviz) text for the engine-injected program image — the pure half of the SVG/PNG path."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/diagram' as=diagram]
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/strings' as=strings]
[$strings:contains [$diagram:render-dot [greet]] "digraph CX {"]"""] [expect """true"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=render-svg scope=public purity=impure
  [sig """-> string | err"""]
  [summary """Render the program image to SVG through graphviz (subprocess capability, allowlist `dot`); without the capability or without `dot` on PATH the round-trip-preserving 1x1 envelope is returned instead."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/diagram' as=diagram]
[$diagram:extract-svg [$diagram:render-svg [greet] "[greet]"]]"""] [expect """'[greet]'"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=render-png scope=public purity=impure
  [sig """-> bytes | err"""]
  [summary """Render the program image to PNG through graphviz, splicing the source into a `cx-source` tEXt chunk; degrades to the 1x1 envelope when `dot` is unavailable."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/diagram' as=diagram]
[$diagram:extract-png [$diagram:render-png [greet] "[greet]"]]"""] [expect """'[greet]'"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=of-source scope=public purity=impure
  [sig """-> string | bytes | err"""]
  [summary """Render CX SOURCE TEXT to a diagram in one call (format mermaid|dot|svg|png, detail rung defaulting to min): the program lift happens inside the module, and `cx diagram` renders through this same entry, so a CX caller and the CLI produce identical bytes."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/diagram' as=diagram]
[$diagram:extract-mermaid [$diagram:of-source "[greet]" "mermaid"]]"""] [expect """'[greet]'"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=code-diagram scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> string | err"""]
  [summary """The playground renderer: classify CX source text (data → ERD, sequence-shape code → SEQ, other code → CFG) and emit Mermaid at the requested level (min|compact|full)."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/diagram' as=diagram]
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/strings' as=strings]
[$strings:contains [$diagram:code-diagram "[user id=1]" "min"] "erDiagram"]"""] [expect """true"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=svg-envelope scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> string"""]
  [summary """The dot-less SVG contract: a valid 1x1 SVG carrying only the embedded source, so the round trip holds on profiles without graphviz."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/diagram' as=diagram]
[$diagram:extract-svg [$diagram:svg-envelope "[x]"]]"""] [expect """'[x]'"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=png-envelope scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> bytes"""]
  [summary """The dot-less PNG contract: a valid 1x1 PNG whose `cx-source` tEXt chunk carries the embedded source."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/diagram' as=diagram]
[$diagram:extract-png [$diagram:png-envelope "[x]"]]"""] [expect """'[x]'"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=inject-svg-metadata scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> string"""]
  [summary """Splice a `<metadata><cx:source>` block carrying the base64 source into an SVG document (after its first `>`, reproducing the shipped placement — DRW2-2)."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/diagram' as=diagram]
[$diagram:extract-svg [$diagram:inject-svg-metadata "<svg></svg>" "[x]"]]"""] [expect """'[x]'"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=inject-png-chunk scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> bytes"""]
  [summary """Splice a `cx-source` tEXt chunk (with its CRC-32) into a PNG immediately after IHDR."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/diagram' as=diagram]
[$diagram:extract-png [$diagram:inject-png-chunk [$diagram:png-envelope "[y]"] "[x]"]]"""] [expect """'[x]'"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=crc32 scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> int"""]
  [summary """The PNG chunk CRC-32 (IEEE 802.3 polynomial) over a byte buffer — the checksum the tEXt splice writes."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/diagram' as=diagram]
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/bytes' as=bytes]
[$diagram:crc32 [$bytes:from-string-utf8 "IEND"]]"""] [expect """2923585666"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=code-rules scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """The sealed wave-3 rule table as data: the sequence triggers, the directives that break a CFG basic block, the SEQ inner-dispatch classes, and the ERD scalar-type map. The emitters read it, so the table IS the set."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/diagram' as=diagram]
[$count [?for [in $r [$diagram:code-rules]/*] [where [= [$name $r] "trigger"]] [yield $r]]]"""] [expect """5"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=code-class scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> string"""]
  [summary """The SEQ inner-dispatch class the playground renderer takes for a directive local name; `generic` (a `Note over WORKER` line) for a directive the table does not name."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/diagram' as=diagram]
[$diagram:code-class "const"]"""] [expect """'generic'"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=effect-graph scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> string | err"""]
  [summary """The EFFECT/CAPABILITY graph of a CX source (RULED: DGX-1): which of security.md §2's nine capabilities the program reaches, through which call path, and which only under a branch — at `min` (the verdict), `compact` (the paths) or `full` (uncharged effects, [?with-caps] denials, colour classes). What it cannot resolve statically — a dynamic [?eval], an unresolvable callee, a source-text hatch, an unreadable [?lib], a Ring-2 pack verb — renders as an explicit UNKNOWN edge, never omitted. Reachability is syntactic and the resource scope is never shown: it answers "it can read", not "it reads /etc/passwd"."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/diagram' as=diagram]
[$diagram:effect-graph "[?def double ($x) [* $x 2]]" "min"]"""] [expect """'flowchart TD\n  prog(["program"])\n  nocap["no capability-charging effect reached"]\n  prog --> nocap'"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=effect-rules scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """The sealed effect-graph rule table as data: the nine-capability roster with its grant flags, the directive heads that charge a capability, the branch-arm carriers that make a reached effect conditional, and the opacity classes that must render as an unknown edge. The primitive→capability map is deliberately NOT here — it is read live from the engine, so this diagram cannot under-report a newly-gated effect point."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/diagram' as=diagram]
[$count [?for [in $r [$diagram:effect-rules]/*] [where [= [$name $r] "cap"]] [yield $r]]]"""] [expect """9"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=effect-cap scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> string"""]
  [summary """The capability a PRIMITIVE charges, read live from the engine's own closed effect-point table (security.md §2.1); the empty string for a primitive that charges nothing."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/diagram' as=diagram]
[$diagram:effect-cap "io-read-file"]"""] [expect """'read'"""]]
]
